"id","quiz_title","subject","grade","description","is_published","due_date","outcome_text","indicator_text","question","option_1","option_2","option_3","option_4","answer","explanation","image_url","bloom_level","difficulty"
"eng-g3-3-2-sentence-expresses-a-580a1927","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","Which sentence expresses a more neutral opinion?","I love the movie.","The movie is okay.","I hate the movie.","The movie is not very good.","The movie is okay.","The sentence 'The movie is okay.' expresses a more neutral opinion because it uses the word 'okay'.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-phrase-sounds-more-474c16a5","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","Which phrase sounds more exciting?","We are going to the park.","We are going to the park for a picnic.","We are going to the park for a walk.","We are staying home today.","We are going to the park for a picnic.","The phrase 'We are going to the park for a picnic.' sounds more exciting because it includes a fun activity.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-sentence-expresses-a-8f33767f","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","Which sentence expresses a stronger opinion?","I like the color blue.","The color blue is my favorite.","I think the color blue is nice.","The color blue is okay.","The color blue is my favorite.","The sentence 'The color blue is my favorite.' expresses a stronger opinion because it uses the word 'favorite'.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-phrase-sounds-more-c9d4756e","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","Which phrase sounds more beautiful to you?","The sun shining brightly in the sky","The sun is shining in the sky","The sun is hiding behind the clouds","The sun is not shining at all","The sun shining brightly in the sky","The phrase 'The sun shining brightly in the sky' uses more descriptive words, making it sound more beautiful.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-sentence-is-more-1467f518","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","Which sentence is more formal?","I'm going to the store.","I'm going to the store to buy some milk.","I'm going to the store, it's really close.","I'm going to the store, I need some milk.","I'm going to the store to buy some milk.","The sentence 'I'm going to the store to buy some milk.' is more formal because it includes a specific reason.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-phrase-sounds-more-85d9c07e","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","Which phrase sounds more descriptive?","The sky is blue.","The sky is a beautiful blue.","The sky is a light blue.","The sky is not blue.","The sky is a beautiful blue.","The phrase 'The sky is a beautiful blue.' sounds more descriptive because it uses the word 'beautiful'.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-sentence-expresses-a-4edb4708","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","Which sentence expresses a more positive opinion?","I like the book.","The book is okay.","I don't like the book.","The book is boring.","I like the book.","The sentence 'I like the book.' expresses a more positive opinion because it uses the word 'like'.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-phrase-sounds-more-110eabbf","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","Which phrase sounds more interesting?","The cat is sleeping.","The cat is sleeping on the couch.","The cat is sleeping on the windowsill.","The cat is not sleeping.","The cat is sleeping on the couch.","The phrase 'The cat is sleeping on the couch.' sounds more interesting because it includes a specific location.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-sentence-is-more-278272d4","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","Which sentence is more polite?","Please give me a cookie.","I want a cookie.","Give me a cookie.","You have to give me a cookie.","Please give me a cookie.","The sentence 'Please give me a cookie.' is more polite because it uses the word 'please'.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-phrase-sounds-more-79b359f6","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","Which phrase sounds more exciting?","We are going to the beach.","We are going to the beach for a day.","We are going to the beach for a week.","We are staying home today.","We are going to the beach for a week.","The phrase 'We are going to the beach for a week.' sounds more exciting because it includes a longer period of time.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-would-you-do-1a7618b3","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What would you do if you were the main character?","I would do the same thing","I would do something different","I would try harder","I would give up","I would do something different","You would do something different if you were the main character.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-do-you-agree-3925abe8","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","Do you agree with the author?","Yes, I agree","No, I don't agree","Maybe, I'm not sure","I don't know","Yes, I agree","You agree with the author's opinion.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-do-you-think-4a946c2a","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What do you think the author meant by this sentence?","The author meant that the main character was happy","The author meant that the main character was sad","The author meant that the main character was excited","The author meant that the main character was surprised","The author meant that the main character was surprised","The author meant that the main character was surprised.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-would-you-change-a8be3651","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","5. Suggesting a title, an ending different from the end of the read text, and solutions to problems or issues appeared within.","What would you change about the story?","I would change the characters","I would change the setting","I would change the plot","I would change the ending","I would change the plot","You would change the plot of the story.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-do-you-think-b0fab513","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","Do you think the story is believable?","Yes, I think it's believable","No, I don't think it's believable","Maybe, I'm not sure","I don't know","Yes, I think it's believable","You think the story is believable.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-do-you-think-5b557fb1","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What do you think the author's purpose was?","The author's purpose was to entertain","The author's purpose was to educate","The author's purpose was to persuade","The author's purpose was to inform","The author's purpose was to educate","The author's purpose was to educate.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-author-trying-e6342783","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What is the author trying to say?","The author is happy","The author is sad","The author is excited","The author is surprised","The author is surprised","The author is trying to say that they are surprised by the main character's new skill.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-main-idea-089fcfbf","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What is the main idea of the story?","The main character went to the park","The main character made new friends","The main character learned a new skill","The main character went on a trip","The main character learned a new skill","The main idea of the story is that the main character learned a new skill.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-do-you-think-55442cb6","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What do you think about the story?","I like the story","I don't like the story","I love the story","I hate the story","I like the story","You think the story is good and you like it.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-do-you-think-2f617e72","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What do you think is the most important part of the story?","The beginning","The middle","The end","The characters","The end","You think the most important part of the story is the end.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-if-you-leave-09bdafd9","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","If you leave a toy outside in the rain, what might happen to it?","It will get cleaner.","It will get dirtier.","It will stay the same.","It will turn into a different toy.","It will get dirtier.","When a toy gets wet, it can get dirty.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-might-happen-to-bf7a3af6","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What will eventually happen to an ice cube left in a warm room?","It will grow larger.","It will freeze immediately.","It will turn into metal.","It will melt and eventually disappear as liquid water evaporates.","It will melt and eventually disappear as liquid water evaporates.","The ice first melts into liquid water; over time, the water may evaporate into the air.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-might-happen-to-652c1cb8","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What might happen to the water in a cup if you leave it outside in the cold?","It will get warmer.","It will get colder.","It will stay the same.","It will turn into ice.","It will get colder.","Water gets colder when it's left outside in the cold.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-if-it-rains-84698a62","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","If it rains tomorrow, what might happen to the park?","The park will be very dry.","The park will be very muddy.","The park will be very sunny.","The park will be very cold.","The park will be very muddy.","If it rains, the ground in the park will get wet and muddy.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-might-happen-to-7d117573","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What might happen to the sandcastle if you leave it outside in the water?","It will stay the same.","It will get bigger.","It will get smaller.","It will disappear.","It will disappear.","When a sandcastle gets wet, it can fall apart and disappear.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-if-you-plant-070bbd12","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","If you plant a seed in the ground, what might happen to it?","It will disappear.","It will stay the same.","It will grow into a flower.","It will turn into a rock.","It will grow into a flower.","Seeds have the potential to grow into plants when given the right conditions.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-might-happen-to-02488cbd","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What might happen to the ice cream if it's left outside in the hot sun?","It will get colder.","It will get warmer.","It will melt.","It will get bigger.","It will melt.","Ice cream is made of water, which turns into liquid when it gets too hot.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-if-you-mix-b2279a04","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","If you mix two different colors of paint, what might happen?","They will stay the same color.","They will turn into a new color.","They will disappear.","They will turn into a different shape.","They will turn into a new color.","When you mix two different colors of paint, you get a new color.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-if-you-plant-ca4918a5","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","If you plant a tree in the ground, what might happen to it?","It will stay the same size.","It will get smaller.","It will grow bigger.","It will turn into a rock.","It will grow bigger.","Trees have the potential to grow bigger when given the right conditions.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-might-happen-to-8b7f13bd","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What might happen to the balloon if you let it go outside in the wind?","It will stay in one place.","It will go up high.","It will go down low.","It will fly away.","It will fly away.","When a balloon is let go outside in the wind, it can fly away.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-story-suggest-value-cf03c556","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What does the story suggest about the value of being honest?","Being honest is not important because it's easier to lie.","Being honest is only important when we're in trouble.","Being honest is very important because it builds trust with others.","Being honest is not necessary when we're with our friends.","Being honest is very important because it builds trust with others.","The story shows how the main character tells the truth and is rewarded for it, which means being honest is important.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-author-imply-main-7c0d1edc","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What does the author imply about the main character's attitude towards learning?","The main character loves to learn and is always eager to learn more.","The main character doesn't like to learn and would rather play games.","The main character is neutral towards learning and doesn't feel strongly about it.","The main character is scared of learning and doesn't want to try new things.","The main character loves to learn and is always eager to learn more.","The story shows the main character being excited and interested in learning, which means they have a positive attitude towards learning.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-story-suggest-value-098b36a7","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What does the story suggest about the value of kindness?","Kindness is not important because we can be mean and still be friends.","Kindness is only important when we're in a good mood.","Kindness is very important because it makes others feel happy and valued.","Kindness is not necessary when we're in a hurry.","Kindness is very important because it makes others feel happy and valued.","The story shows how the main character is kind to others and makes them feel happy, which means kindness is important.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-author-imply-main-05524729","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What does the author imply about the main character's feelings towards their friends?","The main character loves their friends and values their relationships.","The main character doesn't like their friends and wishes they had different ones.","The main character is neutral towards their friends and doesn't feel strongly about them.","The main character is scared of their friends and doesn't want to be around them.","The main character loves their friends and values their relationships.","The story shows the main character being happy and loving towards their friends, which means they have positive feelings towards them.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-author-imply-main-a1f819b4","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What does the author imply about the main character's attitude towards trying new things?","The main character is scared to try new things because they might fail.","The main character loves to try new things because they're always fun.","The main character is not interested in trying new things because they're too hard.","The main character is brave and willing to try new things because they might learn something new.","The main character is brave and willing to try new things because they might learn something new.","The story shows the main character being brave and trying new things, which means they have a positive attitude towards trying new things.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-story-suggest-importance-96bd7c72","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What does the story suggest about the importance of perseverance?","Perseverance is not important because we can give up easily.","Perseverance is only important when we're playing sports.","Perseverance is very important because we can achieve our goals if we keep trying.","Perseverance is not necessary when we have a lot of talent.","Perseverance is very important because we can achieve our goals if we keep trying.","The story shows the main character working hard and not giving up, which means perseverance is important.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-author-imply-main-bc619d19","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What does the author imply about the main character's feelings towards their family?","The main character loves their family and is grateful for them.","The main character doesn't like their family and wishes they had a different one.","The main character is neutral towards their family and doesn't feel strongly about them.","The main character is scared of their family and doesn't want to be around them.","The main character loves their family and is grateful for them.","The story shows the main character being happy and loving towards their family, which means they have positive feelings towards them.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-story-suggest-importance-baa481a9","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What does the story suggest about the importance of teamwork?","Teamwork is not important because we can do things alone.","Teamwork is only important when we're playing games.","Teamwork is very important because we can accomplish more together.","Teamwork is not necessary when we have a lot of money.","Teamwork is very important because we can accomplish more together.","The story shows how the main character and their friends work together to achieve their goal, which means teamwork is important.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-why-do-you-94849f28","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","Why do you think the author wrote this story?","The author wrote this story to teach us a lesson about sharing.","The author wrote this story to make us laugh.","The author wrote this story to show us how to be kind to others.","The author wrote this story to tell us a funny joke.","The author wrote this story to show us how to be kind to others.","The story teaches us about the importance of being kind to others, which is why the author wrote it.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-story-tell-us-7e4dec14","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What does the story tell us about the main character's feelings towards helping others?","The main character likes to help others because it makes them happy.","The main character doesn't like to help others because it's too much work.","The main character helps others because they have to, not because they want to.","The main character loves to help others and thinks it's the best thing to do.","The main character loves to help others and thinks it's the best thing to do.","The story shows the main character smiling and feeling happy when they help others, which means they like to help.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-how-do-you-148551a2","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","How do you think the boy and the puppy can solve the problem of the puppy getting hungry?","Give the puppy a bowl of food","Take the puppy to the park","Ask a neighbor for food","Make the puppy a sandwich","Give the puppy a bowl of food","This is a good solution because giving the puppy a bowl of food can help it feel full and happy.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-do-you-think-7707566f","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What do you think the boy should do to help the puppy get home safely?","Walk the puppy home","Call a friend to help","Ask a neighbor for help","Give the puppy a map","Walk the puppy home","This is a good choice because walking the puppy home can help it get home safely.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-how-do-you-4da0dafc","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","How do you think the boy felt when he found the lost puppy?","Happy and sad","Angry and scared","Excited and happy","Sad and lonely","Excited and happy","This is a good choice because finding a lost puppy can make someone feel happy and excited.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-would-be-a-1715fa9c","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What would be a good solution to the problem of the puppy getting lost again?","Make sure the puppy always wears a collar","Keep the puppy on a leash","Check the neighborhood for the puppy","Ask a neighbor to watch the puppy","Make sure the puppy always wears a collar","This is a good solution because it helps keep the puppy safe.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-do-you-think-adf59689","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What do you think the boy should do to help the puppy feel better when it's scared?","Give the puppy a treat","Play with the puppy","Talk to the puppy softly","Give the puppy a big hug","Give the puppy a big hug","This is a good choice because giving the puppy a big hug can make it feel safe and loved.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-how-do-you-54707d89","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","How do you think the boy and the puppy can solve the problem of the puppy being scared at night?","Give the puppy a nightlight","Leave the puppy alone","Talk to the puppy softly","Give the puppy a big hug","Give the puppy a big hug","This is a good solution because giving the puppy a big hug can make it feel safe and loved.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-would-be-a-e7e4e8ac","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What would be a good title for a story about a boy who finds a lost puppy?","The Boy and the Puppy","The Puppy's Big Adventure","The Boy Who Found a Friend","The Puppy's New Home","The Boy and the Puppy","A good title should tell us what the story is about.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-would-be-a-50fb0bb6","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What would be a good title for a story about a boy who helps a lost puppy find its way home?","The Boy Who Helped the Puppy","The Puppy's Big Journey","The Boy and the Lost Puppy","The Puppy's New Home","The Boy Who Helped the Puppy","A good title should tell us what the story is about.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-how-do-you-48d199b6","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","How do you think the story would end if the boy and the puppy became best friends?","The boy and the puppy got lost again","The boy and the puppy went to the park","The boy and the puppy had a big party","The boy and the puppy went on a long walk","The boy and the puppy had a big party","This ending is a good choice because it shows the boy and the puppy having fun together.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-would-be-a-b175e7de","English G3: Distinguishing between multiple expressions - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What would be a good ending to the story if the boy and the puppy went on a big adventure?","The boy and the puppy got lost in the woods","The boy and the puppy found a treasure","The boy and the puppy met a new friend","The boy and the puppy went back home","The boy and the puppy found a treasure","This is a good ending because finding a treasure can be a fun and exciting adventure.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-purpose-of-8bad4488","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the purpose of the text about a new park?","To tell a story about a park.","To inform readers about a new park.","To persuade readers to visit a park.","To describe a park's features.","To inform readers about a new park.","The text aims to inform readers about the new park, which is its purpose.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-main-idea-870ff4ea","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the main idea of the text about a birthday party?","The birthday party is very big.","The birthday party is very small.","The birthday party is very fun.","The birthday party is very sad.","The birthday party is very fun.","The text states that the birthday party is very fun, which is the main idea.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-purpose-of-a3784eef","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","2. Expressing his/her opinion and points of view on the subject of the read text with appropriate justifications.","What is the purpose of the text about a new book?","To tell a story about a book.","To inform readers about a new book.","To persuade readers to read a book.","To describe a book's features.","To inform readers about a new book.","The text aims to inform readers about the new book, which is its purpose.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-main-idea-a41844ee","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the main idea of the text about a cat?","The cat is very big.","The cat likes to play outside.","The cat is very lazy.","The cat has many toys.","The cat likes to play outside.","The text states that the cat likes to play outside, which is the main idea.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-main-idea-851154af","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the main idea of the text about a school day?","The students go to school to learn.","The students go to school to play.","The students go to school to eat.","The students go to school to sleep.","The students go to school to learn.","The text states that the students go to school to learn, which is the main idea.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-purpose-of-cfcc2b74","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the purpose of the text about a new law?","To tell a story about a law.","To inform readers about a new law.","To persuade readers to follow a law.","To describe a law's features.","To inform readers about a new law.","The text aims to inform readers about the new law, which is its purpose.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-main-idea-9e131970","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the main idea of the text about a family trip?","The family goes on a trip to relax.","The family goes on a trip to play.","The family goes on a trip to learn.","The family goes on a trip to work.","The family goes on a trip to relax.","The text states that the family goes on a trip to relax, which is the main idea.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-main-idea-961c8094","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the main idea of the text about a school event?","The school event is very big.","The school event is very small.","The school event is very fun.","The school event is very sad.","The school event is very fun.","The text states that the school event is very fun, which is the main idea.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-purpose-of-7351778f","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the purpose of the text about a new rule?","To tell a story about a rule.","To inform readers about a new rule.","To persuade readers to follow a rule.","To describe a rule's features.","To inform readers about a new rule.","The text aims to inform readers about the new rule, which is its purpose.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-purpose-of-238eaadd","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 1","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the purpose of the text about a new policy?","To tell a story about a policy.","To inform readers about a new policy.","To persuade readers to follow a policy.","To describe a policy's features.","To inform readers about a new policy.","The text aims to inform readers about the new policy, which is its purpose.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-purpose-of-a660f1e9","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","3. Identifying the components and elements of the text, and arranging events, ideas, or information according to their occurrence.","What is the purpose of a news article?","To entertain us","To teach us a lesson","To inform us about current events","To make us laugh","To inform us about current events","A news article is a type of text that informs us about current events.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-type-of-text-b6865bde","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What type of text is a map?","A poem","A letter","A map","A story","A map","A map is a type of text that shows us locations and directions.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-main-idea-7667cb95","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the main idea of a persuasive text?","The author's opinion","The author's argument","The author's conclusion","The author's introduction","The author's argument","The author's argument is the main idea, it tells us why the author believes something.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-main-idea-d9c46fc1","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the main idea of a story?","The setting of the story","The characters in the story","The plot of the story","The ending of the story","The plot of the story","The plot of the story is the main idea, it tells us what happens.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-purpose-of-cf0bc994","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the purpose of a how-to text?","To entertain us","To teach us a lesson","To give us instructions on how to do something","To make us laugh","To give us instructions on how to do something","A how-to text is a type of text that gives us instructions on how to do something.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-type-of-text-ebfb2e40","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What type of text is a recipe?","A poem","A letter","A recipe","A story","A recipe","A recipe is a type of text that gives us instructions on how to make something.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-main-idea-e7ee34df","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the main idea of a letter?","The greeting in the letter","The body of the letter","The closing of the letter","The signature of the letter","The body of the letter","The body of the letter is the main idea, it tells us what the letter is about.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-main-idea-5165ea4a","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the main idea of a poem?","The rhythm of the poem","The rhyming words in the poem","The message or theme of the poem","The pictures in the poem","The message or theme of the poem","The message or theme of the poem is the main idea, it tells us what the poem is about.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-purpose-of-5abdeb90","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the purpose of a biography?","To entertain us","To teach us a lesson","To tell us about someone's life","To make us laugh","To tell us about someone's life","A biography is a type of text that tells us about someone's life.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-type-of-text-9e06cc07","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What type of text is a diary entry?","A story","A letter","A diary entry","A poem","A diary entry","A diary entry is a type of text that is a personal account of someone's thoughts and feelings.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-purpose-of-c00aefbc","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the purpose of a conclusion in a story?","To tell us the ending","To tell us the main character's name","To summarize the story","To tell us the setting","To summarize the story","The purpose of a conclusion in a story is to summarize the story.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-how-do-we-fcb1c76d","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","How do we arrange events in a story?","In any order","In alphabetical order","In the order they happened","In reverse order","In the order they happened","We arrange events in a story in the order they happened.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-purpose-of-108082ac","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.3 Distinguishing between multiple expressions, expressing opinion about points of view, and proposing alternatives.","5. Suggesting a title, an ending different from the end of the read text, and solutions to problems or issues appeared within.","What is the purpose of a title in a story?","To tell us the ending","To tell us the main character's name","To tell us what the story is about","To tell us the setting","To tell us what the story is about","The purpose of a title in a story is to tell us what the story is about.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-how-do-we-25f9d476","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","3. Identifying the components and elements of the text, and arranging events, ideas, or information according to their occurrence.","How do we determine the text type of a story?","By looking at the title","By looking at the setting","By looking at the events","By looking at the language and structure","By looking at the language and structure","We determine the text type of a story by looking at the language and structure.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-a-text-edba1a16","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.1 Identifying vocabulary meanings in the text, their synonyms, and antonyms, classifying them according to meanings and types in terms of number and grammatical categories, and using them in meaningful sentences and new contexts.","2. Classifying vocabulary according to meanings, grammatical categories (masculine-feminine), (noun-verb-letter), and number (singular-two-plural).","What is a text type?","A story","A poem","A letter","A recipe","A story","A story is a type of text.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-setting-of-5ae6d36b","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the setting of a story?","The time and place of the story","The characters in the story","The events that happen in the story","The ending of the story","The time and place of the story","The setting of a story is the time and place of the story.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-a-character-b9b60cab","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is a character?","A place","A thing","A person or animal in a story","An event","A person or animal in a story","A character is a person or animal in a story.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-a-fact-1ba7e89f","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is a fact?","An opinion","A feeling","Information that can be proven true","A guess","Information that can be proven true","A fact is information that can be proven true.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-main-idea-d1386479","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the main idea of a story?","The setting of the story","The characters in the story","The events that happen in the story","The ending of the story","The events that happen in the story","The main idea of a story is the events that happen in the story.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-how-do-we-89a8f702","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 3","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","How do we identify the main character in a story?","By looking at the title","By looking at the setting","By looking at the events","By looking at who the story is about","By looking at who the story is about","We identify the main character in a story by looking at who the story is about.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-result-of-bdc3add9","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the result of not cleaning up after a meal?","The food becomes tastier","The table becomes cleaner","The floor becomes messy","The dishes become easier to wash","The floor becomes messy","When you don't clean up after a meal, the floor becomes messy and it's harder to clean.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-result-of-ab9c3921","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the result of not sharing toys with friends?","Everyone becomes happy","Friends become sad","Toys become more fun","Sharing becomes easier","Friends become sad","When you don't share toys with friends, they become sad because they want to play with the toys too.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-why-did-character-4a833628","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","Why did the character in the story draw a picture?","To show off their art","To make a mess","To express their feelings","To get a prize","To express their feelings","The character drew a picture to express their feelings and show what they were thinking.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-cause-of-355f7c72","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the cause of a character being late for school?","They overslept","They forgot their lunch","They got lost on the way","They were playing outside","They overslept","The character was late for school because they overslept and didn't wake up on time.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-why-did-character-78775351","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","Why did the character in the story read a book?","To fall asleep","To watch TV","To learn something new","To play a game","To learn something new","The character read a book to learn something new and expand their knowledge.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-cause-of-00aec1d1","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the cause of a character feeling sad?","They lost a toy","They got a new pet","They made a new friend","They ate a yummy treat","They lost a toy","The character felt sad because they lost a toy and were missing it.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-happens-you-mix-63d11145","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What happens when you mix oil and water?","They become best friends","They mix together","They separate into two layers","They turn into a solid","They separate into two layers","When you mix oil and water, they separate into two layers because they don't mix well.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-why-did-character-e77119d5","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","Why did the character in the story go to the park?","To play with his friends","To ride a bike","To watch a movie","To eat a sandwich","To play with his friends","The character went to the park to play with his friends because it was a fun place to be.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-why-did-character-5bab2294","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","Why did the character in the story help their friend?","Because they wanted to be boss","Because they wanted a reward","Because they felt sorry for their friend","Because they wanted to play a game","Because they felt sorry for their friend","The character helped their friend because they felt sorry for them and wanted to make them feel better.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-happens-you-plant-72a279df","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 4","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What happens when you plant a seed in the ground?","It disappears","It stays the same","It grows into a flower","It turns into a rock","It grows into a flower","When you plant a seed in the ground, it grows into a flower or a plant because it needs water and sunlight.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-result-of-db48e795","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","4. Determining causes, results, and relationships, and describing motives and actions of the characters in a text.","What is the result of a character's action in a story?","The character's action resulted in a happy ending.","The character's action resulted in a sad ending.","The character's action resulted in a new friend.","The character's action resulted in a new toy.","The character's action resulted in a happy ending.","The character's action resulted in a happy ending.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-result-of-4445802e","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the result of a problem in a story?","The problem resulted in a happy ending.","The problem resulted in a sad ending.","The problem resulted in a new friend.","The problem resulted in a new toy.","The problem resulted in a sad ending.","The problem resulted in a sad ending.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-cause-of-63604abf","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","4. Determining causes, results, and relationships, and describing motives and actions of the characters in a text.","What is the cause of a character's action in a story?","The character's action was caused by their friend.","The character's action was caused by their feelings.","The character's action was caused by their hunger.","The character's action was caused by their tiredness.","The character's action was caused by their feelings.","The character's action was caused by their feelings.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-difference-two-0a1beb25","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the difference between two characters in a story?","The characters are both wearing the same clothes.","The characters are both eating the same food.","The characters are both happy.","The characters are different ages.","The characters are different ages.","The characters are different ages.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-similarity-two-1855d000","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the similarity between two events in a story?","The events both happened in the morning.","The events both happened in the afternoon.","The events both happened on a sunny day.","The events both happened on a rainy day.","The events both happened on a sunny day.","The events both happened on a sunny day.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-difference-two-ea8022e7","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the difference between two events in a story?","The events both happened on the same day.","The events both happened on different days.","The events both happened in the same place.","The events both happened in different places.","The events both happened in different places.","The events both happened in different places.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-cause-of-115fbd7e","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","4. Determining causes, results, and relationships, and describing motives and actions of the characters in a text.","What is the cause of a problem in a story?","The problem was caused by the character's friend.","The problem was caused by the character's feelings.","The problem was caused by the character's hunger.","The problem was caused by the character's tiredness.","The problem was caused by the character's feelings.","The problem was caused by the character's feelings.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-main-idea-e626ca0d","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the main idea of a story about a boy who lost his favorite toy?","The boy was very sad.","The boy was very happy.","The boy was very angry.","The boy was very tired.","The boy was very sad.","The main idea of the story is that the boy was very sad because he lost his favorite toy.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-difference-a-d66a40d3","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the difference between a fiction and a nonfiction book?","A fiction book is true and a nonfiction book is false.","A fiction book is made up and a nonfiction book is true.","A fiction book is about animals and a nonfiction book is about people.","A fiction book is about the past and a nonfiction book is about the present.","A fiction book is made up and a nonfiction book is true.","A fiction book is made up and a nonfiction book is true.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-similarity-two-5b482fc5","English G3: Identifying explicit ideas in the text - Set 5","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.2 Identifying explicit ideas in the text, derive facts, interpreting and analyzing them, and determining text type.","1. Determining the goal of the text and identifying the main idea in a paragraph.","What is the similarity between two characters in a story?","The characters are both boys.","The characters are both girls.","The characters are both happy.","The characters are both sad.","The characters are both sad.","The characters are both sad.","","",""
