"eng-g3-3-2-is-a-synonym-9dcbe047","Vocabulary: Meanings, Synonyms & Antonyms - English (Grade 3) - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.1 Identifying vocabulary meanings in the text, their synonyms, and antonyms, classifying them according to meanings and types in terms of number and grammatical categories, and using them in meaningful sentences and new contexts.","3. Using vocabulary in meaningful sentences and new linguistic contexts.","What is a synonym for 'happy'?","Sad","Angry","Joyful","Tired","Joyful","A synonym for 'happy' is 'joyful'.","","",""
"eng-g3-3-2-is-opposite-of-a0bd8068","Vocabulary: Meanings, Synonyms & Antonyms - English (Grade 3) - Set 2","English","3","Assessment for Grade 3 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3.2.1.1.1 Identifying vocabulary meanings in the text, their synonyms, and antonyms, classifying them according to meanings and types in terms of number and grammatical categories, and using them in meaningful sentences and new contexts.","3. Using vocabulary in meaningful sentences and new linguistic contexts.","What is the opposite of 'slow'?","Fast","Happy","Sad","Big","Fast","The opposite of 'slow' is 'fast'.","","",""
