"eng-g9-9-2-word-is-a-49386142","English G9: Inferring and classifying the semantics of vocabulary - Set 5","English","9","Assessment for Grade 9 English","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9.2.1.1.1 Inferring and classifying the semantics of vocabulary, through synonymy, antonymy, context, interpretation, definition, classification, representation, and using them in new contexts.","3. Classifying vocabulary and the relationship between them according to their meanings.","Which word is a synonym for 'fastidious'?","Careless","Meticulous","Lazy","Indifferent","Meticulous","The word 'fastidious' means having a strong attention to detail and being very careful, which is similar in meaning to 'meticulous'.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-pencil-a8bf18c4","Addition & Subtraction: Three-Digit Numbers - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","1. Distinguishing the relationship between addition and subtraction for numbers up to three digits, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","If a pencil costs $27 and you buy 9 pencils, how much will you pay in total?","240 dollars","243 dollars","250 dollars","255 dollars","243 dollars","Multiply the price by the number of pencils: 27 x 9 = 243 dollars.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-basket-has-dceaf9cb","Addition & Subtraction: Three-Digit Numbers - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","1. Distinguishing the relationship between addition and subtraction for numbers up to three digits, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","A basket has 156 apples in it. If 32 apples are taken out, how many apples are left?","124 apples","130 apples","136 apples","144 apples","124 apples","Subtract the apples taken out from the starting number: 156 - 32 = 124 apples.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-toy-cb4a9ad5","Addition & Subtraction: Three-Digit Numbers - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","1. Distinguishing the relationship between addition and subtraction for numbers up to three digits, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","If a toy costs $166 and you pay with a $200 bill, how much change will you get?","34 dollars","40 dollars","46 dollars","50 dollars","34 dollars","Subtract the cost from the amount paid: 200 - 166 = 34 dollars.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-bag-has-d6cb567b","Addition & Subtraction: Three-Digit Numbers - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","1. Distinguishing the relationship between addition and subtraction for numbers up to three digits, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","A bag has 219 stickers in it. If 18 stickers are taken out, how many stickers are left?","201 stickers","206 stickers","211 stickers","216 stickers","201 stickers","Subtract the stickers taken out from the starting number: 219 - 18 = 201 stickers.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-toy-bb83a638","Addition & Subtraction: Three-Digit Numbers - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","1. Distinguishing the relationship between addition and subtraction for numbers up to three digits, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","If a toy car costs $65 and you pay with a $100 bill, how much change will you get?","35 dollars","40 dollars","45 dollars","50 dollars","35 dollars","Subtract the cost from the amount paid: 100 - 65 = 35 dollars.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-box-has-e82514e9","Addition & Subtraction: Three-Digit Numbers - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","1. Distinguishing the relationship between addition and subtraction for numbers up to three digits, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","A box has 219 crayons in it. If 17 crayons are taken out, how many crayons are left?","202 crayons","207 crayons","212 crayons","218 crayons","202 crayons","Subtract the crayons taken out from the starting number: 219 - 17 = 202 crayons.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-jar-has-e6d5d1ce","Addition & Subtraction: Three-Digit Numbers - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","1. Distinguishing the relationship between addition and subtraction for numbers up to three digits, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","A jar has 156 marbles in it. If 31 marbles are taken out, how many marbles are left?","125 marbles","130 marbles","135 marbles","140 marbles","125 marbles","Subtract the marbles taken out from the starting number: 156 - 31 = 125 marbles.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-sally-has-69efaab1","Addition & Subtraction: Three-Digit Numbers - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","1. Distinguishing the relationship between addition and subtraction for numbers up to three digits, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","If Sally has 145 pencils and she gives 27 pencils to her friend, how many pencils does Sally have left?","118 pencils","117 pencils","127 pencils","137 pencils","118 pencils","Subtract the pencils given away from the starting number: 145 - 27 = 118 pencils.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-bookshelf-has-68ca6062","Addition & Subtraction: Three-Digit Numbers - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","1. Distinguishing the relationship between addition and subtraction for numbers up to three digits, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","A bookshelf has 234 books on it. If 19 books are removed, how many books are left?","215 books","220 books","225 books","230 books","215 books","Subtract the books removed from the starting number: 234 - 19 = 215 books.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-book-80328ac7","Addition & Subtraction: Three-Digit Numbers - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","1. Distinguishing the relationship between addition and subtraction for numbers up to three digits, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","If a book costs $75 and you pay with a $100 bill and a $20 bill, how much change will you get?","45 dollars","50 dollars","55 dollars","60 dollars","45 dollars","A $100 bill and a $20 bill total $120. Subtract the cost: 120 - 75 = 45 dollars.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-is-value-of-5163a77a","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","1. Distinguishing the types of coins and banknotes and using them to count amounts up to 9999 riyals.","What is the value of 2 riyals and 3 riyals?","5 riyals","4 riyals","6 riyals","50 riyals","5 riyals","When we add 2 riyals and 3 riyals, we get 5 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-is-value-of-0cb11c3b","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","1. Distinguishing the types of coins and banknotes and using them to count amounts up to 9999 riyals.","What is the value of 1 riyal and 1 riyal?","1 riyal","2 riyals","1 riyal and 1 riyal","3 riyals","1 riyal and 1 riyal","1 riyal and 1 riyal is equal to 2 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-is-value-of-d967b5e1","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","1. Distinguishing the types of coins and banknotes and using them to count amounts up to 9999 riyals.","What is the value of 3 riyals and 1 riyal?","2 riyals","1 riyal","4 riyals","5 riyals","4 riyals","The stated calculation gives 4 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-how-much-is-74768ddc","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","1. Distinguishing the types of coins and banknotes and using them to count amounts up to 9999 riyals.","How much is 2 riyals and 2 riyals?","4 riyals","1 riyal","2 riyals","5 riyals","4 riyals","When we add 2 riyals and 2 riyals, we get 4 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-is-value-of-bfb128d8","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","1. Distinguishing the types of coins and banknotes and using them to count amounts up to 9999 riyals.","What is the value of 3 riyals and 2 riyals?","5 riyals","4 riyals","6 riyals","50 riyals","5 riyals","When we add 3 riyals and 2 riyals, we get 5 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-how-much-is-192efca5","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","1. Distinguishing the types of coins and banknotes and using them to count amounts up to 9999 riyals.","How much is 1 riyal and 2 riyals?","3 riyals","2 riyals","4 riyals","30 riyals","3 riyals","1 riyal and 2 riyals is equal to 3 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-how-much-is-44761bd9","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","1. Distinguishing the types of coins and banknotes and using them to count amounts up to 9999 riyals.","How many halalas are equal to 1 riyal and 50 halalas?","100 halalas","50 halalas","150 halalas","1 halala","150 halalas","1 riyal equals 100 halalas, so 1 riyal and 50 halalas equals 100 + 50 = 150 halalas.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-is-value-of-15d47912","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","1. Distinguishing the types of coins and banknotes and using them to count amounts up to 9999 riyals.","What is the value of 5 riyals and 2 riyals?","7 riyals","5 riyals","2 riyals","10 riyals","7 riyals","When we add 5 riyals and 2 riyals, we get 7 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-how-much-is-006c1333","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","1. Distinguishing the types of coins and banknotes and using them to count amounts up to 9999 riyals.","How much is 5 riyals and 1 riyal?","6 riyals","1 riyal","5 riyals","10 riyals","6 riyals","When we add 5 riyals and 1 riyal, we get 6 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-how-much-is-ad258d3a","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","1. Distinguishing the types of coins and banknotes and using them to count amounts up to 9999 riyals.","How much is 1 riyal and 3 riyals?","4 riyals","3 riyals","5 riyals","40 riyals","4 riyals","1 riyal and 3 riyals is equal to 4 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-44a7c410","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3) - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 2 riyals and I get 4 riyals, how much money do I have now?","I have 6 riyals now.","I have 2 riyals now.","I have 1 riyal now.","I have 5 riyals now.","I have 6 riyals now.","We add 4 riyals to the 2 riyals we already have, so we have 6 riyals now.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-1bf1adc0","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3) - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 7 riyals and I spend 1 riyal, how much money do I have left?","I have 6 riyals left.","I have 8 riyals left.","I have 5 riyals left.","I have 10 riyals left.","I have 6 riyals left.","We subtract 1 riyal from the 7 riyals we had, so we have 6 riyals left.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-8a0a2011","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3) - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 9 riyals and I spend 4 riyals, how much money do I have left?","I have 5 riyals left.","I have 13 riyals left.","I have 3 riyals left.","I have 10 riyals left.","I have 5 riyals left.","We subtract 4 riyals from the 9 riyals we had, so we have 5 riyals left.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-f0b3371d","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3) - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 6 riyals and I spend 2 riyals, how much money do I have left?","I have 4 riyals left.","I have 8 riyals left.","I have 3 riyals left.","I have 10 riyals left.","I have 4 riyals left.","We subtract 2 riyals from the 6 riyals we had, so we have 4 riyals left.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-37db42ef","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3) - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 4 riyals and I get 1 riyal, how much money do I have now?","I have 5 riyals now.","I have 3 riyals now.","I have 6 riyals now.","I have 2 riyals now.","I have 5 riyals now.","We add 1 riyal to the 4 riyals we already have, so we have 5 riyals now.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-65cc3217","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3) - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 8 riyals and I spend 3 riyals, how much money do I have left?","I have 5 riyals left.","I have 11 riyals left.","I have 1 riyal left.","I have 10 riyals left.","I have 5 riyals left.","We subtract 3 riyals from the 8 riyals we had, so we have 5 riyals left.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-813a9083","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3) - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 3 riyals and I get 1 riyal, how much money do I have now?","I have 4 riyals now.","I have 2 riyals now.","I have 5 riyals now.","I have 1 riyal now.","I have 4 riyals now.","We add 1 riyal to the 3 riyals we already have, so we have 4 riyals now.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-855cb1c2","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3) - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 1 riyal and I get 2 riyals, how much money do I have now?","I have 3 riyals now.","I have 1 riyal now.","I have 4 riyals now.","I have 2 riyals now.","I have 3 riyals now.","The stated calculation gives 3 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-02ee0437","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3) - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 5 riyals and I spend 4 riyals, how much money do I have left?","I have 1 riyal left.","I have 9 riyals left.","I have 3 riyals left.","I have 10 riyals left.","I have 1 riyal left.","We subtract 4 riyals from the 5 riyals we had, so we have 1 riyal left.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-6f0a7506","Currency: Denominations & Financial Problems - Math (Grade 3) - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 5 riyals and I get 2 more, how much money do I have now?","I have 7 riyals now.","I have 3 riyals now.","I have 10 riyals now.","I have 1 riyal now.","I have 7 riyals now.","We add 2 riyals to the 5 riyals we already have, so we have 7 riyals now.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-group-2385bcbf","Four Operations: Characteristics & Verification - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","2. Distinguishing the commutative property of addition and multiplication and using it to find the results and verify their correctness.","If a group of friends have 15 pencils and they give 3 pencils to another group, then they have 15 - 3 = ? pencils.","12 pencils","18 pencils","15 pencils","20 pencils","12 pencils","The commutative property of addition states that the order of the numbers does not change the result. 15 - 3 is the same as 3 - 15.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-pencil-561c17d4","Four Operations: Characteristics & Verification - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","2. Distinguishing the commutative property of addition and multiplication and using it to find the results and verify their correctness.","If a pencil has a length of 12 cm and it is extended by 5 cm, then it is now 12 + 5 = ? cm long.","17 cm","15 cm","12 cm","18 cm","17 cm","The commutative property of addition states that the order of the numbers does not change the result. 12 + 5 is the same as 5 + 12.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-toy-3863a763","Four Operations: Characteristics & Verification - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","2. Distinguishing the commutative property of addition and multiplication and using it to find the results and verify their correctness.","If a toy car track is 8 meters long and it is shortened by 2 meters, then it is now 8 - 2 = ? meters long.","6 meters","10 meters","4 meters","8 meters","6 meters","The commutative property of addition states that the order of the numbers does not change the result. 8 - 2 is the same as 2 - 8.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-group-67c220cf","Four Operations: Characteristics & Verification - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","2. Distinguishing the commutative property of addition and multiplication and using it to find the results and verify their correctness.","If a group of friends have 12 pencils and they give 4 pencils to another group, then they have 12 - 4 = ? pencils.","8 pencils","10 pencils","12 pencils","16 pencils","8 pencils","The commutative property of addition states that the order of the numbers does not change the result. 12 - 4 is the same as 4 - 12.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-basket-85be3afb","Four Operations: Characteristics & Verification - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","2. Distinguishing the commutative property of addition and multiplication and using it to find the results and verify their correctness.","If a basket has 7 apples in it and 2 more apples are added, then it has 7 + 2 = ? apples.","9 apples","8 apples","10 apples","5 apples","9 apples","The commutative property of addition states that the order of the numbers does not change the result. 7 + 2 is the same as 2 + 7.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-toy-212bceff","Four Operations: Characteristics & Verification - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","2. Distinguishing the commutative property of addition and multiplication and using it to find the results and verify their correctness.","If a toy car track is 6 meters long and it is extended by 2 meters, then it is now 6 + 2 = ? meters long.","8 meters","10 meters","4 meters","6 meters","8 meters","The commutative property of addition states that the order of the numbers does not change the result. 6 + 2 is the same as 2 + 6.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-bookshelf-590ba287","Four Operations: Characteristics & Verification - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","2. Distinguishing the commutative property of addition and multiplication and using it to find the results and verify their correctness.","If a bookshelf has 8 books on it and 4 more books are added, then it has 8 + 4 = ? books.","10 books","12 books","6 books","4 books","12 books","The commutative property of addition states that the order of the numbers does not change the result. 8 + 4 is the same as 4 + 8.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-sally-has-14e9073f","Four Operations: Characteristics & Verification - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","2. Distinguishing the commutative property of addition and multiplication and using it to find the results and verify their correctness.","If Sally has 5 pencils and she gives 2 to her friend, then she has 5 + 2 = ? pencils.","7 pencils","5 pencils","3 pencils","9 pencils","3 pencils","The commutative property of addition states that the order of the numbers does not change the result. 5 + 2 is the same as 2 + 5.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-basket-f21d2cd6","Four Operations: Characteristics & Verification - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","2. Distinguishing the commutative property of addition and multiplication and using it to find the results and verify their correctness.","If a basket has 9 apples in it and 1 more apple is added, then it has 9 + 1 = ? apples.","10 apples","8 apples","11 apples","7 apples","10 apples","The commutative property of addition states that the order of the numbers does not change the result. 9 + 1 is the same as 1 + 9.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-pencil-8bd8293e","Four Operations: Characteristics & Verification - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","2. Distinguishing the commutative property of addition and multiplication and using it to find the results and verify their correctness.","If a pencil has a length of 15 cm and it is extended by 3 cm, then it is now 15 + 3 = ? cm long.","18 cm","20 cm","12 cm","15 cm","18 cm","The commutative property of addition states that the order of the numbers does not change the result. 15 + 3 is the same as 3 + 15.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-bookshelf-0d72a69e","Four Operations: Characteristics & Verification - Math (Grade 3) - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","3. Distinguishing the associative property of addition and multiplication and using it to find the result of adding three numbers within 2-digit, and the result of multiplying several numbers of 1-digit mentally.","If a bookshelf has 5 shelves, and each shelf can hold 4 books, how many books can the bookshelf hold in total?","The bookshelf can hold 18 books.","The bookshelf can hold 20 books.","The bookshelf can hold 22 books.","The bookshelf can hold 24 books.","The bookshelf can hold 18 books.","We can use the associative property of multiplication to find the result. First, we multiply 5 and 4, which is 20.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-basket-fdd42b8f","Four Operations: Characteristics & Verification - Math (Grade 3) - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","2. Distinguishing the relationship between multiplication and addition, and using it to find the result and verify its correctness.","If a basket has 12 apples and we take away 4 apples, then we take away 2 more apples. How many apples are left in the basket?","There are 6 apples left.","8 apples","10 apples","12 apples","There are 6 apples left.","12 - 4 - 2 = 6 apples.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-toy-5c43666d","Four Operations: Characteristics & Verification - Math (Grade 3) - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","3. Distinguishing the associative property of addition and multiplication and using it to find the result of adding three numbers within 2-digit, and the result of multiplying several numbers of 1-digit mentally.","If a toy box has 15 toys and we add 2 more toys, then we add 3 more toys. How many toys are in the toy box now?","There are 18 toys in the toy box.","There are 20 toys in the toy box.","There are 22 toys in the toy box.","There are 24 toys in the toy box.","There are 18 toys in the toy box.","We can use the associative property of addition to find the result. First, we add 15 and 2, which is 17. Then, we add 3 to 17, which is 20.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-sally-has-08c05756","Four Operations: Characteristics & Verification - Math (Grade 3) - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","2. Distinguishing the relationship between multiplication and addition, and using it to find the result and verify its correctness.","If Sally has 15 pencils and she gives 3 to her friend, then she gives 2 more to her brother. How many pencils does Sally have left?","She has 10 pencils left.","She has 13 pencils left.","She has 12 pencils left.","She has 15 pencils left.","She has 10 pencils left.","15 - 3 - 2 = 10 pencils.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-toy-568cd591","Four Operations: Characteristics & Verification - Math (Grade 3) - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-1 Distinguishing the characteristics of four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","2. Distinguishing the relationship between multiplication and addition, and using it to find the result and verify its correctness.","If a toy car costs $8 and a toy truck costs $5, how much will it cost to buy 2 toy cars and 3 toy trucks?","It will cost $31.","$26","$36","$13","It will cost $31.","2 toy cars cost $16, and 3 toy trucks cost $15. Total cost is $31.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-shape-has-five-c1807f39","Four Operations: Relations & Properties - Math (Grade 3)","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-2 Distinguishing the relations between the four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","1. Describing and classifying two-dimensional geometric shapes (triangle, square, rectangle, circle, parallelogram, trapezoid, pentagon, hexagon), and comparing them based on the number of sides, the number of vertices, and the congruence of sides.","What shape has five sides?","A square has four sides","A triangle has three sides","A pentagon has five sides","A hexagon has six sides","A pentagon has five sides","A pentagon has five sides.","","",""
