"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-you-have-86db0a83","Math G3: Describing non-numerical patterns - Set 1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-1-1 Describing non-numerical patterns, numerical patterns, and growing geometric patterns, completing and expanding them.","1. Distinguishing the properties of addition and subtraction with zero, multiplication and division with one, and multiplication with zero, and applying them to find results","If you have 2 groups of 5 pencils and you add 0 more pencils, how many pencils do you have now?","10 pencils","5 pencils","0 pencils","I don't know","10 pencils","When you add 0, the number doesn't change.","","",""
