"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-toy-car-2271f2a6","Math G3: Describing non-numerical patterns - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-1-1 Describing non-numerical patterns, numerical patterns, and growing geometric patterns, completing and expanding them.","1. Distinguishing the properties of addition and subtraction with zero, multiplication and division with one, and multiplication with zero, and applying them to find results","A toy car track is 8 blocks long. If we add 3 more blocks, how long will the track be?","The track will be 5 blocks long","The track will be 8 blocks long","The track will be 11 blocks long","The track will be 15 blocks long","The track will be 11 blocks long","The pattern is adding 3 blocks each time, so 8 + 3 = 11.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-we-have-c9ed41c9","Math G3: Describing non-numerical patterns - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-1-1 Describing non-numerical patterns, numerical patterns, and growing geometric patterns, completing and expanding them.","1. Distinguishing the properties of addition and subtraction with zero, multiplication and division with one, and multiplication with zero, and applying them to find results","If we have 4 groups of 3 toys, how many toys do we have in total?","We have 12 toys","We have 7 toys","We have 15 toys","We have 8 toys","We have 12 toys","4 groups of 3 equals 4 x 3 = 12.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-we-have-87accc65","Math G3: Describing non-numerical patterns - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-1-1 Describing non-numerical patterns, numerical patterns, and growing geometric patterns, completing and expanding them.","1. Distinguishing the properties of addition and subtraction with zero, multiplication and division with one, and multiplication with zero, and applying them to find results","If we have 3 groups of 2 toys, how many toys do we have in total?","We have 6 toys","We have 5 toys","We have 8 toys","We have 3 toys","We have 6 toys","3 groups of 2 equals 3 x 2 = 6.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-we-have-44e11e34","Math G3: Describing non-numerical patterns - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-1-1 Describing non-numerical patterns, numerical patterns, and growing geometric patterns, completing and expanding them.","1. Distinguishing the properties of addition and subtraction with zero, multiplication and division with one, and multiplication with zero, and applying them to find results","If we have 5 pencils and we add 1 more, then we have 6 pencils. What will we have if we add 1 more pencil?","We will have 5 pencils","We will have 6 pencils","We will have 7 pencils","We will have 8 pencils","We will have 7 pencils","The pattern is adding 1 pencil each time, so 6 + 1 = 7.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-we-have-edc09934","Math G3: Describing non-numerical patterns - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-1-1 Describing non-numerical patterns, numerical patterns, and growing geometric patterns, completing and expanding them.","1. Distinguishing the properties of addition and subtraction with zero, multiplication and division with one, and multiplication with zero, and applying them to find results","If we have 8 blocks and we add 1 more block, how many blocks do we have in total?","We have 7 blocks","We have 8 blocks","We have 9 blocks","We have 10 blocks","We have 9 blocks","The pattern is adding 1 block each time, so 8 + 1 = 9.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-we-have-65b79416","Math G3: Describing non-numerical patterns - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-1-1 Describing non-numerical patterns, numerical patterns, and growing geometric patterns, completing and expanding them.","1. Distinguishing the properties of addition and subtraction with zero, multiplication and division with one, and multiplication with zero, and applying them to find results","If we have 2 groups of 4 toys, how many toys do we have in total?","We have 8 toys","We have 6 toys","We have 12 toys","We have 10 toys","We have 8 toys","2 groups of 4 equals 2 x 4 = 8.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-we-have-ba603e61","Math G3: Describing non-numerical patterns - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-1-1 Describing non-numerical patterns, numerical patterns, and growing geometric patterns, completing and expanding them.","1. Distinguishing the properties of addition and subtraction with zero, multiplication and division with one, and multiplication with zero, and applying them to find results","If we have 2 groups of 5 pencils, how many pencils do we have in total?","We have 10 pencils","We have 7 pencils","We have 15 pencils","We have 8 pencils","We have 10 pencils","2 groups of 5 equals 2 x 5 = 10.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-we-have-8babc408","Math G3: Describing non-numerical patterns - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-1-1 Describing non-numerical patterns, numerical patterns, and growing geometric patterns, completing and expanding them.","1. Distinguishing the properties of addition and subtraction with zero, multiplication and division with one, and multiplication with zero, and applying them to find results","If we have 6 blocks and we take away 2 blocks, how many blocks do we have left?","We have 4 blocks","We have 6 blocks","We have 8 blocks","We have 10 blocks","We have 4 blocks","The pattern is subtracting 2 blocks each time, so 6 - 2 = 4.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-we-have-0e3d5f5d","Math G3: Describing non-numerical patterns - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-1-1 Describing non-numerical patterns, numerical patterns, and growing geometric patterns, completing and expanding them.","1. Distinguishing the properties of addition and subtraction with zero, multiplication and division with one, and multiplication with zero, and applying them to find results","If we have 6 pencils and we take away 2 pencils, how many pencils do we have left?","We have 4 pencils","We have 6 pencils","We have 8 pencils","We have 10 pencils","We have 4 pencils","The pattern is subtracting 2 pencils each time, so 6 - 2 = 4.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-sally-has-79a95ee2","Math G3: Describing non-numerical patterns - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-1-1 Describing non-numerical patterns, numerical patterns, and growing geometric patterns, completing and expanding them.","1. Distinguishing the properties of addition and subtraction with zero, multiplication and division with one, and multiplication with zero, and applying them to find results","If Sally has 5 pencils and she adds 2 more, then she has 7 pencils. What will she have if she adds 2 more pencils?","She will have 5 pencils","She will have 7 pencils","She will have 9 pencils","She will have 11 pencils","She will have 9 pencils","The pattern is adding 2 pencils each time, so 7 + 2 = 9.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-you-have-e20423c3","Math G3: Distinguishing currency denominations - Set 1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","1. Distinguishing the types of coins and banknotes and using them to count amounts up to 9999 riyals.","If you have a 5-riyal banknote and a 2-riyal coin, how much money do you have in total?","5 riyals","6 riyals","7 riyals","10 riyals","7 riyals","Because the banknote is worth 5 riyals and the coin is worth 2 riyals, so 5 + 2 = 7 riyals.","","",""
