"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-you-have-75d2f115","Math G3: Distinguishing currency denominations - Set 1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","1. Distinguishing the types of coins and banknotes and using them to count amounts up to 9999 riyals.","If you have 3 five-riyal coins, how much money do you have?","10 riyals","15 riyals","20 riyals","25 riyals","15 riyals","Because each coin is worth 5 riyals and you have 3 coins, so 5 x 3 = 15 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-how-many-1-e2061d05","Math G3: Distinguishing currency denominations - Set 1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","1. Distinguishing the types of coins and banknotes and using them to count amounts up to 9999 riyals.","How many 1-riyal coins are needed to make 8 riyals?","5 coins","6 coins","7 coins","8 coins","8 coins","Because each coin is worth 1 riyal, so to make 8 riyals, you need 8 coins.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-f8d74459","Math G3: Distinguishing currency denominations - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 300 riyals and I spend 100 riyals, how much money do I have left?","200 riyals","300 riyals","400 riyals","500 riyals","200 riyals","To find the amount of money left, we need to subtract the amount spent from the amount I had: 300 riyals - 100 riyals = 200 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-book-costs-806866e8","Math G3: Distinguishing currency denominations - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","1. Distinguishing the types of coins and banknotes and using them to count amounts up to 9999 riyals.","A book costs 50 riyals. If I pay with a 100 riyal bill, how much change will I get?","50 riyals","20 riyals","30 riyals","40 riyals","50 riyals","To find the change, we need to subtract the cost of the book from the amount paid: 100 riyals - 50 riyals = 50 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-pencil-costs-1f12f009","Math G3: Distinguishing currency denominations - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","1. Distinguishing the types of coins and banknotes and using them to count amounts up to 9999 riyals.","A pencil costs 5 riyals. If I pay with a 10 riyal bill, how much change will I get?","3 riyals","5 riyals","10 riyals","15 riyals","5 riyals","To find the change, we need to subtract the cost of the pencil from the amount paid: 10 riyals - 5 riyals = 5 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-book-costs-250283f5","Math G3: Distinguishing currency denominations - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","A book costs 25 riyals. If I have 50 riyals, how much money will I have left after buying the book?","25 riyals","30 riyals","50 riyals","75 riyals","25 riyals","To find the amount of money left, we need to subtract the cost of the book from the amount I have: 50 riyals - 25 riyals = 25 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-d830c906","Math G3: Distinguishing currency denominations - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 150 riyals and my brother has 250 riyals, who has more money?","I have more money","My brother has more money","We have the same amount of money","I do not have any money","My brother has more money","To compare the amounts, we need to look at the numbers: 250 riyals is more than 150 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-7037aef1","Math G3: Distinguishing currency denominations - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 400 riyals and my friend has 600 riyals, how much money do we have in total?","800 riyals","1000 riyals","1200 riyals","1400 riyals","1000 riyals","To find the total amount of money, we need to add the amount I have to the amount my friend has: 400 riyals + 600 riyals = 1000 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-b9070aba","Math G3: Distinguishing currency denominations - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 500 riyals and my friend has 200 riyals, how much money do we have in total?","700 riyals","1000 riyals","500 riyals","300 riyals","700 riyals","To find the total amount of money, we need to add the amount I have to the amount my friend has: 500 riyals + 200 riyals = 700 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-2a38f31d","Math G3: Distinguishing currency denominations - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 2 bills of 50 riyals each, how much money do I have in total?","50 riyals","100 riyals","150 riyals","200 riyals","100 riyals","To find the total amount of money, we need to multiply the number of bills by the value of each bill: 2 * 50 riyals = 100 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-a14e1c15","Math G3: Distinguishing currency denominations - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","If I have 3 bills of 100 riyals each, how much money do I have in total?","200 riyals","300 riyals","400 riyals","500 riyals","300 riyals","To find the total amount of money, we need to multiply the number of bills by the value of each bill: 3 * 100 riyals = 300 riyals.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-toy-car-5f50b18a","Math G3: Distinguishing currency denominations - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-3 Distinguishing currency denominations, using them for counting, representing amounts, and comparing them, and solving mathematical problems including financial applications.","2. Representing amounts up to 9999 riyals by using money categories in a variety of ways, and comparing them.","A toy car costs 20 riyals. If I have 50 riyals, how much money will I have left after buying the toy car?","30 riyals","40 riyals","50 riyals","60 riyals","30 riyals","To find the amount of money left, we need to subtract the cost of the toy car from the amount I have: 50 riyals - 20 riyals = 30 riyals.","","",""
