"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-toy-car-fec3fee6","Math G3: Distinguishing the relations between the four operations - Set 4","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-2 Distinguishing the relations between the four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","4. Distinguishing the relationship between multiplication and division, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","A toy car track is 12 feet long, and it needs to be divided into sections that are 2 feet long. How many sections can be made?","We can make 5 sections","We can make 6 sections","We can make 7 sections","We can make 8 sections","We can make 6 sections","Because 12 divided by 2 equals 6, so we can make 6 sections that are 2 feet long.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-f2ce96b9","Math G3: Distinguishing the relations between the four operations - Set 4","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-2 Distinguishing the relations between the four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","4. Distinguishing the relationship between multiplication and division, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","If I have 18 marbles and I want to put them in boxes of 3, how many boxes can I make?","I can make 5 boxes","I can make 6 boxes","I can make 7 boxes","I can make 8 boxes","I can make 6 boxes","Because 18 divided by 3 equals 6, so I can make 6 boxes with 3 marbles in each.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-group-of-559411e6","Math G3: Distinguishing the relations between the four operations - Set 4","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-2 Distinguishing the relations between the four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","4. Distinguishing the relationship between multiplication and division, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","A group of friends want to share some candy equally. If they have 20 pieces of candy and there are 4 friends, how many pieces will each friend get?","Each friend will get 4 pieces","Each friend will get 5 pieces","Each friend will get 6 pieces","Each friend will get 7 pieces","Each friend will get 5 pieces","Because 20 divided by 4 equals 5, so each friend will get 5 pieces of candy.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-6eea5e2b","Math G3: Distinguishing the relations between the four operations - Set 4","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-2 Distinguishing the relations between the four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","4. Distinguishing the relationship between multiplication and division, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","If I have 15 stickers and I want to put them in rows of 5, how many rows can I make?","I can make 2 rows","I can make 3 rows","I can make 4 rows","I can make 5 rows","I can make 3 rows","Because 15 divided by 5 equals 3, so I can make 3 rows with 5 stickers in each.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-92953fcf","Math G3: Distinguishing the relations between the four operations - Set 4","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-2 Distinguishing the relations between the four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","4. Distinguishing the relationship between multiplication and division, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","If I have 9 crayons and I want to share them equally among 3 of my friends, how many crayons will each friend get?","Each friend will get 2 crayons","Each friend will get 3 crayons","Each friend will get 4 crayons","Each friend will get 5 crayons","Each friend will get 3 crayons","Because 9 divided by 3 equals 3, so each friend will get 3 crayons.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-basket-contains-10d6fa56","Math G3: Distinguishing the relations between the four operations - Set 4","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-2 Distinguishing the relations between the four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","4. Distinguishing the relationship between multiplication and division, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","A basket contains 24 apples, and they need to be packed in bags that hold 4 apples each. How many bags are needed?","We need 5 bags","We need 6 bags","We need 7 bags","We need 8 bags","We need 6 bags","Because 24 divided by 4 equals 6, so we need 6 bags to pack all the apples.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-eee14b1c","Math G3: Distinguishing the relations between the four operations - Set 4","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-2 Distinguishing the relations between the four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","4. Distinguishing the relationship between multiplication and division, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","If I have 16 buttons and I want to put them in bags of 2, how many bags can I fill?","I can fill 6 bags","I can fill 7 bags","I can fill 8 bags","I can fill 9 bags","I can fill 8 bags","Because 16 divided by 2 equals 8, so I can fill 8 bags with 2 buttons in each.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-bookshelf-has-b53134b4","Math G3: Distinguishing the relations between the four operations - Set 4","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-2 Distinguishing the relations between the four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","4. Distinguishing the relationship between multiplication and division, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","A bookshelf has 18 books on it, and they need to be packed in boxes that hold 3 books each. How many boxes are needed?","We need 5 boxes","We need 6 boxes","We need 7 boxes","We need 8 boxes","We need 6 boxes","Because 18 divided by 3 equals 6, so we need 6 boxes to pack all the books.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-i-have-8bf808f3","Math G3: Distinguishing the relations between the four operations - Set 4","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-2 Distinguishing the relations between the four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","4. Distinguishing the relationship between multiplication and division, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","If I have 12 pencils and I want to put them in boxes of 4, how many boxes can I make?","I can make 2 boxes","I can make 3 boxes","I can make 4 boxes","I can make 6 boxes","I can make 3 boxes","Because 12 divided by 4 equals 3, so I can make 3 boxes with 4 pencils in each.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-library-has-2f15db58","Math G3: Distinguishing the relations between the four operations - Set 4","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-2 Distinguishing the relations between the four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","4. Distinguishing the relationship between multiplication and division, and using it to find results and verify their correctness.","A library has 24 books that need to be put on shelves that hold 4 books each. How many shelves can be filled?","We can fill 5 shelves","We can fill 6 shelves","We can fill 7 shelves","We can fill 8 shelves","We can fill 6 shelves","Because 24 divided by 4 equals 6, so we can fill 6 shelves with 4 books on each.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-it-takes-2cac0c44","Math G3: Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of - Set 1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-4 Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of time, reading and writing time, and solving mathematical problems including time applications.","1. Selecting the suitable units of time (seconds, minutes, hours) to estimate the duration of an event.","If it takes 30 minutes to eat breakfast, and you start eating at 7:00, what time will you finish?","6:30","7:30","8:00","8:30","7:30","If it takes 30 minutes to eat breakfast, and you start eating at 7:00, you will finish at 7:30.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-bus-ride-e38a77ec","Math G3: Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of - Set 1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-4 Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of time, reading and writing time, and solving mathematical problems including time applications.","1. Selecting the suitable units of time (seconds, minutes, hours) to estimate the duration of an event.","A bus ride takes 25 minutes. If the bus leaves the stop at 8:10, what time will it arrive at school?","8:30","8:35","8:40","8:45","8:35","If the bus ride takes 25 minutes, and the bus leaves the stop at 8:10, you will add 25 minutes to 8:10, which results in 8:35.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-it-takes-04b83578","Math G3: Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of - Set 1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-4 Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of time, reading and writing time, and solving mathematical problems including time applications.","1. Selecting the suitable units of time (seconds, minutes, hours) to estimate the duration of an event.","If it takes 15 minutes to walk from the classroom to the cafeteria, and you leave the classroom at 11:45, what time will you arrive at the cafeteria?","11:50","11:55","0.5","12:00","12:00","If it takes 15 minutes to walk from the classroom to the cafeteria, and you leave the classroom at 11:45, you will add 15 minutes to 11:45, which results in 12:00.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-frequency-table-5153efaa","Math G3: Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of - Set 1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-4 Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of time, reading and writing time, and solving mathematical problems including time applications.","1. Collecting data from the environment and organizing it into multiple categories by using frequency tables.","A frequency table shows that 5 students arrived at school at 7:45, 10 students arrived at 8:00, and 3 students arrived at 8:15. What time did most students arrive at school?","7:45","8:00","8:15","8:30","8:00","According to the frequency table, 10 students arrived at 8:00, which is the highest number, so most students arrived at school at 8:00.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-is-purpose-of-7ac7abb7","Math G3: Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of - Set 1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-4 Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of time, reading and writing time, and solving mathematical problems including time applications.","1. Collecting data from the environment and organizing it into multiple categories by using frequency tables.","What is the purpose of using a frequency table to collect data about the time students arrive at school?","To find the heaviest student","To find the tallest student","To find the time when most students arrive","To find the student who lives farthest from school","To find the time when most students arrive","The purpose of using a frequency table is to organize and analyze data, and in this case, it helps to find the time when most students arrive at school.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-a-student-90ea29bb","Math G3: Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of - Set 1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-4 Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of time, reading and writing time, and solving mathematical problems including time applications.","1. Selecting the suitable units of time (seconds, minutes, hours) to estimate the duration of an event.","If a student wakes up at 6:30 and it takes 30 minutes to get dressed, what time will the student be ready to leave for school?","6:45","7:00","7:15","7:30","7:00","If the student wakes up at 6:30 and it takes 30 minutes to get dressed, the student will be ready to leave for school at 7:00.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-is-best-way-6fa14482","Math G3: Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of - Set 1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-4 Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of time, reading and writing time, and solving mathematical problems including time applications.","1. Selecting the suitable units of time (seconds, minutes, hours) to estimate the duration of an event.","What is the best way to measure the time it takes to walk from home to school?","Using a calendar to count the days","Using a clock to measure the hours and minutes","Using a ruler to measure the distance","Using a scale to measure the weight","Using a clock to measure the hours and minutes","A clock is the best tool to measure time, and it can measure hours and minutes, which is suitable for measuring the time it takes to walk from home to school.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-it-takes-b386f0c2","Math G3: Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of - Set 1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-4 Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of time, reading and writing time, and solving mathematical problems including time applications.","1. Selecting the suitable units of time (seconds, minutes, hours) to estimate the duration of an event.","If it takes 20 minutes to walk to the library, and you leave home at 3:45, what time will you arrive at the library?","4:05","4:15","4:25","4:45","4:05","Add 20 minutes to 3:45. The arrival time is 4:05.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-if-you-have-4a12ccf4","Math G3: Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of - Set 1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-4 Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of time, reading and writing time, and solving mathematical problems including time applications.","1. Selecting the suitable units of time (seconds, minutes, hours) to estimate the duration of an event.","If you have a 45-minute recess, and you start playing at 10:15, what time will recess end?","10:45","0.458333333","11:00","11:15","11:00","If you start playing at 10:15, and recess lasts for 45 minutes, you will add 45 minutes to 10:15, which results in 11:00.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-a-student-has-1ea059f4","Math G3: Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of - Set 1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-4 Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of time, reading and writing time, and solving mathematical problems including time applications.","1. Selecting the suitable units of time (seconds, minutes, hours) to estimate the duration of an event.","A student has a schedule that includes 30 minutes for breakfast, 60 minutes for lunch, and 45 minutes for recess. What is the total time spent on these activities?","1 hour","1 hour 15 minutes","2 hours 15 minutes","1 hour 45 minutes","2 hours 15 minutes","30 minutes + 60 minutes + 45 minutes = 135 minutes, which is 2 hours and 15 minutes.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-how-long-it-f46ba11c","Math G3: Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of - Set 1 T1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-4 Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of time, reading and writing time, and solving mathematical problems including time applications.","1. Selecting the suitable units of time (seconds, minutes, hours) to estimate the duration of an event.","How long does it take to get to school?","a few seconds","a few minutes","a few hours","a few days","a few minutes","It usually takes a few minutes to get to school, depending on how far you live.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-is-best-unit-175a2038","Math G3: Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of - Set 1 T1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-4 Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of time, reading and writing time, and solving mathematical problems including time applications.","1. Selecting the suitable units of time (seconds, minutes, hours) to estimate the duration of an event.","What is the best unit of time to measure how long you brush your teeth?","seconds","minutes","hours","days","minutes","You should brush your teeth for at least two minutes, twice a day.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-is-best-unit-d5217a0b","Math G3: Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of - Set 1 T1","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-2-4 Estimating and measuring time using appropriate units of time, reading and writing time, and solving mathematical problems including time applications.","1. Selecting the suitable units of time (seconds, minutes, hours) to estimate the duration of an event.","What is the best unit of time to measure how long you sleep at night?","seconds","minutes","hours","days","hours","We usually sleep for several hours at night.","","",""
