"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-number-is-greater-a1560a68","Math G3: Understanding the place value of numbers up to four digits - Set 4","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-1-1-1 Understanding the place value of numbers up to four digits and using it to represent numbers, read, write, compare, order, and round them.","1. Identifying the place value of a digit in whole number up to four digits, representing numbers using models, diagrams, number line, and rounding them to the nearest ten, hundred, or thousand.","Which number is greater than 987?","900","980","990","1000","1000","1000 is greater than 987 because it has a larger thousands digit.","","",""
