"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-of-is-an-726d2a67","Math G3: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-1-1 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes, and using them to classify and compare them.","2. Distinguishing shapes with symmetry, identifying axes of symmetry in shapes, drawings, and pictures, and drawing or completing shapes that are symmetric about a given axis.","Which of the following is an example of a shape with symmetry?","A hand","A foot","A butterfly","A cloud","A butterfly","A butterfly is an example of a shape with symmetry, as it has a line of symmetry down the middle of its body.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-of-shapes-has-b7f1eda9","Math G3: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-2 Distinguishing the relations between the four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","1. Describing and classifying two-dimensional geometric shapes (triangle, square, rectangle, circle, parallelogram, trapezoid, pentagon, hexagon), and comparing them based on the number of sides, the number of vertices, and the congruence of sides.","Which of the following shapes has two lines of symmetry?","A circle","A square","A triangle","A rectangle","A square","A square has two lines of symmetry, one that divides it horizontally and one that divides it vertically.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-happens-you-fold-9dc4ea6a","Math G3: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-1-1 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes, and using them to classify and compare them.","2. Distinguishing shapes with symmetry, identifying axes of symmetry in shapes, drawings, and pictures, and drawing or completing shapes that are symmetric about a given axis.","What happens when you fold a shape along its line of symmetry?","The shape gets bigger","The shape gets smaller","The two parts of the shape match up perfectly","The shape disappears","The two parts of the shape match up perfectly","When you fold a shape along its line of symmetry, the two parts of the shape match up perfectly.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-is-an-axis-ba1d5ee8","Math G3: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-1-1 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes, and using them to classify and compare them.","2. Distinguishing shapes with symmetry, identifying axes of symmetry in shapes, drawings, and pictures, and drawing or completing shapes that are symmetric about a given axis.","What is an axis of symmetry?","A line that divides a shape into two equal parts","A line that makes a shape bigger","A line that makes a shape smaller","A line that makes a shape disappear","A line that divides a shape into two equal parts","An axis of symmetry is a line that divides a shape into two equal parts.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-of-is-a-1f6130bd","Math G3: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-1-1 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes, and using them to classify and compare them.","2. Distinguishing shapes with symmetry, identifying axes of symmetry in shapes, drawings, and pictures, and drawing or completing shapes that are symmetric about a given axis.","Which of the following is a property of a shape with symmetry?","It has no lines of symmetry","It has one or more lines of symmetry","It is always a circle","It is always a square","It has one or more lines of symmetry","A shape with symmetry has one or more lines of symmetry, which divide the shape into two equal parts.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-is-line-called-b7a9699c","Math G3: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-1-1 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes, and using them to classify and compare them.","2. Distinguishing shapes with symmetry, identifying axes of symmetry in shapes, drawings, and pictures, and drawing or completing shapes that are symmetric about a given axis.","What is the line called that divides a shape into two equal parts?","A line that makes the shape bigger","A line that makes the shape smaller","A line of symmetry","A line that makes the shape disappear","A line of symmetry","A line of symmetry is a line that divides a shape into two equal parts.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-of-shapes-is-bb3457e4","Math G3: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-1-1 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes, and using them to classify and compare them.","2. Distinguishing shapes with symmetry, identifying axes of symmetry in shapes, drawings, and pictures, and drawing or completing shapes that are symmetric about a given axis.","Which of the following shapes is symmetric about a vertical axis?","A heart","A circle","A square","A triangle with the base on the bottom","A heart","A heart is symmetric about a vertical axis, meaning it looks the same on both sides of the vertical line.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-is-term-a-f386abb6","Math G3: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-1-1 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes, and using them to classify and compare them.","2. Distinguishing shapes with symmetry, identifying axes of symmetry in shapes, drawings, and pictures, and drawing or completing shapes that are symmetric about a given axis.","What is the term for a shape that looks the same when it is flipped or turned?","Symmetry","Asymmetry","Line of symmetry","Axis of symmetry","Symmetry","Symmetry is the term for a shape that looks the same when it is flipped or turned.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-of-shapes-has-42cfc459","Math G3: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-2-2-2 Distinguishing the relations between the four operations, and using them to find the results and verify their correctness.","1. Describing and classifying two-dimensional geometric shapes (triangle, square, rectangle, circle, parallelogram, trapezoid, pentagon, hexagon), and comparing them based on the number of sides, the number of vertices, and the congruence of sides.","Which of the following shapes has one line of symmetry?","A circle","A square","A triangle","A rectangle","A triangle","A triangle can have one line of symmetry, depending on the type of triangle.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-happens-you-draw-845dddd6","Math G3: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 2","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-1-1 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes, and using them to classify and compare them.","2. Distinguishing shapes with symmetry, identifying axes of symmetry in shapes, drawings, and pictures, and drawing or completing shapes that are symmetric about a given axis.","What happens when you draw a shape that is symmetric about a given axis?","The shape will be the same on both sides of the axis","The shape will be different on both sides of the axis","The shape will disappear","The shape will get bigger","The shape will be the same on both sides of the axis","When you draw a shape that is symmetric about a given axis, the shape will be the same on both sides of the axis.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-shape-has-six-7091cab6","Math G3: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 3","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-1-1 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes, and using them to classify and compare them.","3. Describing and classifying three-dimensional geometric shapes (cube, sphere, cone, cylinder, pyramid, and rectangular prism), and comparing them based on the number of faces and shapes, the number of vertices, and the number of edges.","What shape has six square faces and twelve edges?","A sphere","A cube","A cone","A cylinder","A cube","A cube has six square faces and twelve edges, which makes it different from other three-dimensional shapes.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-shape-has-one-5118d987","Math G3: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 3","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-1-1 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes, and using them to classify and compare them.","3. Describing and classifying three-dimensional geometric shapes (cube, sphere, cone, cylinder, pyramid, and rectangular prism), and comparing them based on the number of faces and shapes, the number of vertices, and the number of edges.","What shape has one circular base and gets smaller as it goes up?","A cone","A cylinder","A pyramid","A sphere","A cone","A cone has one circular base and gets smaller as it goes up, which makes it different from other three-dimensional shapes.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-shape-has-no-fe991ea3","Math G3: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 3","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-1-1 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes, and using them to classify and compare them.","3. Describing and classifying three-dimensional geometric shapes (cube, sphere, cone, cylinder, pyramid, and rectangular prism), and comparing them based on the number of faces and shapes, the number of vertices, and the number of edges.","Which shape has no corners or edges?","A sphere","A cone","A cylinder","A pyramid","A sphere","A sphere has no corners or edges, which makes it unique among three-dimensional shapes.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-shape-has-a-fa487a9d","Math G3: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 3","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-1-1 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes, and using them to classify and compare them.","3. Describing and classifying three-dimensional geometric shapes (cube, sphere, cone, cylinder, pyramid, and rectangular prism), and comparing them based on the number of faces and shapes, the number of vertices, and the number of edges.","What shape has a square base and four triangular faces that meet at the top?","A pyramid","A cone","A cylinder","A rectangular prism","A pyramid","A pyramid has a square base and four triangular faces that meet at the top, which makes it different from other three-dimensional shapes.","","",""
"math-g3-3-4-2-1-1-shape-has-two-0ef14cf3","Math G3: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 3","Math","3","Assessment for Grade 3 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","3-4-3-1-1 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes, and using them to classify and compare them.","3. Describing and classifying three-dimensional geometric shapes (cube, sphere, cone, cylinder, pyramid, and rectangular prism), and comparing them based on the number of faces and shapes, the number of vertices, and the number of edges.","Which shape has two parallel and circular bases connected by a curved surface?","A cone","A cylinder","A sphere","A pyramid","A cylinder","A cylinder has two parallel and circular bases connected by a curved surface, which makes it different from other three-dimensional shapes.","","",""
