"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-product-of-61d7d108","Math G6: Adding and subtracting whole numbers up - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-1 Adding and subtracting whole numbers up to seven digits, multiplying numbers up to three digits, dividing numbers of up to four digits by numbers of up to two digits, and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","1. Adding and subtracting numbers up to seven digits, with and without regrouping.","What is the product of 219 and 9?","1,971","1,774","2,168","19,710","1,971","Multiply 219 by 9: 219 x 9 = 1,971.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-result-of-6e217550","Math G6: Adding and subtracting whole numbers up - Set 2","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-1-2 Distinguishing Proper fractions, mixed numbers, and improper fractions, representing, reading, writing, comparing, ordering, and rounding them.","2. Finding equivalent fractions, converting them to their simplest form, and rounding them to the nearest whole, half, or one.","What is 6789 ÷ 19, rounded to the nearest whole number?","357","322","392","3,570","357","6,789 ÷ 19 = 357.32, which rounds to 357.","","",""
