"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-type-of-line-b6fab07c","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","3. Distinguishing intersecting, parallel, and perpendicular lines, and identifying them on geometric figures.","Which type of line is perpendicular to another line?","A line that is the same length as another line","A line that is the same width as another line","A line that is always the same distance apart from another line","A line that forms a 90-degree angle with another line","A line that forms a 90-degree angle with another line","A line that forms a 90-degree angle with another line is perpendicular to that line.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-type-of-line-9853d48a","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","1. Distinguishing points, lines, rays, and line segments, and identifying them on geometric figures.","Which type of line touches another line at two points?","A line that never touches another line","A line that touches another line at two points","A line that touches another line at one point","A line that is always the same distance apart from another line","A line that touches another line at two points","A transversal line touches another line at two points.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-type-of-angle-aa4c0e30","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","2. Distinguishing angles (right, acute, obtuse, and straight), and estimating and finding their measures.","What type of angle is formed when two perpendicular lines intersect?","A right angle","An acute angle","An obtuse angle","A straight angle","A right angle","When two perpendicular lines intersect, they form a right angle, which measures exactly 90 degrees.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-type-of-angle-01aca829","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","2. Distinguishing angles (right, acute, obtuse, and straight), and estimating and finding their measures.","Which type of angle is exactly 90 degrees?","A right angle","An acute angle","An obtuse angle","A straight angle","A right angle","A right angle is exactly 90 degrees.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-type-of-line-08014891","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","3. Distinguishing intersecting, parallel, and perpendicular lines, and identifying them on geometric figures.","Which type of line never intersects with another line?","A line that touches another line at two points","A line that touches another line at one point","A line that is always the same distance apart from another line","A line that never touches another line","A line that never touches another line","A parallel line never intersects with another line.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-a-ray-44d8b1e2","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","1. Distinguishing points, lines, rays, and line segments, and identifying them on geometric figures.","What is a ray in geometry?","A set of points that extend infinitely in two directions","A set of points that extend infinitely in one direction","A location in space with no size or dimension","A set of points that are connected by a curve","A set of points that extend infinitely in one direction","A ray is a set of points that extend infinitely in one direction, it has one end point.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-of-is-not-08d945a3","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","1. Distinguishing points, lines, rays, and line segments, and identifying them on geometric figures.","Which of the following is NOT an example of a geometric concept?","A point","A line","A ray","A color","A color","A color is not a geometric concept, it is a property of an object.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-of-is-an-c5850603","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","1. Distinguishing points, lines, rays, and line segments, and identifying them on geometric figures.","Which of the following is an example of a line segment?","A line that extends from one wall of a room to the other","A line that extends from the earth to the sun","A line that extends from a point to another point on a circle","A line that extends infinitely in two directions","A line that extends from one wall of a room to the other","A line segment is a part of a line that is bounded by two end points, a line that extends from one wall of a room to the other is an example of a line segment.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-relationship-a-dc52e209","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","1. Distinguishing points, lines, rays, and line segments, and identifying them on geometric figures.","What is the relationship between a line and a ray?","A line is a set of rays","A ray is a set of lines","A line extends infinitely in two directions, while a ray extends infinitely in one direction","A ray extends infinitely in two directions, while a line extends infinitely in one direction","A line extends infinitely in two directions, while a ray extends infinitely in one direction","A line extends infinitely in two directions, while a ray extends infinitely in one direction.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-a-line-75cfd0a8","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","1. Distinguishing points, lines, rays, and line segments, and identifying them on geometric figures.","What is a line segment in geometry?","A set of points that extend infinitely in two directions","A set of points that extend infinitely in one direction","A set of points that are connected by a curve","A part of a line that is bounded by two end points","A part of a line that is bounded by two end points","A line segment is a part of a line that is bounded by two end points, it has a fixed length.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-a-line-ed359209","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","1. Distinguishing points, lines, rays, and line segments, and identifying them on geometric figures.","What is a line in geometry?","A set of points that are connected by a curve","A set of points that extend infinitely in one direction","A set of points that extend infinitely in two directions","A location in space with no size or dimension","A set of points that extend infinitely in two directions","A line is a set of points that extend infinitely in two directions, it has no end points.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-a-point-63cb7c79","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","1. Distinguishing points, lines, rays, and line segments, and identifying them on geometric figures.","What is a point in geometry?","A location in space with no size or dimension","A set of points that extend infinitely in two directions","A set of points that extend infinitely in one direction","A set of points that are connected by a curve","A location in space with no size or dimension","A point is a location in space with no size or dimension, it has no length, width, or height.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-difference-a-24eee976","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","1. Distinguishing points, lines, rays, and line segments, and identifying them on geometric figures.","What is the difference between a line and a line segment?","A line has a fixed length, while a line segment does not","A line has two end points, while a line segment does not","A line extends infinitely in two directions, while a line segment has two end points","A line segment extends infinitely in two directions, while a line has two end points","A line extends infinitely in two directions, while a line segment has two end points","A line extends infinitely in two directions, while a line segment has two end points and a fixed length.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-of-is-an-537ce972","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","1. Distinguishing points, lines, rays, and line segments, and identifying them on geometric figures.","Which of the following is an example of a point?","The center of a circle","The edge of a circle","The area inside a circle","The circumference of a circle","The center of a circle","A point is a location in space with no size or dimension, the center of a circle is an example of a point.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-of-is-an-987b8913","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","1. Distinguishing points, lines, rays, and line segments, and identifying them on geometric figures.","Which of the following is an example of a ray?","A line that extends from the earth to the sun","A line that extends from one wall of a room to the other","A line that extends infinitely in two directions","A line that extends from a point to another point on a circle","A line that extends from the earth to the sun","A ray is a set of points that extend infinitely in one direction, a line that extends from the earth to the sun is an example of a ray.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-of-is-an-24263e2d","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts - Set 2","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-2 Distinguishing formulas for the perimeter and area of two-dimensional shapes, using them to find perimeter and area, and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing formulas for the areas of the rectangle, square, parallelogram, and triangle, and using them to calculate their areas and the areas of composite shapes formed from them.","Which of the following is an example of a right angle in real life?","The angle formed by a clock's hands at 3 o'clock","The angle formed by a clock's hands at 12 o'clock","The angle formed by the corner of a piece of paper","The angle formed by the intersection of two roads that meet at a 45-degree angle","The angle formed by the corner of a piece of paper","The corner of a piece of paper forms a right angle, which is 90 degrees.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-term-amount-a0c93874","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts - Set 2","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","1. Distinguishing points, lines, rays, and line segments, and identifying them on geometric figures.","What is the term for the amount of rotation between two lines or planes?","Angle measure","Line segment","Plane","Angle","Angle","An angle is the term for the amount of rotation between two lines or planes.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-of-angles-is-f37ce956","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts - Set 2","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","2. Distinguishing angles (right, acute, obtuse, and straight), and estimating and finding their measures.","Which of the following angles is less than 90 degrees?","Right angle","Obtuse angle","Straight angle","Acute angle","Acute angle","An acute angle is less than 90 degrees.","","",""
