"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-type-of-angle-e9884d99","Math G6: Distinguishing basic geometric concepts - Set 2","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","2. Distinguishing angles (right, acute, obtuse, and straight), and estimating and finding their measures.","What type of angle is formed when two lines intersect to create a 30-degree angle?","Right angle","Obtuse angle","Straight angle","Acute angle","Acute angle","An acute angle is formed when two lines intersect to create an angle less than 90 degrees, such as 30 degrees.","","",""
