"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-square-has-9bc63aa6","Math G6: Distinguishing formulas for the perimeter and - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-2 Distinguishing formulas for the perimeter and area of two-dimensional shapes, using them to find perimeter and area, and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","1. Distinguishing formulas for the perimeters of the rectangle, square, and circle, and using them to find the perimeter.","A square has a side length of 6 cm. What is its area?","30 cm^2","36 cm^2","40 cm^2","50 cm^2","36 cm^2","The area of the square is found by multiplying the side length by itself: 6 cm x 6 cm = 36 cm^2.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-formula-area-8a326005","Math G6: Distinguishing formulas for the perimeter and - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-2 Distinguishing formulas for the perimeter and area of two-dimensional shapes, using them to find perimeter and area, and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing formulas for the areas of the rectangle, square, parallelogram, and triangle, and using them to calculate their areas and the areas of composite shapes formed from them.","What is the formula for the area of a composite shape?","Area = Sum of individual shapes","Area = Difference of individual shapes","Area = Product of individual shapes","Area = Quotient of individual shapes","Area = Sum of individual shapes","The area of a composite shape is found by adding the areas of the individual shapes.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-formula-area-dff8b1de","Math G6: Distinguishing formulas for the perimeter and - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-2 Distinguishing formulas for the perimeter and area of two-dimensional shapes, using them to find perimeter and area, and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing formulas for the areas of the rectangle, square, parallelogram, and triangle, and using them to calculate their areas and the areas of composite shapes formed from them.","What is the formula for the area of a triangle?","Area = Base x Height","Area = 1/2 x Base x Height","Area = Base + Height","Area = Base / Height","Area = 1/2 x Base x Height","The area of a triangle is found by multiplying the base by the height and then dividing by 2.","","",""
