"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-85-multiplied-29286b8b","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","3. Applying the distributive property to multiply a two-digit number by a one-digit number mentally.","What is 85 multiplied by 8?","680","650","660","670","680","We can use the distributive property to multiply 85 by 8. First, we multiply 80 by 8 to get 640. Then, we multiply 5 by 8 to get 40. Finally, we add 640 and 40 to get 680.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-62-multiplied-985a1169","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","3. Applying the distributive property to multiply a two-digit number by a one-digit number mentally.","What is 62 multiplied by 7?","434","420","430","440","434","We can use the distributive property to multiply 62 by 7. First, we multiply 60 by 7 to get 420. Then, we multiply 2 by 7 to get 14. Finally, we add 420 and 14 to get 434.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-24-multiplied-9694f61f","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","3. Applying the distributive property to multiply a two-digit number by a one-digit number mentally.","What is 24 multiplied by 5?","120","130","140","150","120","To find the product of 24 and 5, we can use the distributive property by multiplying 24 by 5 and getting 120.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-46-multiplied-298c1380","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","3. Applying the distributive property to multiply a two-digit number by a one-digit number mentally.","What is 46 multiplied by 3?","138","140","150","160","138","We can use the distributive property to multiply 46 by 3. First, we multiply 40 by 3 to get 120. Then, we multiply 6 by 3 to get 18. Finally, we add 120 and 18 to get 138.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-93-multiplied-c4a521d4","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","3. Applying the distributive property to multiply a two-digit number by a one-digit number mentally.","What is 93 multiplied by 2?","186","190","200","210","186","We can use the distributive property to multiply 93 by 2. First, we multiply 90 by 2 to get 180. Then, we multiply 3 by 2 to get 6. Finally, we add 180 and 6 to get 186.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-95-multiplied-1b116ecd","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","3. Applying the distributive property to multiply a two-digit number by a one-digit number mentally.","What is 95 multiplied by 3?","285","280","290","300","285","We can use the distributive property to multiply 95 by 3. First, we multiply 90 by 3 to get 270. Then, we multiply 5 by 3 to get 15. Finally, we add 270 and 15 to get 285.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-49-multiplied-c2fecfc3","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","3. Applying the distributive property to multiply a two-digit number by a one-digit number mentally.","What is 49 multiplied by 9?","441","420","430","440","441","We can use the distributive property to multiply 49 by 9. First, we multiply 40 by 9 to get 360. Then, we multiply 9 by 9 to get 81. Finally, we add 360 and 81 to get 441.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-67-multiplied-f0d127a6","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","3. Applying the distributive property to multiply a two-digit number by a one-digit number mentally.","What is 67 multiplied by 6?","402","400","410","420","402","We can use the distributive property to multiply 67 by 6. First, we multiply 60 by 6 to get 360. Then, we multiply 7 by 6 to get 42. Finally, we add 360 and 42 to get 402.","","",""
