"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-75-multiplied-03c3b1ff","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","3. Applying the distributive property to multiply a two-digit number by a one-digit number mentally.","What is 75 multiplied by 4?","280","290","300","310","300","We can use the distributive property to multiply 75 by 4. First, we multiply 70 by 4 to get 280. Then, we multiply 5 by 4 to get 20. Finally, we add 280 and 20 to get 300.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-approximate-sum-c5b25fed","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 5","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","1 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, mixed numbers, and decimal Proper by using rounding.","What is the approximate sum of 2.5 and 1.8?","3.5","4","4.5","5","4","The sum is 2.5 + 1.8 = 4.3. For an approximate answer, 4.3 is closest to 4 among the given options.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-group-of-0bd8a0b1","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 5","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","1 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, mixed numbers, and decimal Proper by using rounding.","A group of friends want to share some candy equally. If they have 48 pieces of candy and there are 8 friends, how many pieces of candy will each friend get?","Each friend will get 6 pieces of candy","5 pieces","7 pieces","48 pieces","Each friend will get 6 pieces of candy","48 ÷ 8 = 6 pieces of candy.","/image-source/math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-group-of-0bd8a0b1.png","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-approximate-difference-fd7ca146","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 5","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","1 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, mixed numbers, and decimal Proper by using rounding.","What is the approximate difference between 945 and 279?","600","650","700","750","600","Estimate by rounding 945 to 900 and 279 to 300. Then 900 - 300 = 600, so the approximate difference is 600.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-water-tank-6d6cb7bc","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 5","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","3. Applying the distributive property to multiply a two-digit number by a one-digit number mentally.","A water tank can hold 2400 liters of water. If 1200 liters of water are already in the tank, what fraction of the tank is filled?","One quarter","One half","Three quarters","Two thirds","One half","Since 1200 liters is half of 2400 liters, the tank is half filled.","/image-source/math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-water-tank-6d6cb7bc.png","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-approximate-product-7f995dcc","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 5","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","1 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, mixed numbers, and decimal Proper by using rounding.","What is the approximate product of 4.5 and 6.2?","20","25","27","30","30","Estimate by rounding 4.5 to 5 and 6.2 to 6. Then 5 x 6 = 30, so the approximate product is 30.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-approximate-quotient-c8559dd3","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 5","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","1 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, mixed numbers, and decimal Proper by using rounding.","What is the approximate quotient of 945 and 15?","50","60","70","80","60","Estimate 945 divided by 15 as about 900 divided by 15. Since 900 / 15 = 60, the approximate quotient is 60.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-bakery-sells-92e1d9d6","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 5","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","1 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, mixed numbers, and decimal Proper by using rounding.","A bakery sells 240 loaves of bread per day. If they pack 12 loaves of bread in a box, how many boxes do they sell per day?","10 boxes","15 boxes","20 boxes","25 boxes","20 boxes","To find the number of boxes, divide the total number of loaves by the number of loaves per box: 240 / 12 = 20.","/image-source/math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-bakery-sells-92e1d9d6.png","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-approximate-sum-6f2262c0","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 5","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","1 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, mixed numbers, and decimal Proper by using rounding.","What is the approximate sum of 457 and 279?","600","700","750","800","700","The sum of 457 and 279 is approximately 736, which is closest to 700.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-bookshelf-has-080b143b","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 5","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","1 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, mixed numbers, and decimal Proper by using rounding.","A bookshelf has 5 shelves, and each shelf can hold 8 books. If the bookshelf is currently empty, how many books can be placed on it in total?","40 books","30 books","45 books","50 books","40 books","Multiply shelves by books per shelf: 5 x 8 = 40 books.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-pencil-is-df787424","Math G6: Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations - Set 5","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-1-2-7 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, and decimal fractions, and using mental calculation strategies to find results, and verifying the plausibility and accuracy of the results.","1 Estimating the results of the four arithmetic operations on whole numbers, Proper fractions, mixed numbers, and decimal Proper by using rounding.","A pencil is 15 cm long. If it is divided into 5 parts, how long is each part?","1 cm","2 cm","3 cm","5 cm","3 cm","15 ÷ 5 = 3.","/image-source/math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-pencil-is-df787424.png","",""
