"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-of-is-an-8ed76305","Math G6: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-2 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes and using them to identify and classify the shapes.","3. Distinguishing quadrilaterals (parallelogram, rectangle, rhombus, square, and trapezoid), identifying and naming their elements, and classifying them according to the properties of their sides and angles.","Which of the following is an example of an irregular polygon?","A square with all sides equal","A rectangle with equal sides","A triangle with two sides equal","A rectangle with sides of different lengths","A rectangle with sides of different lengths","An irregular polygon has sides and angles that are not all equal, like a rectangle with sides of different lengths.","","",""
