"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-a-polygon-2fe5b5dc","Math G6: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-2 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes and using them to identify and classify the shapes.","1. Distinguishing polygons, classifying them into regular and irregular polygons, and naming them.","What is a polygon with all sides and angles equal called?","Irregular Polygon","Regular Polygon","Triangle","Quadrilateral","Regular Polygon","A regular polygon has all sides and angles equal, whereas an irregular polygon does not.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-type-of-triangle-01da5204","Math G6: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 2","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-1 Distinguishing basic geometric concepts, identifying types of angles, relationships between lines, and relationships between angles.","2. Distinguishing angles (right, acute, obtuse, and straight), and estimating and finding their measures.","Which type of triangle has one angle greater than 90 degrees?","Right Triangle","Acute Triangle","Obtuse Triangle","Isosceles Triangle","Obtuse Triangle","An obtuse triangle has one angle greater than 90 degrees.","","",""
