"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-name-of-fd98717a","Math G6: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 2","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-2 Distinguishing formulas for the perimeter and area of two-dimensional shapes, using them to find perimeter and area, and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","1. Distinguishing formulas for the perimeters of the rectangle, square, and circle, and using them to find the perimeter.","What is the name of the shape that is round and has no corners?","Square","Circle","Triangle","Rectangle","Circle","A circle is a shape that is round and has no corners.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-name-of-a4ce0b4c","Math G6: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 2","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-2 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes and using them to identify and classify the shapes.","4. Distinguishing prisms (triangular, quadrilateral) and cubes, identifying their vertices, edges, faces, and bases, and drawing their nets.","What is the name of the point where two sides of a triangle meet?","Vertex","Edge","Face","Angle","Vertex","A vertex is the point where two sides of a triangle meet.","","",""
