"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-name-of-e60deb76","Math G6: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-2 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes and using them to identify and classify the shapes.","3. Distinguishing quadrilaterals (parallelogram, rectangle, rhombus, square, and trapezoid), identifying and naming their elements, and classifying them according to the properties of their sides and angles.","What is the name of a quadrilateral with two sets of opposite sides that are parallel to each other?","Trapezoid","Rhombus","Parallelogram","Rectangle","Parallelogram","A parallelogram is a quadrilateral with two sets of opposite sides that are parallel to each other.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-type-of-quadrilateral-9ca0d60e","Math G6: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-2 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes and using them to identify and classify the shapes.","3. Distinguishing quadrilaterals (parallelogram, rectangle, rhombus, square, and trapezoid), identifying and naming their elements, and classifying them according to the properties of their sides and angles.","Which type of quadrilateral has one pair of parallel sides?","Parallelogram","Trapezoid","Rectangle","Rhombus","Trapezoid","A trapezoid is a quadrilateral with one pair of parallel sides, which means only two sides are parallel to each other.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-name-of-255a4e44","Math G6: Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-di - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-1-2 Understanding the properties of two-dimensional and three-dimensional geometric shapes and using them to identify and classify the shapes.","3. Distinguishing quadrilaterals (parallelogram, rectangle, rhombus, square, and trapezoid), identifying and naming their elements, and classifying them according to the properties of their sides and angles.","What is the name of a quadrilateral with four right angles, but not necessarily four sides of equal length?","Square","Rhombus","Rectangle","Trapezoid","Rectangle","A rectangle is a quadrilateral with four right angles, but its sides are not necessarily all of equal length.","","",""
