"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-rectangular-prism-0a2ee0a8","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","A rectangular prism has a length of 7 cm, a width of 3 cm, and a height of 2 cm. What is its surface area?","The surface area is 60 square centimeters.","The surface area is 72 square centimeters.","82 square centimeters.","The surface area is 90 square centimeters.","82 square centimeters.","To find the surface area of a rectangular prism, we add the areas of all its faces. SA = 2(lw + lh + wh) = 2(7×3 + 7×2 + 3×2) = 2(21 + 14 + 6) = 2(41) = 82 square centimeters.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-rectangular-prism-b35d99cb","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","A rectangular prism has a length of 5 cm, a width of 2 cm, and a height of 3 cm. What is its volume?","The volume is 30 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 27 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 33 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 300 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 30 cubic centimeters.","Volume of a rectangular prism is length x width x height: 5 x 2 x 3 = 30 cubic centimeters.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-rectangular-prism-86da979a","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","A rectangular prism has a length of 8 cm, a width of 4 cm, and a height of 2 cm. What is its surface area?","The surface area is 80 square centimeters.","The surface area is 96 square centimeters.","The surface area is 112 square centimeters.","The surface area is 128 square centimeters.","The surface area is 112 square centimeters.","To find the surface area of a rectangular prism, we add the areas of all its faces. In this case, the surface area is 2 * (8 cm * 4 cm) + 2 * (8 cm * 2 cm) + 2 * (4 cm * 2 cm) = 112 square centimeters.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-rectangular-prism-b8b4afa2","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","A rectangular prism has a length of 8 cm, a width of 4 cm, and a height of 3 cm. What is its surface area?","The surface area is 80 square centimeters.","The surface area is 96 square centimeters.","136 square centimeters.","The surface area is 128 square centimeters.","136 square centimeters.","To find the surface area of a rectangular prism, we add the areas of all its faces. SA = 2(lw + lh + wh) = 2(8×4 + 8×3 + 4×3) = 2(32 + 24 + 12) = 2(68) = 136 square centimeters.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-rectangular-prism-6746af7a","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","A rectangular prism has a length of 5 cm, a width of 3 cm, and a height of 2 cm. What is its volume?","The volume is 30 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 27 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 33 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 300 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 30 cubic centimeters.","Volume of a rectangular prism is length x width x height: 5 x 3 x 2 = 30 cubic centimeters.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-rectangular-prism-3b624b4b","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","A rectangular prism has a length of 6 cm, a width of 3 cm, and a height of 2 cm. What is its volume?","The volume is 36 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 33 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 39 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 360 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 36 cubic centimeters.","Volume of a rectangular prism is length x width x height: 6 x 3 x 2 = 36 cubic centimeters.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-rectangular-prism-7f6e09b1","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","A rectangular prism has a length of 9 cm, a width of 5 cm, and a height of 2 cm. What is its surface area?","The surface area is 140 square centimeters.","The surface area is 144 square centimeters.","The surface area is 160 square centimeters.","146 square centimeters.","146 square centimeters.","To find the surface area of a rectangular prism, we add the areas of all its faces. SA = 2(lw + lh + wh) = 2(9×5 + 9×2 + 5×2) = 2(45 + 18 + 10) = 2(73) = 146 square centimeters.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-rectangular-prism-f81be328","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","A rectangular prism has a length of 9 cm, a width of 5 cm, and a height of 3 cm. What is its surface area?","The surface area is 160 square centimeters.","The surface area is 180 square centimeters.","The surface area is 200 square centimeters.","174 square centimeters.","174 square centimeters.","To find the surface area of a rectangular prism, we add the areas of all its faces. SA = 2(lw + lh + wh) = 2(9×5 + 9×3 + 5×3) = 2(45 + 27 + 15) = 2(87) = 174 square centimeters.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-container-can-500bbd56","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and their units - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","A container can hold 500 milliliters of liquid. What is the volume of the container in cubic centimeters?","500 cubic centimeters","50 cubic centimeters","5 cubic centimeters","0.5 cubic centimeters","500 cubic centimeters","Since 1 milliliter is equal to 1 cubic centimeter, the volume of the container is 500 cubic centimeters.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-rectangular-prism-d324dd1a","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and their units - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","A rectangular prism has a length of 8 cm, a width of 4 cm, and a height of 2 cm. What is the volume of the prism in cubic centimeters?","The volume is 64 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 58 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 70 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 640 cubic centimeters.","The volume is 64 cubic centimeters.","Volume of a rectangular prism is length x width x height: 8 x 4 x 2 = 64 cubic centimeters.","","",""
