"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-volume-of-9abcb838","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and their units - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","What is the volume of a cube with a side length of 5 cm?","100 cubic centimeters","125 cubic centimeters","25 cubic centimeters","50 cubic centimeters","125 cubic centimeters","To find the volume of a cube, cube the side length, so 5 * 5 * 5 = 125 cubic centimeters.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-bucket-can-92c0b8f5","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and their units - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","A bucket can hold 20 liters of water. What is the volume of the bucket in cubic meters?","0.02 cubic meters","0.2 cubic meters","2 cubic meters","20 cubic meters","0.02 cubic meters","Since 1 cubic meter is equal to 1000 liters, the volume of the bucket is 20 / 1000 = 0.02 cubic meters.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-volume-of-648abd29","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and their units - Set 1","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","What is the volume of a rectangular prism with a length of 5 m, a width of 2 m, and a height of 3 m?","10 cubic meters","30 cubic meters","15 cubic meters","20 cubic meters","30 cubic meters","To find the volume of a rectangular prism, multiply the length, width, and height, so 5 * 2 * 3 = 30 cubic meters.","","",""
