"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-formula-to-e039ad7d","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and their units - Set 2","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","What is the formula to calculate the volume of a right rectangular prism?","Length times width","Length times width times height","Length plus width plus height","Length minus width minus height","Length times width times height","The formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism is length times width times height, because you need to multiply the area of the base by the height to get the volume.","","",""
