"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-gift-box-29765689","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and their units - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","A gift box is 12 inches long, 10 inches wide, and 6 inches tall. What is the surface area of the gift box?","352 square inches","384 square inches","504 square inches","448 square inches","504 square inches","Surface area = 2lw + 2lh + 2wh = 2(12*10) + 2(12*6) + 2(10*6) = 240 + 144 + 120 = 504 square inches.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-bookshelf-is-87419802","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and their units - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","A bookshelf is 5 feet long, 3 feet wide, and 2 feet tall. What is the surface area of the bookshelf?","62 square feet","56 square feet","64 square feet","70 square feet","62 square feet","To find the surface area, we use the formula 2lw + 2lh + 2wh, where l = 5, w = 3, and h = 2. So, the surface area is 2(5*3) + 2(5*2) + 2(3*2) = 30 + 20 + 12 = 62 square feet.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-surface-area-14a1460d","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and their units - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","What is the surface area of a cube with a side length of 6 inches?","216 square inches","36 square inches","72 square inches","216 square inches is the volume","216 square inches","Since a cube has 6 equal faces, we can find the surface area by calculating 6 times the area of one face. The area of one face is 6 * 6 = 36 square inches. So, the surface area is 6 * 36 = 216 square inches.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-surface-area-d964e46f","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and their units - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","What is the surface area of a rectangular prism with a length of 15 cm, a width of 8 cm, and a height of 5 cm?","242 square centimeters","258 square centimeters","470 square centimeters","298 square centimeters","470 square centimeters","Surface area = 2lw + 2lh + 2wh = 2(15*8) + 2(15*5) + 2(8*5) = 240 + 150 + 80 = 470 square centimeters.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-is-formula-surface-ba38e430","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and their units - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","What is the formula for the surface area of a right rectangular prism?","Length times width times height","2 times length plus 2 times width plus 2 times height","Length plus width plus height","2 times length times width times height","2 times length plus 2 times width plus 2 times height","The surface area of a right rectangular prism is calculated by finding the area of each face and adding them together, which is equivalent to 2 times length plus 2 times width plus 2 times height.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-rectangular-prism-515b7fc8","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and their units - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","A rectangular prism has a length of 8 cm, a width of 5 cm, and a height of 3 cm. What is the surface area of the prism?","134 square centimeters","108 square centimeters","118 square centimeters","158 square centimeters","158 square centimeters","Surface area = 2lw + 2lh + 2wh = 2(8*5) + 2(8*3) + 2(5*3) = 80 + 48 + 30 = 158 square centimeters.","","",""
"math-g6-6-4-2-1-1-a-box-is-35687abf","Math G6: Understanding volume and surface area and their units - Set 3","Math","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-4-3-3-3 Understanding volume and surface area and their units, distinguishing the formulas for a right rectangular prism, and applying them to find volume and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","2. Distinguishing the formula for the volume of a right rectangular prism and using it to calculate its volume.","A box is 10 inches long, 8 inches wide, and 4 inches tall. What is the surface area of the box?","144 square inches","192 square inches","304 square inches","208 square inches","304 square inches","Surface area = 2lw + 2lh + 2wh = 2(10*8) + 2(10*4) + 2(8*4) = 160 + 80 + 64 = 304 square inches.","","",""
