"math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-is-value-of-0550e1d1","Math G9: Performing the four operations on integers - Set 1 T1","Math","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-4-2-2-1 Writing algebraic expressions with rational coefficients, finding their values, performing arithmetic operations on them, and Distinguishing basic identities.","3. Distinguishing the basic identities: the square of a sum of two terms, the square of a difference of two terms, and the product of the sum and difference of two terms, and using them.","What is the value of 8 / 2?","4","The quotient of 8 and 2","The sum of 8 and 2","The difference of 8 and 2","4","Division is repeated subtraction.","","",""
"math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-is-value-of-69e07cf0","Math G9: Performing the four operations on integers - Set 1 T1","Math","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-4-1-1-1 Understanding integers and rational numbers, reading, writing, representing, comparing, and ordering them.","3. Finding the absolute value of an integer  number and representing it on the number line.","What is the value of 2 + (-6)?","-4","4","-8","8","-4","2 + (-6) = 2 - 6 = -4.","","",""
"math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-is-value-of-bc494279","Math G9: Performing the four operations on integers - Set 1 T1","Math","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-4-2-2-1 Writing algebraic expressions with rational coefficients, finding their values, performing arithmetic operations on them, and Distinguishing basic identities.","3. Distinguishing the basic identities: the square of a sum of two terms, the square of a difference of two terms, and the product of the sum and difference of two terms, and using them.","What is the value of 4 * 9?","36","The product of 4 and 9","The sum of 4 and 9","The difference of 4 and 9","36","Multiplication is repeated addition.","","",""
"math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-is-value-of-189ac3aa","Math G9: Performing the four operations on integers - Set 1 T1","Math","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-4-1-1-1 Understanding integers and rational numbers, reading, writing, representing, comparing, and ordering them.","3. Finding the absolute value of an integer  number and representing it on the number line.","What is the value of 6 + 2?","8","6","10","12","8","6 + 2 = 8.","","",""
"math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-is-value-of-c63323c1","Math G9: Performing the four operations on integers - Set 1 T1","Math","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-4-2-2-1 Writing algebraic expressions with rational coefficients, finding their values, performing arithmetic operations on them, and Distinguishing basic identities.","3. Distinguishing the basic identities: the square of a sum of two terms, the square of a difference of two terms, and the product of the sum and difference of two terms, and using them.","What is the value of 9 * (-2)?","-18","The product of 9 and -2","The sum of 9 and -2","The difference of 9 and -2","-18","When multiplying a positive number by a negative number, we get a negative product.","","",""
"math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-is-value-of-4cc92b21","Math G9: Performing the four operations on integers - Set 1 T1","Math","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-4-2-2-1 Writing algebraic expressions with rational coefficients, finding their values, performing arithmetic operations on them, and Distinguishing basic identities.","3. Distinguishing the basic identities: the square of a sum of two terms, the square of a difference of two terms, and the product of the sum and difference of two terms, and using them.","What is the value of 3 - 1?","2","The difference of 3 and 1","The sum of 3 and 1","The product of 3 and 1","2","Subtraction is the inverse operation of addition.","","",""
"math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-is-value-of-e4bacacd","Math G9: Performing the four operations on integers - Set 1 T1","Math","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-4-2-2-1 Writing algebraic expressions with rational coefficients, finding their values, performing arithmetic operations on them, and Distinguishing basic identities.","3. Distinguishing the basic identities: the square of a sum of two terms, the square of a difference of two terms, and the product of the sum and difference of two terms, and using them.","What is the value of 6 / 3?","2","The quotient of 6 and 3","The sum of 6 and 3","The difference of 6 and 3","2","Division is repeated subtraction.","","",""
"math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-is-value-of-57dedb72","Math G9: Performing the four operations on integers - Set 1 T1","Math","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-4-1-1-1 Understanding integers and rational numbers, reading, writing, representing, comparing, and ordering them.","3. Finding the absolute value of an integer  number and representing it on the number line.","What is the value of 5 + (-3)?","2","The sum of 5 and -3","The difference of 5 and 3","The product of 5 and -3","2","When adding a positive and a negative number, we subtract the absolute value of the negative number from the positive number.","","",""
