"math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-a-water-tank-6cde6d4c","Math G9: Performing the four operations on integers - Set 2","Math","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-4-1-2-2 Performing the four operations on integers, rational numbers, and square roots, and using them to simplify the numerical expressions and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","4. Simplifying numerical expressions involving square roots using operations on square roots and rationalizing the denominator.","A water tank can hold 1200 liters of water. If 300 liters of water are already in the tank, what percentage of the tank is filled?","25% of the tank is filled.","30%","20%","300%","25% of the tank is filled.","300 ÷ 1200 × 100 = 25%, so the tank is 25% full.","/image-source/math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-a-water-tank-6cde6d4c.png","",""
"math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-solve-equation-4x-6164509b","Math G9: Performing the four operations on integers - Set 2","Math","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-4-2-2-3 Writing linear and quadratic equations, solving them algebraically and graphically, and estimating their solutions from graph representations.","1. Writing and solving a system of two linear equations with two variables, both algebraically (by substitution or elimination) and graphically.","Solve the equation: 4x = 28","x = 7","x = 7.0","x = 6","x = 6.0","x = 7","Divide both sides of the equation by 4 to solve for x.","","",""
