"math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-a-car-travels-9cc3704d","Math G9: Performing the four operations on integers - Set 2","Math","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-4-1-2-2 Performing the four operations on integers, rational numbers, and square roots, and using them to simplify the numerical expressions and solving mathematical problems including real-life applications.","4. Simplifying numerical expressions involving square roots using operations on square roots and rationalizing the denominator.","A car travels 250 miles in 5 hours. How many miles does it travel per hour?","50 miles per hour","40 miles per hour","60 miles per hour","250 miles per hour","50 miles per hour","250 ÷ 5 = 50 miles per hour.","/image-source/math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-a-car-travels-9cc3704d.png","",""
