"math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-arrange-integers-in-4bfd9de8","Math G9: Understanding integers and rational numbers - Set 2","Math","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-4-1-1-1 Understanding integers and rational numbers, reading, writing, representing, comparing, and ordering them.","2. Comparing integers numbers and ordering them in ascending and descending order.","Arrange the following integers in ascending order: 5, -2, 0, 8","-2, 0, 5, 8","5, -2, 0, 8","8, 5, 0, -2","0, -2, 5, 8","-2, 0, 5, 8","The correct order is -2, 0, 5, 8.","/image-source/math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-arrange-integers-in-4bfd9de8.png","",""
"math-g9-9-4-2-1-1-is-absolute-value-1d4573eb","Math G9: Understanding integers and rational numbers - Set 3","Math","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Math","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-4-1-1-1 Understanding integers and rational numbers, reading, writing, representing, comparing, and ordering them.","3. Finding the absolute value of an integer  number and representing it on the number line.","What is the absolute value of -7?","The value is negative 7","The value is 7","The value is -7","The value is zero","The value is 7","The absolute value of a number is its distance from zero on the number line, which is always positive.","","",""
