"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-effect-of-c5c6228c","Science G6: Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying - Set 4","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-3 Describing the factors and processes that affected the Earth›s surface which changed some of its","3. Explaining the factors of erosion, weathering, and sedimentation and their causes, and predicting the patterns of their action and their effects on earth.","What is the effect of climate change on sea levels?","Climate change has no effect on sea levels.","Climate change causes sea levels to decrease.","Climate change causes sea levels to increase, leading to coastal erosion and flooding.","Climate change has no effect on the Earth's rotation speed.","Climate change causes sea levels to increase, leading to coastal erosion and flooding.","Climate change causes sea levels to increase, leading to coastal erosion and flooding.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-benefit-of-37c076cc","Science G6: Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying - Set 4","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-1Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying their components, characteristics, changes, its effects on the environment and their benefits to humans.","2. Explaining the movement of air masses and air currents and describing their effects on Earth’s weather.","What is the benefit of the Troposphere to humans?","The Troposphere has no benefit to humans.","The Troposphere protects us from the sun's harmful rays.","The Troposphere helps to regulate the Earth's temperature.","The Troposphere is the layer of the atmosphere where weather occurs.","The Troposphere is the layer of the atmosphere where weather occurs.","The Troposphere is the layer of the atmosphere where weather occurs, including clouds, rain, and wind.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-layer-2552eef6","Science G6: Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying - Set 4","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","1. Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and comparing them in terms of similarities and differences, and identifying some environmental problems resulting from changes in atmospheric layers.","What is the main layer of the atmosphere that protects us from the sun's harmful rays?","The Troposphere is the layer that protects us from the sun's harmful rays.","The Stratosphere is the layer that protects us from the sun's harmful rays.","The Mesosphere is the layer that protects us from the sun's harmful rays.","The Thermosphere is the layer that protects us from the sun's harmful rays.","The Stratosphere is the layer that protects us from the sun's harmful rays.","The Stratosphere is the layer of the atmosphere that contains a high concentration of ozone, which protects us from the sun's harmful ultraviolet (UV) rays.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-one-way-750e9238","Science G6: Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying - Set 4","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","1. Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and comparing them in terms of similarities and differences, and identifying some environmental problems resulting from changes in atmospheric layers.","What is one way to reduce the impacts of climate change?","One way to reduce the impacts of climate change is to build more dams.","One way to reduce the impacts of climate change is to increase our carbon footprint by using more fossil fuels.","One way to reduce the impacts of climate change is to reduce our carbon footprint by using renewable energy sources and increasing energy efficiency.","One way to reduce the impacts of climate change is to stop using fossil fuels altogether.","One way to reduce the impacts of climate change is to reduce our carbon footprint by using renewable energy sources and increasing energy efficiency.","Reducing our carbon footprint by using renewable energy sources and increasing energy efficiency is one way to reduce the impacts of climate change.","/image-source/sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-one-way-750e9238.png","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-effect-of-beeb3479","Science G6: Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying - Set 4","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-1Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying their components, characteristics, changes, its effects on the environment and their benefits to humans.","4. Explaining the causes of climate change in some regions of the world and proposing multiple solutions to address the impacts and risks of weather fluctuations.","What is the effect of deforestation on the environment?","Deforestation has no effect on the environment.","Deforestation causes the Earth's temperature to decrease.","Deforestation causes the loss of biodiversity and contributes to climate change.","Deforestation causes the Earth's rotation speed to increase.","Deforestation causes the loss of biodiversity and contributes to climate change.","Deforestation causes the loss of biodiversity and contributes to climate change by releasing greenhouse gases such as carbon dioxide and methane into the atmosphere.","","",""
