"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-role-of-17312bdb","Science G6: Classifying the layers of the atmosphere - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","1. Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and comparing them in terms of similarities and differences, and identifying some environmental problems resulting from changes in atmospheric layers.","What is the role of the atmosphere in the Earth's water cycle?","The atmosphere has no role in the Earth's water cycle.","The atmosphere is a separate process from the Earth's water cycle.","The atmosphere is closely related to the Earth's water cycle, including the formation of clouds, wind, and precipitation.","The atmosphere is only related to the Earth's water cycle in certain regions.","The atmosphere is closely related to the Earth's water cycle, including the formation of clouds, wind, and precipitation.","The atmosphere is closely related to the Earth's water cycle, including the formation of clouds, wind, and precipitation, which is a key part of the Earth's water cycle.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-effect-of-b9da3c7d","Science G6: Classifying the layers of the atmosphere - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-1Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying their components, characteristics, changes, its effects on the environment and their benefits to humans.","3. Identifying the causes of weather variability and their relationship to the Earth’s water cycle, and predicting their environmental impacts on weather.","What is the effect of condensation on the environment?","Condensation has no effect on the environment.","Condensation causes the air to become cooler.","Condensation causes the air to become warmer and leads to the formation of clouds and precipitation.","Condensation causes the air to become drier and leads to drought.","Condensation causes the air to become warmer and leads to the formation of clouds and precipitation.","Condensation causes the air to become warmer and leads to the formation of clouds and precipitation, which is a key part of the Earth's water cycle.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-relationship-earth-4c24f6a3","Science G6: Classifying the layers of the atmosphere - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-1Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying their components, characteristics, changes, its effects on the environment and their benefits to humans.","3. Identifying the causes of weather variability and their relationship to the Earth’s water cycle, and predicting their environmental impacts on weather.","What is the relationship between the Earth's atmosphere and weather?","The Earth's atmosphere has no relationship to weather.","The Earth's atmosphere is a separate process from weather.","The Earth's atmosphere is closely related to weather, including the formation of clouds, wind, and precipitation.","The Earth's atmosphere is only related to weather in certain regions.","The Earth's atmosphere is closely related to weather, including the formation of clouds, wind, and precipitation.","The Earth's atmosphere is closely related to weather, including the formation of clouds, wind, and precipitation, which is a key part of the Earth's water cycle.","","",""
