"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-effect-of-d6ff4c33","Science G6: Classifying the layers of the atmosphere - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-1Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying their components, characteristics, changes, its effects on the environment and their benefits to humans.","3. Identifying the causes of weather variability and their relationship to the Earth’s water cycle, and predicting their environmental impacts on weather.","What is the effect of evaporation on the environment?","Evaporation has no effect on the environment.","Evaporation causes the air to become cooler.","Evaporation causes the air to become warmer and leads to the formation of clouds and precipitation.","Evaporation causes the air to become drier and leads to drought.","Evaporation causes the air to become warmer and leads to the formation of clouds and precipitation.","Evaporation causes the air to become warmer and leads to the formation of clouds and precipitation, which is a key part of the Earth's water cycle.","","",""
