"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-role-of-7538f118","Science G6: Classifying the layers of the atmosphere - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-1Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying their components, characteristics, changes, its effects on the environment and their benefits to humans.","3. Identifying the causes of weather variability and their relationship to the Earth’s water cycle, and predicting their environmental impacts on weather.","What is the role of the troposphere in the Earth's atmosphere?","The troposphere is the outermost layer of the atmosphere and protects the Earth from harm.","The troposphere is the layer of the atmosphere where weather occurs and is home to clouds, wind, and precipitation.","The troposphere is the layer of the atmosphere where the air is too hot to support life.","The troposphere is the layer of the atmosphere where the air is too cold to support life.","The troposphere is the layer of the atmosphere where weather occurs and is home to clouds, wind, and precipitation.","The troposphere is the layer of the atmosphere where weather occurs and is home to clouds, wind, and precipitation, which is a key part of the Earth's water cycle.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-reason-e1d83eb9","Science G6: Classifying the layers of the atmosphere - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","1. Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and comparing them in terms of similarities and differences, and identifying some environmental problems resulting from changes in atmospheric layers.","What is the main reason for the formation of clouds?","Clouds form when the air cools down and water vapor turns into liquid water.","Clouds form when the air is heated up and water vapor turns into gas.","Clouds form when the air is polluted with dust and particles.","Clouds form when the air is too dry and there is no water vapor.","Clouds form when the air cools down and water vapor turns into liquid water.","Clouds form when the air cools down and water vapor turns into liquid water, which is a key part of the Earth's water cycle.","","",""
