"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-effect-of-b79853f5","Science G6: Classifying the layers of the atmosphere - Set 3","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","1. Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and comparing them in terms of similarities and differences, and identifying some environmental problems resulting from changes in atmospheric layers.","What is the effect of climate change on weather patterns?","It makes the weather more stable","It makes the weather more unpredictable","It makes the weather colder","It makes the weather warmer","It makes the weather more unpredictable","Climate change makes the weather more unpredictable, leading to more extreme weather events, such as hurricanes, droughts, and heatwaves.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-force-24fdfad9","Science G6: Concluding the effect of gravity on - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-2-1 Describing the concept of force and distinguishing between different types","3. Distinguishing between types of forces based on their causes (gravity, friction, and magnetism).","What is the main force that pulls planets towards the Sun?","Gravity is the force that pulls planets towards the Sun.","Magnetism is the force that pulls planets towards the Sun.","Electricity is the force that pulls planets towards the Sun.","Friction is the force that pulls planets towards the Sun.","Gravity is the force that pulls planets towards the Sun.","Gravity is the force that pulls planets towards the Sun because of its mass.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-reason-expansion-e3bd35f2","Science G6: Concluding the effect of gravity on - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-3 Concluding the effect of gravity on the movement of the solar system, galaxies and associated phenomena.","4. Relating the speed of rotation and gravity between celestial bodies, and providing evidence for that","What is the reason for the expansion of the universe?","The Big Bang is the reason for the expansion of the universe.","The gravitational pull of galaxies is the reason for the expansion of the universe.","The rotation of galaxies is the reason for the expansion of the universe.","The size of galaxies is the reason for the expansion of the universe.","The Big Bang is the reason for the expansion of the universe.","The Big Bang is the reason for the expansion of the universe because of the rapid expansion of space-time.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-study-a4b1625a","Science G6: Concluding the effect of gravity on - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","2. Comparing the sun and other stars in terms of size, color and explans the relationship between a star’s color and its temperature","What is the term for the study of the universe?","Astronomy is the study of the universe.","Astrophysics is the study of the universe.","Cosmology is the study of the universe.","Geology is the study of the universe.","Astronomy is the study of the universe.","Astronomy is the study of the universe, including stars, planets, and galaxies.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-reason-formation-cfab7c60","Science G6: Concluding the effect of gravity on - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-3 Concluding the effect of gravity on the movement of the solar system, galaxies and associated phenomena.","4. Relating the speed of rotation and gravity between celestial bodies, and providing evidence for that","What is the reason for the formation of a black hole?","The collapse of a star is the reason for the formation of a black hole.","The explosion of a star is the reason for the formation of a black hole.","The rotation of a star is the reason for the formation of a black hole.","The size of a star is the reason for the formation of a black hole.","The collapse of a star is the reason for the formation of a black hole.","The collapse of a star is the reason for the formation of a black hole because of its massive gravity.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-explosion-5a31add2","Science G6: Concluding the effect of gravity on - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-3 Concluding the effect of gravity on the movement of the solar system, galaxies and associated phenomena.","2. Describing the movement of celestial bodies in the solar system, their relationships with each other, and their effects.","What is the term for the explosion of a star?","Supernova is the explosion of a star.","Nebula is the explosion of a star.","Black hole is the explosion of a star.","Comet is the explosion of a star.","Supernova is the explosion of a star.","A supernova is the explosion of a star that occurs when it runs out of fuel.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-movement-7595c85d","Science G6: Concluding the effect of gravity on - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-2 Explaining the phenomena related to the movement of the earth, the moon and the sun and the resulting","1. Explaining the importance and impact of the sun's movement on aspects of life around them.","What is the term for the movement of the Earth around the Sun?","Revolution is the movement of the Earth around the Sun.","Rotation is the movement of the Earth around the Sun.","Orbit is the movement of the Earth around the Sun.","Eccentricity is the movement of the Earth around the Sun.","Revolution is the movement of the Earth around the Sun.","Revolution is the movement of the Earth around the Sun due to gravity.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-difference-3b629397","Science G6: Concluding the effect of gravity on - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-3 Concluding the effect of gravity on the movement of the solar system, galaxies and associated phenomena.","2. Describing the movement of celestial bodies in the solar system, their relationships with each other, and their effects.","What is the main difference between a galaxy and a star cluster?","A galaxy is a vast system containing billions of stars, gas, and dust, while a star cluster is a smaller grouping of stars.","A galaxy is a collection of planets, while a star cluster is a collection of stars.","A galaxy is a collection of stars, while a star cluster is a collection of stars.","A galaxy is a collection of planets, while a star cluster is a collection of galaxies.","A galaxy is a vast system containing billions of stars, gas, and dust, while a star cluster is a smaller grouping of stars.","A galaxy is an enormous system containing billions of stars, gas clouds, dust, and dark matter. A star cluster is a much smaller grouping of stars (hundreds to thousands) that are gravitationally bound together. Both are made of stars, but galaxies are far larger and more complex.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-movement-85747cfd","Science G6: Concluding the effect of gravity on - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-3 Concluding the effect of gravity on the movement of the solar system, galaxies and associated phenomena.","4. Relating the speed of rotation and gravity between celestial bodies, and providing evidence for that","What is the term for the movement of galaxies through space?","Galactic drift is the movement of galaxies through space.","Cosmic flow is the movement of galaxies through space.","Galactic rotation is the movement of galaxies through space.","Galactic oscillation is the movement of galaxies through space.","Galactic drift is the movement of galaxies through space.","Galactic drift is the movement of galaxies through space due to the expansion of the universe.","","",""
