"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-phase-of-d2062d29","Science G6: Describing the changes in the appearance of the moon during - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-1 Describing the changes in the appearance of the moon during its revolution around the Earth explains the reasons for these changes","2. Explaining the change in the apparent shape of the moon during its orbit around earth","What is the phase of the moon when it appears as a thin crescent in the sky?","New Moon","Full Moon","First Quarter Moon","Waxing Crescent Moon","Waxing Crescent Moon","The waxing crescent moon phase occurs when the moon appears as a thin crescent in the sky, which happens when the moon is moving towards full moon and more of its illuminated surface is visible from Earth.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-phase-of-moon-338a9e81","Science G6: Describing the changes in the appearance of the moon during - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-1 Describing the changes in the appearance of the moon during its revolution around the Earth explains the reasons for these changes","2. Explaining the change in the apparent shape of the moon during its orbit around earth","Which phase of the moon occurs when the left half of the moon is illuminated and the right half is in shadow?","First Quarter Moon","Last Quarter Moon","Waxing Crescent Moon","Waning Gibbous Moon","Last Quarter Moon","The last quarter moon phase occurs when the left half of the moon is illuminated by the sun and the right half is in shadow, making it appear as a half-moon shape.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-moon-f7f2be62","Science G6: Describing the changes in the appearance of the moon during - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-1 Describing the changes in the appearance of the moon during its revolution around the Earth explains the reasons for these changes","2. Explaining the change in the apparent shape of the moon during its orbit around earth","What is the term for the moon's rotation on its axis?","Revolution","Rotation","Orbit","Eclipse","Rotation","The moon's rotation on its axis is the term used to describe the moon spinning around its own axis, which takes approximately the same amount of time as its orbit around the Earth.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-of-best-describes-055f5731","Science G6: Describing the changes in the appearance of the moon during - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-1 Describing the changes in the appearance of the moon during its revolution around the Earth explains the reasons for these changes","2. Explaining the change in the apparent shape of the moon during its orbit around earth","Which of the following best describes the gibbous moon phase?","The moon appears as a thin crescent in the sky","The moon appears more than half full but not completely full","The moon appears as a complete circle in the sky","The moon is not visible from Earth","The moon appears more than half full but not completely full","The gibbous moon phase occurs when the moon appears more than half full but not completely full, which happens when the moon is nearing full moon or moving away from full moon.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-phase-of-cbbb4217","Science G6: Describing the changes in the appearance of the moon during - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-1 Describing the changes in the appearance of the moon during its revolution around the Earth explains the reasons for these changes","2. Explaining the change in the apparent shape of the moon during its orbit around earth","What is the phase of the moon when the side of the moon facing the Earth is not illuminated by the sun?","New Moon","Full Moon","First Quarter Moon","Last Quarter Moon","New Moon","The new moon phase occurs when the side of the moon facing the Earth is not illuminated by the sun, making it invisible from our planet.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-phase-of-bbac2c5b","Science G6: Describing the changes in the appearance of the moon during - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-1 Describing the changes in the appearance of the moon during its revolution around the Earth explains the reasons for these changes","2. Explaining the change in the apparent shape of the moon during its orbit around earth","What is the phase of the moon when it appears as a complete circle in the sky?","New Moon","Full Moon","First Quarter Moon","Last Quarter Moon","Full Moon","The full moon phase occurs when the entire face of the moon is illuminated by the sun, making it appear as a complete circle in the sky.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-different-4950d761","Science G6: Describing the changes in the appearance of the moon during - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-1 Describing the changes in the appearance of the moon during its revolution around the Earth explains the reasons for these changes","1. Describing the apparent shape of the moon during its rotation around the earth, and naming the different phases of the moon.","What is the term for the different shapes the moon appears to change into as it orbits the Earth?","Moon Phases","Earth Rotations","Solar Flares","Galaxy Cycles","Moon Phases","The different shapes the moon appears to change into as it orbits the Earth are called moon phases, which include new moon, full moon, and the quarter phases.","","",""
