"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-difference-2e328fab","Science G6: Describing the factors and processes that affected the Earth's - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-3 Describing the factors and processes that affected the Earth›s surface which changed some of its","2. Describing the impact of earthquakes and volcanoes in shaping the Earth's surface and changing its features.","What is the main difference between a volcano and a mountain?","A volcano is taller than a mountain","A volcano is a mountain with a crater","A volcano is a landform that erupts with lava and ash","A volcano is a type of rock","A volcano is a landform that erupts with lava and ash","A volcano is a landform that erupts with lava and ash, whereas a mountain is a natural elevation of the Earth's surface.","","",""
