"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-reason-03cb2b64","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-1Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying their components, characteristics, changes, its effects on the environment and their benefits to humans.","2. Explaining the movement of air masses and air currents and describing their effects on Earth’s weather.","What is the main reason why earthquakes occur?","Movement of the Earth's crust","Volcanic eruptions","Weather changes","Tides","Movement of the Earth's crust","Earthquakes occur due to the movement of the Earth's crust, which can cause the ground to shake violently.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-movement-5d675aea","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-3 Describing the factors and processes that affected the Earth›s surface which changed some of its","2. Describing the impact of earthquakes and volcanoes in shaping the Earth's surface and changing its features.","What is the term for the movement of the Earth's crust that can cause earthquakes and volcanoes?","Weathering","Erosion","Plate Tectonics","Glaciation","Plate Tectonics","Plate Tectonics is the movement of the Earth's crust that can cause earthquakes and volcanoes.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-area-77905212","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-5 Determining the causes and effects of earthquakes and volcanoes and identifying the sites most vulnerable to earthquakes and volcanoes.","1. Relating the change of the Earth's shape with the external and internal geological processes.","What is the term for the area that is most likely to be affected by earthquakes and volcanoes?","Tectonic Plate","Volcanic Zone","Earthquake Zone","Geological Fault","Tectonic Plate","A Tectonic Plate is the area that is most likely to be affected by earthquakes and volcanoes.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-effect-2c4bfac1","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-2 Deducing the relationship of the Earth›s spheres to each other and predicting the interactions, and changes that occur between them and the geological effects resulting from them.","2. Describing how magma moves Earth's plates, using that for explaining the formation of oceans and mountains.","What is the main effect of an earthquake on buildings and structures?","Formation of new land","Creation of new oceans","Damage to buildings and structures","Changes in the weather","Damage to buildings and structures","An earthquake can cause damage to buildings and structures, depending on the intensity of the quake.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-shaking-bc2502af","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-3 Describing the factors and processes that affected the Earth›s surface which changed some of its","3. Explaining the factors of erosion, weathering, and sedimentation and their causes, and predicting the patterns of their action and their effects on earth.","What is the term for the shaking of the ground caused by the movement of magma beneath the Earth's surface?","Seismic activity","Volcanic activity","Earth's rotation","Weathering","Volcanic activity","Volcanic activity refers to the shaking of the ground caused by the movement of magma beneath the Earth's surface.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-cause-78d0d1fe","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-3 Describing the factors and processes that affected the Earth›s surface which changed some of its","3. Explaining the factors of erosion, weathering, and sedimentation and their causes, and predicting the patterns of their action and their effects on earth.","What is the main cause of volcanic eruptions?","Movement of the Earth's crust","Changes in the weather","Earth's rotation","Magma buildup","Magma buildup","Volcanic eruptions occur when magma from the Earth's interior builds up and is released through the surface.","","",""
