"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-goal-22defd2a","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 3","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-5 Determining the causes and effects of earthquakes and volcanoes and identifying the sites most vulnerable to earthquakes and volcanoes.","3. Determining the locations and types of earthquake monitoring stations and devices in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia and comparing between them.","What is the main goal of earthquake monitoring in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia?","To predict the weather","To detect and measure earthquake waves","To study the movement of the Earth's crust","To track the movement of animals","To detect and measure earthquake waves","The main goal of earthquake monitoring in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia is to detect and measure earthquake waves, which helps scientists understand the causes and effects of earthquakes and prepare for future earthquakes.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-are-earthquake-9711c1cf","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 3","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-5 Determining the causes and effects of earthquakes and volcanoes and identifying the sites most vulnerable to earthquakes and volcanoes.","3. Determining the locations and types of earthquake monitoring stations and devices in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia and comparing between them.","Why are earthquake monitoring stations located in different parts of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia?","To detect and measure earthquake waves","To study the movement of the Earth's crust","To track the movement of animals","To predict the weather","To detect and measure earthquake waves","Earthquake monitoring stations are located in different parts of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia to detect and measure earthquake waves, which helps scientists understand the causes and effects of earthquakes and prepare for future earthquakes.","/image-source/sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-are-earthquake-9711c1cf.png","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-name-of-602292ef","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 3","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-5 Determining the causes and effects of earthquakes and volcanoes and identifying the sites most vulnerable to earthquakes and volcanoes.","1. Relating the change of the Earth's shape with the external and internal geological processes.","What is the name of the device that measures the strength of earthquake waves?","Seismometer","Accelerometer","Barometer","Thermometer","Accelerometer","An accelerometer is a device that measures the strength of earthquake waves, which helps scientists understand the severity of the earthquake.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-are-earthquake-1cca4465","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 3","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-5 Determining the causes and effects of earthquakes and volcanoes and identifying the sites most vulnerable to earthquakes and volcanoes.","3. Determining the locations and types of earthquake monitoring stations and devices in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia and comparing between them.","Why are earthquake monitoring stations important for the people of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia?","To predict the weather","To detect and measure earthquake waves","To study the movement of the Earth's crust","To track the movement of animals","To detect and measure earthquake waves","Earthquake monitoring stations are important for the people of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia because they help scientists detect and measure earthquake waves, which helps them understand the causes and effects of earthquakes and prepare for future earthquakes.","/image-source/sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-are-earthquake-1cca4465.png","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-type-of-data-a373905d","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 3","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-5 Determining the causes and effects of earthquakes and volcanoes and identifying the sites most vulnerable to earthquakes and volcanoes.","3. Determining the locations and types of earthquake monitoring stations and devices in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia and comparing between them.","What type of data do seismographs record?","Temperature and humidity","Pressure and wind speed","Ground motion and earthquake waves","Earthquake location and depth","Ground motion and earthquake waves","Seismographs record ground motion and earthquake waves, which helps scientists understand the causes and effects of earthquakes.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-are-earthquake-1cecf1bb","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 3","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-5 Determining the causes and effects of earthquakes and volcanoes and identifying the sites most vulnerable to earthquakes and volcanoes.","3. Determining the locations and types of earthquake monitoring stations and devices in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia and comparing between them.","Why are earthquake monitoring stations important?","To predict the weather","To detect and measure earthquake waves","To study the movement of the Earth's crust","To track the movement of animals","To detect and measure earthquake waves","Earthquake monitoring stations are important because they help scientists detect and measure earthquake waves, which helps them understand the causes and effects of earthquakes and prepare for future earthquakes.","/image-source/sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-are-earthquake-1cecf1bb.png","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-name-of-891e34f5","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 3","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-5 Determining the causes and effects of earthquakes and volcanoes and identifying the sites most vulnerable to earthquakes and volcanoes.","1. Relating the change of the Earth's shape with the external and internal geological processes.","What is the name of the device that records the time and strength of earthquakes?","Seismometer","Spectrometer","Telescope","Microscope","Seismometer","A seismometer is a device that records the time and strength of earthquakes, which helps scientists understand the causes and effects of earthquakes.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-are-some-491f3451","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 3","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-5 Determining the causes and effects of earthquakes and volcanoes and identifying the sites most vulnerable to earthquakes and volcanoes.","3. Determining the locations and types of earthquake monitoring stations and devices in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia and comparing between them.","Why are some areas in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia more prone to earthquakes?","Because they are near the ocean","Because they are near mountains","Because they are near fault lines","Because they are near deserts","Because they are near fault lines","Areas near fault lines are more prone to earthquakes because fault lines are cracks in the Earth's crust where tectonic plates move and sometimes get stuck, causing earthquakes.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-type-of-device-934f7cb7","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 3","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-5 Determining the causes and effects of earthquakes and volcanoes and identifying the sites most vulnerable to earthquakes and volcanoes.","1. Relating the change of the Earth's shape with the external and internal geological processes.","What type of device is often used to measure the ground motion during an earthquake?","Seismograph","Barometer","Thermometer","Hygrometer","Seismograph","A seismograph is a device that measures the ground motion during an earthquake, which helps scientists understand the severity of the earthquake.","/image-source/sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-type-of-device-934f7cb7.png","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-purpose-2b04e8ab","Science G6: Determining the causes and effects of - Set 3","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-5 Determining the causes and effects of earthquakes and volcanoes and identifying the sites most vulnerable to earthquakes and volcanoes.","3. Determining the locations and types of earthquake monitoring stations and devices in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia and comparing between them.","What is the main purpose of earthquake monitoring stations?","To predict the weather","To detect and measure earthquake waves","To study the movement of the Earth's crust","To track the movement of animals","To detect and measure earthquake waves","Earthquake monitoring stations are used to detect and measure earthquake waves, which helps scientists understand the causes and effects of earthquakes.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-cause-b4b03b2c","Science G6: Determining the characteristics of the solar - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","2. Comparing the sun and other stars in terms of size, color and explans the relationship between a star’s color and its temperature","What is the main cause of the greenhouse effect?","The main cause of the greenhouse effect is the release of carbon dioxide into the atmosphere.","The main cause of the greenhouse effect is the release of methane into the atmosphere.","The main cause of the greenhouse effect is the release of chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs) into the atmosphere.","The main cause of the greenhouse effect is the release of sulfur dioxide into the atmosphere.","The main cause of the greenhouse effect is the release of carbon dioxide into the atmosphere.","The main cause of the greenhouse effect is the release of carbon dioxide into the atmosphere.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-of-correctly-lists-85a4a418","Science G6: Determining the characteristics of the solar - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","2. Comparing the sun and other stars in terms of size, color and explans the relationship between a star’s color and its temperature","Which of the following correctly lists the main layers of the Earth's atmosphere from lowest to highest?","Troposphere, stratosphere, mesosphere, thermosphere, exosphere","Stratosphere, troposphere, mesosphere, thermosphere, exosphere","Troposphere, mesosphere, stratosphere, thermosphere, exosphere","Troposphere, stratosphere, thermosphere, mesosphere, exosphere","Troposphere, stratosphere, mesosphere, thermosphere, exosphere","The Earth's atmosphere is divided into five main layers. From lowest to highest: the troposphere (where weather occurs), the stratosphere (contains the ozone layer), the mesosphere (where meteors burn up), the thermosphere (very high temperatures due to solar radiation), and the exosphere (outermost layer that gradually merges into space).","/image-source/sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-of-correctly-lists-85a4a418.png","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-difference-53fdb66d","Science G6: Determining the characteristics of the solar - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","2. Comparing the sun and other stars in terms of size, color and explans the relationship between a star’s color and its temperature","What is the main difference between the troposphere and the thermosphere?","The troposphere is colder than the thermosphere.","The troposphere is warmer than the thermosphere.","The troposphere is the layer where weather occurs, while the thermosphere is the layer where the ozone layer is located.","The troposphere is the layer where the ozone layer is located, while the thermosphere is the layer where weather occurs.","The troposphere is colder than the thermosphere.","The thermosphere is much hotter than the troposphere: temperatures in the thermosphere can reach up to 2,000 degrees C due to the direct absorption of intense solar radiation. The troposphere, where we live, has an average temperature of about 15 degrees C near the surface and gets colder with altitude.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-ionosphere-1b10ff1a","Science G6: Determining the characteristics of the solar - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-1Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying their components, characteristics, changes, its effects on the environment and their benefits to humans.","2. Explaining the movement of air masses and air currents and describing their effects on Earth’s weather.","What is the ionosphere?","The ionosphere is the layer of the atmosphere that extends from the surface of the Earth to the edge of space.","The ionosphere is the layer of the atmosphere that extends from about 50 to 85 kilometers above the Earth's surface.","The ionosphere is the layer of the atmosphere that extends from about 85 to 600 kilometers above the Earth's surface.","The ionosphere is the layer of the atmosphere that extends from about 600 to 10,000 kilometers above the Earth's surface.","The ionosphere is the layer of the atmosphere that extends from about 85 to 600 kilometers above the Earth's surface.","The ionosphere is the layer of the atmosphere that extends from about 85 to 600 kilometers above the Earth's surface.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-effect-07e24496","Science G6: Determining the characteristics of the solar - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-1Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying their components, characteristics, changes, its effects on the environment and their benefits to humans.","3. Identifying the causes of weather variability and their relationship to the Earth’s water cycle, and predicting their environmental impacts on weather.","What is the main effect of the greenhouse effect on the environment?","The greenhouse effect has no effect on the environment.","The greenhouse effect causes global cooling.","The greenhouse effect causes global warming.","The greenhouse effect has a neutral effect on the environment.","The greenhouse effect causes global warming.","The greenhouse effect causes global warming.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-difference-6817d09e","Science G6: Determining the characteristics of the solar - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","2. Comparing the sun and other stars in terms of size, color and explans the relationship between a star’s color and its temperature","What is the main difference between the troposphere and the stratosphere?","The troposphere is colder than the stratosphere.","The troposphere is warmer than the stratosphere.","The troposphere is the layer where weather occurs, while the stratosphere is the layer where the ozone layer is located.","The troposphere is the layer where the ozone layer is located, while the stratosphere is the layer where weather occurs.","The troposphere is the layer where weather occurs, while the stratosphere is the layer where the ozone layer is located.","The troposphere is the layer where weather occurs, while the stratosphere is the layer where the ozone layer is located.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-mesosphere-6ad10934","Science G6: Determining the characteristics of the solar - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-1Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying their components, characteristics, changes, its effects on the environment and their benefits to humans.","2. Explaining the movement of air masses and air currents and describing their effects on Earth’s weather.","What is the mesosphere?","The mesosphere is the layer where the ozone layer is located.","The mesosphere is the layer where weather occurs.","The mesosphere is the layer of the atmosphere that extends from about 50 to 85 kilometers above the Earth's surface.","The mesosphere is the layer of the atmosphere that extends from the surface of the Earth to the edge of space.","The mesosphere is the layer of the atmosphere that extends from about 50 to 85 kilometers above the Earth's surface.","The mesosphere is the layer of the atmosphere that extends from about 50 to 85 kilometers above the Earth's surface.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-problem-4194e5f0","Science G6: Determining the characteristics of the solar - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","2. Comparing the sun and other stars in terms of size, color and explans the relationship between a star’s color and its temperature","What is the main problem caused by the depletion of the ozone layer?","The depletion of the ozone layer causes global warming.","The depletion of the ozone layer causes acid rain.","The depletion of the ozone layer allows more UV radiation to reach the Earth's surface, which can cause skin cancer and other health problems.","The depletion of the ozone layer has no effect on the Earth's climate.","The depletion of the ozone layer allows more UV radiation to reach the Earth's surface, which can cause skin cancer and other health problems.","The depletion of the ozone layer allows more UV radiation to reach the Earth's surface, which can cause skin cancer and other health problems.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-cause-60c5a500","Science G6: Determining the characteristics of the solar - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","1. Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and comparing them in terms of similarities and differences, and identifying some environmental problems resulting from changes in atmospheric layers.","What is the main cause of the depletion of the ozone layer?","The main cause of the depletion of the ozone layer is the release of carbon dioxide into the atmosphere.","The main cause of the depletion of the ozone layer is the release of methane into the atmosphere.","The main cause of the depletion of the ozone layer is the release of chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs) into the atmosphere.","The main cause of the depletion of the ozone layer is the release of sulfur dioxide into the atmosphere.","The main cause of the depletion of the ozone layer is the release of chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs) into the atmosphere.","The main cause of the depletion of the ozone layer is the release of chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs) into the atmosphere.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-effect-of-0a36a8b9","Science G6: Determining the characteristics of the solar - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","2. Comparing the sun and other stars in terms of size, color and explans the relationship between a star’s color and its temperature","What is the effect of acid rain on the environment?","Acid rain has no effect on the environment.","Acid rain causes global warming.","Acid rain causes the death of trees and other plants.","Acid rain causes the acidification of lakes and rivers.","Acid rain causes the acidification of lakes and rivers.","Acid rain causes the acidification of lakes and rivers.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-do-we-c8d17a68","Science G6: Determining the characteristics of the solar - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","2. Comparing the sun and other stars in terms of size, color and explans the relationship between a star’s color and its temperature","Why do we see different colors in the sky at different times of day?","Because of the scattering of sunlight by the atmosphere","Because the Sun changes color during the day","Because of the different temperatures of the air","Because clouds block sunlight differently at different times","Because of the scattering of sunlight by the atmosphere","The sky appears different colors at different times of day because of Rayleigh scattering. When sunlight passes through the atmosphere, gas molecules scatter shorter (blue) wavelengths in all directions during midday, making the sky look blue. At sunrise and sunset, sunlight travels through more atmosphere, scattering away blue light and leaving red and orange wavelengths.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-do-stars-cfd00e3b","Science G6: Determining the characteristics of the solar - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","2. Comparing the sun and other stars in terms of size, color and explans the relationship between a star’s color and its temperature","Why do stars come in different colors?","Because they are different sizes","Because they are different temperatures","Because they are different shapes","Because they are different materials","Because they are different temperatures","Stars come in different colors because they are different temperatures.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-difference-1c81f5ab","Science G6: Determining the characteristics of the solar - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","2. Comparing the sun and other stars in terms of size, color and explans the relationship between a star’s color and its temperature","What is the main difference between a star and a planet?","A star is bigger than a planet","A star is smaller than a planet","A star is a huge ball of hot, glowing gas, while a planet is a smaller, cooler body","A star is a smaller, cooler body, while a planet is a huge ball of hot, glowing gas","A star is a huge ball of hot, glowing gas, while a planet is a smaller, cooler body","A star is a huge ball of hot, glowing gas, while a planet is a smaller, cooler body.","","",""
