"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-relationship-a-282d720e","Science G6: Determining the characteristics of the solar - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","2. Comparing the sun and other stars in terms of size, color and explans the relationship between a star’s color and its temperature","What is the relationship between a star's color and its temperature?","The hotter the star, the cooler its color","The cooler the star, the hotter its color","The hotter the star, the hotter its color","The cooler the star, the cooler its color","The hotter the star, the hotter its color","The hotter a star is, the hotter its color. This means that blue stars are hotter than red stars.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-main-sequence-stars-e49b93bb","Science G6: Determining the characteristics of the solar - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-1-4 Determining the characteristics of the solar system, and comparing the solar system to the galaxy and the","2. Comparing the sun and other stars in terms of size, color and explans the relationship between a star’s color and its temperature","For main-sequence stars, what is the general relationship between a star's color and its surface temperature?","Blue stars are the hottest and red stars are the coolest","Red stars are the hottest and blue stars are the coolest","Yellow stars are the hottest of all star types","All stars have the same surface temperature","Blue stars are the hottest and red stars are the coolest","For main-sequence stars, color indicates surface temperature. Blue and blue-white stars are the hottest (above 10,000 degrees C), white and yellow stars like our Sun are intermediate, and orange and red stars are the coolest (below 5,000 degrees C).","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-is-it-e61611e3","Science G6: Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-2 Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and their types, explaining chemical changes of matter and the related concepts and methods, and comparing the masses of substances when their properties change based on the law of conservation of mass.","4. Explaining the concept of solubility and gives the factors affecting it.","Why is it important to know about solubility?","Because it helps us understand the properties of substances.","Because it helps us understand the behavior of substances in different liquids.","Because it helps us understand the effects of temperature and pressure on substances.","Because it helps us understand the laws of physics.","Because it helps us understand the effects of temperature and pressure on substances.","It is important to know about solubility because it helps us understand the effects of temperature and pressure on substances.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-law-of-05906646","Science G6: Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-2 Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and their types, explaining chemical changes of matter and the related concepts and methods, and comparing the masses of substances when their properties change based on the law of conservation of mass.","4. Explaining the concept of solubility and gives the factors affecting it.","What is the law of conservation of mass related to solubility?","The law of conservation of mass states that the mass of a substance remains the same when it dissolves in a liquid.","The law of conservation of mass states that the mass of a substance increases when it dissolves in a liquid.","The law of conservation of mass states that the mass of a substance decreases when it dissolves in a liquid.","The law of conservation of mass has no relation to solubility.","The law of conservation of mass states that the mass of a substance remains the same when it dissolves in a liquid.","The law of conservation of mass states that the mass of a substance remains the same when it dissolves in a liquid.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-solubility-d80fae05","Science G6: Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What is solubility?","The ability of a substance to change its state from solid to liquid.","The ability of a substance to dissolve in a liquid.","The ability of a substance to change its state from liquid to gas.","The ability of a substance to change its state from gas to solid.","The ability of a substance to dissolve in a liquid.","Solubility is the ability of a substance to dissolve in a liquid.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-affects-solubility-of-7a58f42c","Science G6: Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-2 Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and their types, explaining chemical changes of matter and the related concepts and methods, and comparing the masses of substances when their properties change based on the law of conservation of mass.","4. Explaining the concept of solubility and gives the factors affecting it.","What affects the solubility of a substance?","Only the temperature of the liquid.","Only the pressure of the liquid.","The temperature and pressure of the liquid.","The amount of the substance added to the liquid.","The temperature and pressure of the liquid.","The solubility of a substance is affected by both the temperature and pressure of the liquid.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-do-some-7662e126","Science G6: Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-2 Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and their types, explaining chemical changes of matter and the related concepts and methods, and comparing the masses of substances when their properties change based on the law of conservation of mass.","5. Distinguishing between the physical methods used to separate the components of a mixture or solution, and providing examples. Describing the process of distillation and identifying some of its industrial applications.","Why do some substances dissolve in water?","Because they are attracted to the water molecules.","Because they are repelled by the water molecules.","Because they are the same as the water molecules.","Because they are different from the water molecules.","Because they are attracted to the water molecules.","Substances dissolve in water because they are attracted to the water molecules.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-a-substance-25c10e5c","Science G6: Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-2 Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and their types, explaining chemical changes of matter and the related concepts and methods, and comparing the masses of substances when their properties change based on the law of conservation of mass.","1. Defining the chemical bond, explaining its role in changing the properties of a chemical substance, and identifying indicators of a chemical reaction occurrence.","What happens when a substance dissolves in a liquid?","The substance changes its state from solid to liquid.","The substance changes its state from liquid to gas.","The substance breaks down into its individual particles.","The substance remains the same as it was before.","The substance breaks down into its individual particles.","When a substance dissolves in a liquid, it breaks down into its individual particles.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-do-some-edd3634f","Science G6: Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-2 Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and their types, explaining chemical changes of matter and the related concepts and methods, and comparing the masses of substances when their properties change based on the law of conservation of mass.","4. Explaining the concept of solubility and gives the factors affecting it.","Why do some substances not dissolve in water?","Because they are too heavy for the water.","Because they are too light for the water.","Because they are not attracted to the water molecules.","Because they are the same as the water molecules.","Because they are not attracted to the water molecules.","Some substances do not dissolve in water because they are not attracted to the water molecules.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-difference-a-1f8ccaaa","Science G6: Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-2 Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and their types, explaining chemical changes of matter and the related concepts and methods, and comparing the masses of substances when their properties change based on the law of conservation of mass.","4. Explaining the concept of solubility and gives the factors affecting it.","What is the difference between a soluble and an insoluble substance?","A soluble substance dissolves in water, while an insoluble substance does not.","A soluble substance does not dissolve in water, while an insoluble substance does.","A soluble substance is heavier than an insoluble substance.","A soluble substance is lighter than an insoluble substance.","A soluble substance dissolves in water, while an insoluble substance does not.","A soluble substance dissolves in water, while an insoluble substance does not.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-how-temperature-affect-7788a929","Science G6: Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-2 Distinguishing between compounds and mixtures and their types, explaining chemical changes of matter and the related concepts and methods, and comparing the masses of substances when their properties change based on the law of conservation of mass.","4. Explaining the concept of solubility and gives the factors affecting it.","How does temperature affect the solubility of a substance?","It increases the solubility of the substance.","It decreases the solubility of the substance.","It has no effect on the solubility of the substance.","It increases the solubility of the substance at high temperatures and decreases it at low temperatures.","It decreases the solubility of the substance.","Temperature can decrease the solubility of a substance.","","",""
