"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-an-acid-3bdf782e","Science G6: Exploring the chemical properties of materials - Set 5","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-4 Exploring the chemical properties of materials, and distinguishing between the interactions of acids and bases, their chemical properties, and their uses.","5. Explaining what is meant by the neutralization reaction between an acid and a base to form a salt, and name some types of salts, and their properties and uses","What happens when an acid and a base mix together?","The acid and base get stronger.","The acid and base form a new substance called a salt.","The acid and base cancel each other out.","The acid and base turn into water.","The acid and base form a new substance called a salt.","When an acid and a base mix together, they form a new substance called a salt, which is a type of chemical compound.","","",""
