"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-an-example-aec8f400","Science G6: Exploring the chemical properties of materials - Set 5","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-4 Exploring the chemical properties of materials, and distinguishing between the interactions of acids and bases, their chemical properties, and their uses.","5. Explaining what is meant by the neutralization reaction between an acid and a base to form a salt, and name some types of salts, and their properties and uses","What is an example of a salt that can be formed from a neutralization reaction?","Sodium chloride (table salt).","Hydrochloric acid.","Baking soda.","Ammonia.","Sodium chloride (table salt).","Sodium chloride, also known as table salt, is an example of a salt that can be formed from a neutralization reaction between sodium hydroxide and hydrochloric acid.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-purpose-of-2db72ef0","Science G6: Exploring the chemical properties of materials - Set 5","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-4 Exploring the chemical properties of materials, and distinguishing between the interactions of acids and bases, their chemical properties, and their uses.","5. Explaining what is meant by the neutralization reaction between an acid and a base to form a salt, and name some types of salts, and their properties and uses","Which products are typically formed when an acid reacts with a base in a neutralization reaction?","A salt and water.","Only oxygen gas.","Only the original acid.","A metal and hydrogen gas.","A salt and water.","A typical acid-base neutralization reaction produces a salt and water.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-a-common-c8c27772","Science G6: Exploring the chemical properties of materials - Set 5","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-4 Exploring the chemical properties of materials, and distinguishing between the interactions of acids and bases, their chemical properties, and their uses.","5. Explaining what is meant by the neutralization reaction between an acid and a base to form a salt, and name some types of salts, and their properties and uses","What is a common use of a salt formed from a neutralization reaction?","As a cleaning agent.","As a food preservative.","As a medicine.","As a fuel source.","As a food preservative.","A common use of a salt formed from a neutralization reaction is as a food preservative, such as sodium chloride (table salt).","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-result-of-88ce6c0c","Science G6: Exploring the chemical properties of materials - Set 5","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-4 Exploring the chemical properties of materials, and distinguishing between the interactions of acids and bases, their chemical properties, and their uses.","5. Explaining what is meant by the neutralization reaction between an acid and a base to form a salt, and name some types of salts, and their properties and uses","What is the result of mixing an acid and a base in a neutralization reaction?","A new acid or base is formed.","A gas and a solid are produced.","A salt and water are formed.","The acid and base cancel each other out.","A salt and water are formed.","The result of mixing an acid and a base in a neutralization reaction is the formation of a salt and water.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-reaction-8c0ae23d","Science G6: Exploring the chemical properties of materials - Set 5","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-4 Exploring the chemical properties of materials, and distinguishing between the interactions of acids and bases, their chemical properties, and their uses.","5. Explaining what is meant by the neutralization reaction between an acid and a base to form a salt, and name some types of salts, and their properties and uses","What is the term for the reaction between an acid and a base?","Neutralization reaction.","Acid-base reaction.","Chemical reaction.","Physical reaction.","Neutralization reaction.","The term for the reaction between an acid and a base is a neutralization reaction.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-characteristic-1ba997fa","Science G6: Exploring the chemical properties of materials - Set 5","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-4 Exploring the chemical properties of materials, and distinguishing between the interactions of acids and bases, their chemical properties, and their uses.","5. Explaining what is meant by the neutralization reaction between an acid and a base to form a salt, and name some types of salts, and their properties and uses","What is the main characteristic of a salt formed from a neutralization reaction?","It is highly reactive.","It is highly soluble in water.","It is a type of chemical compound.","It is highly flammable.","It is a type of chemical compound.","The main characteristic of a salt formed from a neutralization reaction is that it is a type of chemical compound.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-purpose-of-38ca8876","Science G6: Exploring the chemical properties of materials - Set 5","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-4 Exploring the chemical properties of materials, and distinguishing between the interactions of acids and bases, their chemical properties, and their uses.","5. Explaining what is meant by the neutralization reaction between an acid and a base to form a salt, and name some types of salts, and their properties and uses","What is the main purpose of an acid-base neutralization reaction?","To reduce acidity or basicity by reacting an acid with a base.","To make every solution strongly acidic.","To produce only a gas.","To separate atoms by nuclear fission.","To reduce acidity or basicity by reacting an acid with a base.","Neutralization reacts an acid with a base, reducing their acidic and basic properties and commonly forming salt and water.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-temperature-329df141","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","2. Distinguishing the different materials in terms of the physical properties of the substance that can be calculated or measured, such as mass, volume, density, buoyancy, color and boiling point","What is the term for the temperature at which a substance changes state from a solid to a liquid?","Melting point","Freezing point","Boiling point","Condensation point","Melting point","Melting point is the temperature at which a substance changes state from a solid to a liquid.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-particles-b5aa8664","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","5. Explaining the changes of matter due to the effect of heat.","What happens to the particles of a substance when it is cooled?","They move faster","They move slower","They stay the same","They disappear","They move slower","When a substance is cooled, its particles lose energy and move slower, causing the substance to contract and decrease in volume.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-how-1d63fc3d","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","2. Distinguishing the different materials in terms of the physical properties of the substance that can be calculated or measured, such as mass, volume, density, buoyancy, color and boiling point","What is the term for how tightly packed the particles of a substance are?","The amount of space between particles","The temperature of a substance","The density of a substance","The color of a substance","The density of a substance","Density is the measure of how tightly packed the particles of a substance are.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-volume-43dff3a2","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","5. Explaining the changes of matter due to the effect of heat.","What happens to the volume of a substance when it is heated?","It increases","It decreases","It stays the same","It disappears","It increases","When a substance is heated, its particles gain energy and move faster, causing the substance to expand and increase in volume.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-ability-0d51c84a","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","2. Distinguishing the different materials in terms of the physical properties of the substance that can be calculated or measured, such as mass, volume, density, buoyancy, color and boiling point","What is the term for the ability of an object to float or sink in a fluid?","Buoyancy","Density","Mass","Volume","Buoyancy","Buoyancy is the ability of an object to float or sink in a fluid, depending on its density relative to the fluid.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-amount-d183371c","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","2. Distinguishing the different materials in terms of the physical properties of the substance that can be calculated or measured, such as mass, volume, density, buoyancy, color and boiling point","What is the term for the amount of space inside a substance?","Volume","Mass","Density","Buoyancy","Volume","Volume is the amount of space inside a substance and is measured in units such as liters or milliliters.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-ability-48277160","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","2. Distinguishing the different materials in terms of the physical properties of the substance that can be calculated or measured, such as mass, volume, density, buoyancy, color and boiling point","What is the term for the ability of an object to resist changes in its shape or volume?","Elasticity","Density","Mass","Volume","Elasticity","Elasticity is the ability of an object to resist changes in its shape or volume, but it is not directly related to the question.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-temperature-ea54dcf8","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","2. Distinguishing the different materials in terms of the physical properties of the substance that can be calculated or measured, such as mass, volume, density, buoyancy, color and boiling point","What is the term for the temperature at which a substance changes state from a liquid to a gas?","Melting point","Boiling point","Freezing point","Condensation point","Boiling point","Boiling point is the temperature at which a substance changes state from a liquid to a gas.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-amount-b9bc4f83","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","2. Distinguishing the different materials in terms of the physical properties of the substance that can be calculated or measured, such as mass, volume, density, buoyancy, color and boiling point","What is the term for the amount of matter in an object?","Mass","Volume","Density","Buoyancy","Mass","Mass is the amount of matter in an object and is measured in units such as grams or kilograms.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-amount-531fc823","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","2. Distinguishing the different materials in terms of the physical properties of the substance that can be calculated or measured, such as mass, volume, density, buoyancy, color and boiling point","What is the term for the amount of mass per unit volume of a substance?","Density","Mass","Volume","Buoyancy","Density","Density is the amount of mass per unit volume of a substance and is measured in units such as grams per cubic centimeter.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-process-0e13c7e6","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1 T1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What is the term for the process by which a solid changes directly to a gas?","Melting","Boiling","Sublimation","Condensation","Sublimation","Sublimation is the process by which a solid changes directly to a gas, without going through the liquid phase.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-mass-2041edfc","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1 T1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","1. Explaining the changes in the composition and properties of matter as a result of a chemical reaction. Concluding that the mass of the substance remains preserved during the chemical reaction and when forming mixtures.","What happens to the mass of a substance during a chemical reaction?","The mass of the substance increases","The mass of the substance decreases","The mass of the substance remains the same","The mass of the substance is lost completely","The mass of the substance remains the same","The law of conservation of mass states that matter cannot be created or destroyed in a chemical reaction, so the mass of the substance remains the same.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-difference-eb6f4e71","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1 T1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","1. Explaining the changes in the composition and properties of matter as a result of a chemical reaction. Concluding that the mass of the substance remains preserved during the chemical reaction and when forming mixtures.","What is the main difference between a mixture and a compound?","A mixture has a uniform composition, while a compound does not","A mixture can be separated into its components, while a compound cannot","A mixture has a fixed ratio of components, while a compound does not","A mixture is formed by a chemical reaction, while a compound is not","A mixture can be separated into its components, while a compound cannot","A mixture is a physical combination of two or more substances, and its components can be separated by physical means, whereas a compound is a chemical combination of two or more substances that cannot be separated by physical means.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-process-262d992c","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1 T1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What is the term for the process by which a liquid changes to a solid?","Melting","Boiling","Freezing","Condensation","Freezing","Freezing is the process by which a liquid changes to a solid, resulting in a change of state.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-particles-5a29081e","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1 T1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","1. Explaining the changes in the composition and properties of matter as a result of a chemical reaction. Concluding that the mass of the substance remains preserved during the chemical reaction and when forming mixtures.","What happens to the particles of a substance when it changes from a liquid to a solid?","The particles get closer together","The particles get farther apart","The particles start moving in a straight line","The particles stop moving altogether","The particles get closer together","When a liquid changes to a solid, the particles lose energy and start moving more slowly, resulting in a decrease in the distance between them.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-difference-f9b8451f","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1 T1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","1. Explaining the changes in the composition and properties of matter as a result of a chemical reaction. Concluding that the mass of the substance remains preserved during the chemical reaction and when forming mixtures.","What is the main difference between a physical change and a chemical change?","A physical change involves a change in state, while a chemical change involves a change in composition","A physical change involves a change in composition, while a chemical change involves a change in state","A physical change is reversible, while a chemical change is not","A physical change is irreversible, while a chemical change is reversible","A physical change involves a change in state, while a chemical change involves a change in composition","A physical change involves a change in state, such as from solid to liquid, without a change in composition, whereas a chemical change involves a change in composition, resulting in a new substance.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-amount-cdbf07d5","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1 T1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","2. Distinguishing the different materials in terms of the physical properties of the substance that can be calculated or measured, such as mass, volume, density, buoyancy, color and boiling point","What is the term for the amount of matter in an object?","Weight","Volume","Density","Mass","Mass","Mass is a measure of the amount of matter in an object, and it remains constant regardless of the object's location.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-energy-6a462be7","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1 T1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","1. Explaining the changes in the composition and properties of matter as a result of a chemical reaction. Concluding that the mass of the substance remains preserved during the chemical reaction and when forming mixtures.","What happens to the energy of the particles in a substance when it is heated?","The energy of the particles decreases","The energy of the particles remains the same","The energy of the particles increases","The energy of the particles is lost","The energy of the particles increases","When a substance is heated, the energy of the particles increases, causing them to move more rapidly.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-characteristic-5daee901","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1 T1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What is the main characteristic that distinguishes a gas from a liquid?","The shape of the particles","The volume of the particles","The ability to flow","The ability to expand and fill a container","The ability to expand and fill a container","Gases have the ability to expand and fill a container, whereas liquids take the shape of their container but have a fixed volume.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-particles-479b280d","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 1 T1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","1. Explaining the changes in the composition and properties of matter as a result of a chemical reaction. Concluding that the mass of the substance remains preserved during the chemical reaction and when forming mixtures.","What happens to the particles of a substance when it changes from a solid to a liquid?","The particles get closer together","The particles get farther apart","The particles start moving in a straight line","The particles stop moving altogether","The particles get farther apart","When a solid changes to a liquid, the particles gain energy and start moving more freely, resulting in an increase in the distance between them.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-a-9d69d549","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What happens to a liquid when it is cooled?","It turns into a gas.","It turns into a solid.","It stays the same.","It turns into a different liquid.","It turns into a solid.","When a liquid is cooled, it changes into a solid.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-a-c6de2fd6","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What happens to a solid when it is cooled?","It turns into a gas.","It turns into a liquid.","It stays the same.","It turns into ice.","It turns into ice.","When a solid is cooled, it turns into ice.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-ice-ff13bcb3","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","5. Explaining the changes of matter due to the effect of heat.","What happens to ice when it is heated?","It turns into a liquid and stays that way.","It turns into a gas and stays that way.","It changes directly into steam.","It melts into water and then turns into water vapor.","It melts into water and then turns into water vapor.","When ice is heated, it first melts into liquid water and then turns into water vapor.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-effect-of-f1abb384","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What is the effect of heat on a solid?","It becomes a liquid.","It becomes a gas.","It stays the same.","It becomes a different solid.","It becomes a liquid.","When a solid is heated, it changes into a liquid.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-water-56a18018","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What happens to water when it is heated?","It turns into ice.","It turns into steam.","It stays the same.","It turns into a liquid.","It stays the same.","Water stays the same when it is heated, but it can change from a solid (ice) to a liquid (water) or from a liquid to a gas (steam).","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-effect-of-79a3d421","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What is the effect of heat on a liquid?","It becomes a solid.","It becomes a gas.","It stays the same.","It becomes a different liquid.","It becomes a gas.","When a liquid is heated, it changes into a gas.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-steam-d67c4b1f","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What happens to steam when it is cooled?","It turns into ice.","It turns into a liquid.","It stays the same.","It turns into a different gas.","It turns into a liquid.","When steam is cooled, it turns back into a liquid.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-effect-of-7e069699","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What is the effect of heat on a gas?","It becomes a liquid.","It becomes a solid.","It stays the same.","It becomes a different gas.","It stays the same.","A gas stays the same when it is heated, but it can change from a gas to a liquid or from a gas to a solid.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-steam-078b4473","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What happens to steam when it is heated?","It turns into a liquid.","It turns into a solid.","It stays the same.","It turns into a different gas.","It stays the same.","Steam stays the same when it is heated, but it can change from a gas to a liquid.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-effect-of-d3e7de65","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What is the effect of heat on ice?","It becomes a liquid.","It becomes a gas.","It stays the same.","It becomes a different solid.","It becomes a liquid.","When ice is heated, it changes into a liquid.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-size-4b86e871","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 4","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What happens to the size of a substance when it changes from a solid to a liquid?","It becomes smaller and more compact.","It becomes larger and less compact.","It stays the same size and shape.","It disappears completely.","It becomes larger and less compact.","When a solid changes to a liquid, it becomes larger and less compact, as the molecules spread out and gain more space.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-molecules-df2b3a29","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 4","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","5. Explaining the changes of matter due to the effect of heat.","What happens to the molecules of a substance when it changes from a solid to a liquid?","The molecules start moving faster and spread out.","The molecules start moving slower and come together.","The molecules stay the same speed and distance apart.","The molecules disappear completely.","The molecules start moving faster and spread out.","When a solid changes to a liquid, the molecules gain enough energy to break free from their fixed positions and start moving faster and spreading out.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-difference-f2ae12a9","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 4","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What is the main difference between the molecules in a solid and a liquid?","The molecules in a solid are bigger than the molecules in a liquid.","The molecules in a solid are smaller than the molecules in a liquid.","The molecules in a solid are fixed in place, while the molecules in a liquid are free to move.","The molecules in a solid are moving faster than the molecules in a liquid.","The molecules in a solid are fixed in place, while the molecules in a liquid are free to move.","In a solid, the molecules are fixed in place and have a fixed position, while in a liquid, the molecules are free to move and change position.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-molecules-1021a47e","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 4","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","5. Explaining the changes of matter due to the effect of heat.","What happens to the molecules of a substance when it changes from a liquid to a gas?","The molecules start moving slower and come together.","The molecules start moving faster and spread out even more.","The molecules stay the same speed and distance apart.","The molecules disappear completely.","The molecules start moving faster and spread out even more.","When a liquid changes to a gas, the molecules gain even more energy and start moving faster and spreading out even more.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-effect-of-426886b2","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 4","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What is the effect of heat on the state of matter?","It causes the molecules to move slower and come together.","It causes the molecules to move faster and spread out.","It has no effect on the molecules.","It causes the molecules to disappear completely.","It causes the molecules to move faster and spread out.","Heat energy causes the molecules to gain energy and move faster, which can change the state of matter from solid to liquid to gas.","","",""
