"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-effect-of-a368f134","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 4","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What is the effect of cooling on the state of matter?","It causes the molecules to move faster and spread out.","It causes the molecules to move slower and come together.","It has no effect on the molecules.","It causes the molecules to disappear completely.","It causes the molecules to move slower and come together.","Cooling energy causes the molecules to lose energy and move slower, which can change the state of matter from gas to liquid to solid.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-happens-to-shape-b645c043","Science G6: Exploring the physical properties of matter - Set 4","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-1-1 Exploring the physical properties of matter, distinguishing the molecular structure of its different states, and explaining the change of matter states due to heat.","4. Comparing, through models, the states of matter (solid, liquid, and gas), and in terms of movement and forces of attraction between molecules, and the effect of that on the shape and size of matter.","What happens to the shape of a substance when it changes from a solid to a liquid?","It becomes more rigid and maintains its shape.","It becomes more flexible and changes shape.","It stays the same shape and size.","It disappears completely.","It becomes more flexible and changes shape.","When a solid changes to a liquid, it becomes more flexible and can change shape to fit its container.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-an-example-49676e3a","Science G6: Identifying the inheritance of traits, explaining - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-4-1 Identifying the inheritance of traits, explaining the variation in them, tracing their transmission from one generation to the next, distinguishing their types (dominant and recessive), and clarifying the impact of the environment on them.","5. Identifying some of the environmental factors that affect the acquired traits of animals and plants (the amount of food, the amount of water, the amount of animal movement), and identifying the traits that are affected by environmental factors (height, weight, and color).","What is an example of an environmental factor that can affect the height of a plant?","The amount of sunlight a plant receives","The type of soil a plant is grown in","The amount of water a plant receives","The temperature of the environment a plant is in","The amount of water a plant receives","The amount of water a plant receives can affect its height, as a plant that receives too little water may become stunted.","","",""
