"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-difference-f553bf4c","Science G6: Identifying the inheritance of traits, explaining - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-4-1 Identifying the inheritance of traits, explaining the variation in them, tracing their transmission from one generation to the next, distinguishing their types (dominant and recessive), and clarifying the impact of the environment on them.","4. Distinguishing genetic traits from acquired traits and comparing them.","What is the main difference between a dominant and a recessive trait?","A dominant trait is always expressed, while a recessive trait is never expressed.","A dominant trait is expressed when paired with a recessive trait, while a recessive trait is only expressed when paired with another recessive trait.","A dominant trait is expressed when paired with another dominant trait, while a recessive trait is expressed when paired with another recessive trait.","A dominant trait is never expressed, while a recessive trait is always expressed.","A dominant trait is expressed when paired with a recessive trait, while a recessive trait is only expressed when paired with another recessive trait.","A dominant trait will be expressed when paired with a recessive trait, while a recessive trait will only be expressed when paired with another recessive trait.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-an-example-40b32db4","Science G6: Identifying the inheritance of traits - Set 5","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-4-1 Identifying the inheritance of traits, explaining the variation in them, tracing their transmission from one generation to the next, distinguishing their types (dominant and recessive), and clarifying the impact of the environment on them.","5. Identifying some of the environmental factors that affect the acquired traits of animals and plants (the amount of food, the amount of water, the amount of animal movement), and identifying the traits that are affected by environmental factors (height, weight, and color).","What is an example of an acquired trait?","The color of an animal's fur.","The shape of an animal's ears.","The height of an animal after it has grown up.","The color of an animal's eyes.","The height of an animal after it has grown up.","The height of an animal after it has grown up is an example of an acquired trait.","","",""
