"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-effect-of-8237627c","Science G6: Identifying the inheritance of traits - Set 5","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-4-1 Identifying the inheritance of traits, explaining the variation in them, tracing their transmission from one generation to the next, distinguishing their types (dominant and recessive), and clarifying the impact of the environment on them.","5. Identifying some of the environmental factors that affect the acquired traits of animals and plants (the amount of food, the amount of water, the amount of animal movement), and identifying the traits that are affected by environmental factors (height, weight, and color).","What is the effect of too much animal movement on an animal's body?","It will make the animal's body stronger.","It will make the animal's body weaker.","It will make the animal's body bigger.","It will not affect the animal's body at all.","It will make the animal's body weaker.","Too much animal movement will cause an animal's body to become weaker.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-how-amount-of-a76f6a0b","Science G6: Identifying the inheritance of traits - Set 5","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-4-1 Identifying the inheritance of traits, explaining the variation in them, tracing their transmission from one generation to the next, distinguishing their types (dominant and recessive), and clarifying the impact of the environment on them.","5. Identifying some of the environmental factors that affect the acquired traits of animals and plants (the amount of food, the amount of water, the amount of animal movement), and identifying the traits that are affected by environmental factors (height, weight, and color).","How does the amount of water affect an animal's body?","It will make the animal's body bigger.","It will make the animal's body smaller.","It will make the animal's body stronger.","It will not affect the animal's body at all.","It will make the animal's body smaller.","Too little water will cause an animal's body to become smaller.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-is-it-731d2af7","Science G6: Inferring the impact of human activity on environmental - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-3-5 Inferring the impact of human activity on environmental habitats and populations, and predicting its effect, proposing solutions for their protection","3. Proposing solutions to protect the earth's resources and preserve the environment.","Why is it important to protect endangered species?","Because it helps to increase their population and habitat size.","Because it has no effect on the environment.","Because it helps to maintain the balance of ecosystems and prevent extinctions.","Because it helps to improve their hunting skills.","Because it helps to maintain the balance of ecosystems and prevent extinctions.","Protecting endangered species helps to maintain the balance of ecosystems and prevent extinctions, which can have severe impacts on the environment and human populations.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-reason-6fae3d1c","Science G6: Inferring the impact of human activity on environmental - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-3-5 Inferring the impact of human activity on environmental habitats and populations, and predicting its effect, proposing solutions for their protection","1. Explaining human interaction with environments, and inferring the positive and negative impact of human activities on the environmental habitats and populations.","What is the main reason why deforestation is a problem for the environment?","It helps to reduce the amount of greenhouse gases in the atmosphere.","It allows for more space for wildlife to live.","It leads to soil erosion and loss of biodiversity.","It helps to increase the amount of oxygen in the air.","It leads to soil erosion and loss of biodiversity.","Deforestation leads to soil erosion, which can cause landslides and floods, and also results in the loss of biodiversity as many species rely on forests for their habitats.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-impact-of-9518333c","Science G6: Inferring the impact of human activity on environmental - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-3-4 Describing the effect of environmental changes on plants and animals that live in specific environments. Inferring how behavioral and structural adaptations can help plants and animals survive in their habitats","4. Describing the climatic conditions in different environments and their impact on living organisms.","What is the impact of pollution on human health?","It has no effect on human health.","It helps to improve human health.","It leads to the spread of diseases and harm to human health.","It helps to increase the lifespan of humans.","It leads to the spread of diseases and harm to human health.","Pollution can lead to the spread of diseases and harm to human health, as pollutants can contaminate the air and water and harm the humans that live in it.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-is-it-3c65b3ec","Science G6: Inferring the impact of human activity on environmental - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-3-5 Inferring the impact of human activity on environmental habitats and populations, and predicting its effect, proposing solutions for their protection","1. Explaining human interaction with environments, and inferring the positive and negative impact of human activities on the environmental habitats and populations.","Why is it important to conserve forests?","Because it helps to increase the amount of greenhouse gases in the atmosphere.","Because it has no effect on the environment.","Because it helps to maintain the balance of ecosystems and prevent deforestation.","Because it helps to improve the water quality in rivers and lakes.","Because it helps to maintain the balance of ecosystems and prevent deforestation.","Conserving forests helps to maintain the balance of ecosystems and prevent deforestation, which can have severe impacts on the environment and human populations.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-impact-of-b7ebe0a2","Science G6: Inferring the impact of human activity on environmental - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-3-4 Describing the effect of environmental changes on plants and animals that live in specific environments. Inferring how behavioral and structural adaptations can help plants and animals survive in their habitats","4. Describing the climatic conditions in different environments and their impact on living organisms.","What is the impact of littering on the environment?","It helps to increase the amount of oxygen in the air.","It has no effect on the environment.","It leads to the pollution of waterways and harm to wildlife.","It helps to improve the water quality in rivers and lakes.","It leads to the pollution of waterways and harm to wildlife.","Littering can lead to the pollution of waterways and harm to wildlife, as litter can contaminate the water and harm the animals that live in it.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-impact-of-1a0d50a3","Science G6: Inferring the impact of human activity on environmental - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-3-4 Describing the effect of environmental changes on plants and animals that live in specific environments. Inferring how behavioral and structural adaptations can help plants and animals survive in their habitats","4. Describing the climatic conditions in different environments and their impact on living organisms.","What is the impact of pollution on aquatic life?","It helps to increase the population of aquatic animals.","It has no effect on aquatic life.","It leads to the death of many aquatic animals and the destruction of their habitats.","It helps to improve the water quality in rivers and lakes.","It leads to the death of many aquatic animals and the destruction of their habitats.","Pollution can lead to the death of many aquatic animals and the destruction of their habitats, as pollutants can contaminate the water and harm the animals that live in it.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-is-it-b95d3164","Science G6: Inferring the impact of human activity on environmental - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-3-2-1Classifying the layers of the atmosphere and identifying their components, characteristics, changes, its effects on the environment and their benefits to humans.","3. Identifying the causes of weather variability and their relationship to the Earth’s water cycle, and predicting their environmental impacts on weather.","Why is it important to conserve water?","Because it helps to increase the amount of water in the ocean.","Because it helps to reduce the amount of greenhouse gases in the atmosphere.","Because it helps to maintain the balance of the water cycle and prevent droughts.","Because it has no effect on the environment.","Because it helps to maintain the balance of the water cycle and prevent droughts.","Conserving water helps to maintain the balance of the water cycle and prevent droughts, which can have severe impacts on the environment and human populations.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-impact-of-fd2101f7","Science G6: Inferring the impact of human activity on environmental - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-3-4 Describing the effect of environmental changes on plants and animals that live in specific environments. Inferring how behavioral and structural adaptations can help plants and animals survive in their habitats","1. Identifying the physical factors that affect the survival of plants and animals in specific habitats","What is the impact of overfishing on marine ecosystems?","It helps to increase the population of fish and other marine animals.","It has no effect on marine ecosystems.","It leads to the depletion of fish populations and the destruction of marine habitats.","It helps to improve the water quality in oceans.","It leads to the depletion of fish populations and the destruction of marine habitats.","Overfishing can lead to the depletion of fish populations and the destruction of marine habitats, as many species rely on fish for food and other marine animals for their survival.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-is-it-64d16b98","Science G6: Inferring the impact of human activity on environmental - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-3-5 Inferring the impact of human activity on environmental habitats and populations, and predicting its effect, proposing solutions for their protection","3. Proposing solutions to protect the earth's resources and preserve the environment.","Why is it important to reduce, reuse, and recycle?","Because it helps to increase the amount of waste in landfills.","Because it has no effect on the environment.","Because it helps to conserve natural resources and reduce pollution.","Because it helps to increase the amount of greenhouse gases in the atmosphere.","Because it helps to conserve natural resources and reduce pollution.","Reducing, reusing, and recycling helps to conserve natural resources and reduce pollution, which can have severe impacts on the environment and human populations.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-impact-of-294bafb6","Science G6: Inferring the impact of human activity on environmental - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-3-5 Inferring the impact of human activity on environmental habitats and populations, and predicting its effect, proposing solutions for their protection","1. Explaining human interaction with environments, and inferring the positive and negative impact of human activities on the environmental habitats and populations.","What is the impact of climate change on polar bears?","It helps to increase their population and habitat size.","It has no effect on polar bears.","It leads to the decline of their population and habitat size.","It helps to improve their hunting skills.","It leads to the decline of their population and habitat size.","Climate change leads to the decline of polar bears' population and habitat size, as melting sea ice reduces their access to food and habitat.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-main-reason-da80c19c","Science G6: Inferring the impact of human activity - Set 1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-3-4 Describing the effect of environmental changes on plants and animals that live in specific environments. Inferring how behavioral and structural adaptations can help plants and animals survive in their habitats","3. Describing how structural and behavioral adaptations can help plants and animals live and survive in specific habitats.","What is the main reason why deforestation is a problem for the environment?","It provides more space for animals to live.","It helps to reduce the amount of greenhouse gases.","It leads to the loss of habitats for many species.","It increases the amount of oxygen in the air.","It leads to the loss of habitats for many species.","Deforestation leads to the loss of habitats for many species, which can cause their populations to decline or even become extinct.","","",""
