"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-of-is-an-2449d726","Science G6: Representing the relationships between living organisms - Set 2 T1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-3-3 Representing the relationships between living organisms in which matter is circulated in the ecosystem, and identifying the relationship between plants and energy obtained from the sun to produce food.","2. Classifying living organisms into (autotrophic - heterotrophic).","Which of the following is an example of a heterotrophic organism that eats plants for food?","A lion that eats other lions","A deer that eats plants for food","A tree that makes its own food from sunlight","A car that runs on gasoline","A deer that eats plants for food","A deer is a heterotroph that eats plants for food.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-why-do-heterotrophic-2b7166e9","Science G6: Representing the relationships between living organisms - Set 2 T1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-3-3 Representing the relationships between living organisms in which matter is circulated in the ecosystem, and identifying the relationship between plants and energy obtained from the sun to produce food.","2. Classifying living organisms into (autotrophic - heterotrophic).","Why do heterotrophic organisms need to eat other organisms for food?","Because they are lazy","Because they do not have the ability to make their own food","Because they want to be big and strong","Because they can fly","Because they do not have the ability to make their own food","Heterotrophic organisms need to eat other organisms for food because they do not have the ability to make their own food.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-role-of-eb3df610","Science G6: Representing the relationships between living organisms - Set 2 T1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-3-3 Representing the relationships between living organisms in which matter is circulated in the ecosystem, and identifying the relationship between plants and energy obtained from the sun to produce food.","2. Classifying living organisms into (autotrophic - heterotrophic).","What is the role of autotrophic organisms in the ecosystem?","To eat other organisms for food","To make their own food and provide food for heterotrophs","To run fast and jump high","To fly and swim","To make their own food and provide food for heterotrophs","Autotrophic organisms play a crucial role in the ecosystem by making their own food and providing food for heterotrophs.","","",""
