"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-of-is-a-b02efb47","Science G6: Representing the relationships between living organisms - Set 2 T1","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-1-3-3 Representing the relationships between living organisms in which matter is circulated in the ecosystem, and identifying the relationship between plants and energy obtained from the sun to produce food.","2. Classifying living organisms into (autotrophic - heterotrophic).","Which of the following is a characteristic of autotrophic organisms?","They eat other organisms for food","They make their own food from sunlight","They are always big and strong","They can fly and swim","They make their own food from sunlight","Autotrophic organisms are characterized by their ability to make their own food from sunlight.","","",""
