"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-how-can-you-e4c57925","Science G6: Understanding Newton's three laws of motion - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-2-2 Understanding Newton›s three laws of motion and using them to explain body motion","2. Define velocity and its unit, calculating velocity by knowing distance and time, and distinguishing between speed and velocity.","How can you calculate velocity if you know the distance an object travels and the time it takes?","Divide the distance by the time","Multiply the distance by the time","Add the distance to the time","Subtract the distance from the time","Divide the distance by the time","To calculate velocity, you need to divide the distance an object travels by the time it takes, which gives you the rate at which it moves.","/image-source/sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-how-can-you-e4c57925.png","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-unit-of-75e5e509","Science G6: Understanding Newton's three laws of motion - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-2-2 Understanding Newton›s three laws of motion and using them to explain body motion","4. Explaining Newton's three laws of motion and their real life applications.","What is the unit of velocity?","Meter","Meter per second","Second","Kilogram","Meter per second","The unit of velocity is meter per second (m/s), which represents the rate at which an object moves in a straight line.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-term-rate-bba4da21","Science G6: Understanding Newton's three laws of motion - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-2-2 Understanding Newton›s three laws of motion and using them to explain body motion","3. Defining acceleration and its unit, calculating acceleration by knowing the change in velocity and time, and showing the effect of changing the direction of movement on acceleration.","What is the term for the rate of change of velocity?","Acceleration","Deceleration","Velocity","Speed","Acceleration","The term for the rate of change of velocity is acceleration, which represents the change in velocity over time.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-difference-uniform-63423604","Science G6: Understanding Newton's three laws of motion - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-2-2 Understanding Newton›s three laws of motion and using them to explain body motion","4. Explaining Newton's three laws of motion and their real life applications.","What is the difference between uniform motion and non-uniform motion?","Uniform motion is when an object moves at a constant speed, while non-uniform motion is when an object moves at a changing speed","Uniform motion is when an object moves at a changing speed, while non-uniform motion is when an object moves at a constant speed","Uniform motion is when an object moves in a straight line, while non-uniform motion is when an object moves in a circle","Uniform motion is when an object moves in a circle, while non-uniform motion is when an object moves in a straight line","Uniform motion is when an object moves at a constant speed, while non-uniform motion is when an object moves at a changing speed","Uniform motion is when an object moves at a constant speed, while non-uniform motion is when an object moves at a changing speed.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-how-can-you-bfc509b1","Science G6: Understanding Newton's three laws of motion - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-2-2 Understanding Newton›s three laws of motion and using them to explain body motion","3. Defining acceleration and its unit, calculating acceleration by knowing the change in velocity and time, and showing the effect of changing the direction of movement on acceleration.","How can you tell if an object is moving at a constant velocity?","If its speed is changing","If its direction is changing","If it is moving in a straight line at a constant rate","If it is moving in a circle","If it is moving in a straight line at a constant rate","An object is moving at a constant velocity if it is moving in a straight line at a constant rate, with no changes in speed or direction.","/image-source/sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-how-can-you-bfc509b1.png","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-unit-of-dbf83702","Science G6: Understanding Newton's three laws of motion - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-2-2 Understanding Newton›s three laws of motion and using them to explain body motion","2. Define velocity and its unit, calculating velocity by knowing distance and time, and distinguishing between speed and velocity.","What is the unit of speed?","Meter per second","Meter","Second","Kilogram","Meter per second","The unit of speed is meter per second (m/s), which represents the rate at which an object moves in a straight line.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-if-an-object-5df42684","Science G6: Understanding Newton's three laws of motion - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-2-2 Understanding Newton›s three laws of motion and using them to explain body motion","2. Define velocity and its unit, calculating velocity by knowing distance and time, and distinguishing between speed and velocity.","If an object travels 20 meters in 4 seconds, what is its velocity?","2 meters per second","4 meters per second","5 meters per second","10 meters per second","5 meters per second","To calculate velocity, you need to divide the distance by the time, which gives you 20 meters / 4 seconds = 5 meters per second.","/image-source/sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-if-an-object-5df42684.png","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-formula-to-88cf3074","Science G6: Understanding Newton's three laws of motion - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-2-2 Understanding Newton›s three laws of motion and using them to explain body motion","2. Define velocity and its unit, calculating velocity by knowing distance and time, and distinguishing between speed and velocity.","What is the formula to calculate velocity?","v = d/t","v = t/d","v = d x t","v = t - d","v = d/t","The formula to calculate velocity is v = d/t, where v is velocity, d is distance, and t is time.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-velocity-e2736eb7","Science G6: Understanding Newton's three laws of motion - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-2-2 Understanding Newton›s three laws of motion and using them to explain body motion","2. Define velocity and its unit, calculating velocity by knowing distance and time, and distinguishing between speed and velocity.","What is velocity?","The rate at which an object changes direction","The rate at which an object moves in a straight line","The speed of an object in a specific direction","The distance an object travels in a given time","The speed of an object in a specific direction","Velocity is the rate at which an object moves in a specific direction, taking into account both speed and direction.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-difference-speed-cc7c6e62","Science G6: Understanding Newton's three laws of motion - Set 2","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-2-2 Understanding Newton›s three laws of motion and using them to explain body motion","2. Define velocity and its unit, calculating velocity by knowing distance and time, and distinguishing between speed and velocity.","What is the difference between speed and velocity?","Speed is a measure of distance, while velocity is a measure of time","Speed is a measure of time, while velocity is a measure of distance","Speed is a measure of how fast an object moves, while velocity is a measure of its direction","Speed is a measure of an object's direction, while velocity is a measure of its speed","Speed is a measure of how fast an object moves, while velocity is a measure of its direction","Speed is a measure of how fast an object moves, while velocity is a measure of its direction, taking into account both speed and direction.","","",""
"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-how-can-you-cea59276","Science G6: Understanding Newton's three laws of motion - Set 3","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-2-2 Understanding Newton›s three laws of motion and using them to explain body motion","3. Defining acceleration and its unit, calculating acceleration by knowing the change in velocity and time, and showing the effect of changing the direction of movement on acceleration.","How can you calculate acceleration?","By knowing the distance traveled and time taken.","By knowing the change in velocity and time taken.","By knowing the force applied and mass of the object.","By knowing the speed and direction of the object.","By knowing the change in velocity and time taken.","Acceleration can be calculated by knowing the change in velocity and time taken.","/image-source/sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-how-can-you-cea59276.png","",""
