"sci-g6-6-5-1-2-1-is-effect-of-11917b28","Science G6: Understanding Newton's three laws of motion - Set 3","Science","6","Assessment for Grade 6 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","6-5-2-2-2 Understanding Newton›s three laws of motion and using them to explain body motion","3. Defining acceleration and its unit, calculating acceleration by knowing the change in velocity and time, and showing the effect of changing the direction of movement on acceleration.","What is the effect of decreasing the time taken on an object's acceleration?","Acceleration decreases.","Acceleration remains the same.","Acceleration increases.","Acceleration becomes zero.","Acceleration increases.","Decreasing the time taken increases an object's acceleration.","","",""
