"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-different-295622d8","Science G9: Describing the development of genetics, and - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-4-1 Describing the development of genetics, and the use of Mendelian laws to explain the inheritance of genetic traits, and the probabilities of their appearance in different generations.","1. Distinguishing the structure of the chromosome, and the relationship between its components. Explaining the concept of a gene, identifying its components and its location on the chromosome, and explains the occurrence of genetic mutation and its effects on making protein in the cell.","What is the term for the different forms of a gene?","Genetic traits","Alleles","Genetic mutations","Genetic variations","Alleles","Alleles are the different forms of a gene that can occupy a specific position on a chromosome.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-law-of-c1439d30","Science G9: Describing the development of genetics, and - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-7 Explaining how atoms bond with each other, identifying what is a chemical bond and how it is formed, and distinguishing between different types","2. Describes the states of the outer electron level (valence electrons) through the periodic chemical properties of elements within the same group.","What is the law of segregation in genetics?","The law of independent assortment","The law of segregation","The law of dominance","The law of incomplete dominance","The law of segregation","The law of segregation states that each pair of alleles separates from each other during gamete formation.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-role-of-3f2ec4a5","Science G9: Describing the development of genetics, and - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-4-1 Describing the development of genetics, and the use of Mendelian laws to explain the inheritance of genetic traits, and the probabilities of their appearance in different generations.","4. Distinguishing between homozygous and heterozygous genes, distinguish between homozygous genes organisms and non- homozygous organisms, and providing an example of each.","What is the role of the dominant allele in genetics?","It is always expressed","It is never expressed","It is expressed if the individual is homozygous for the allele","It is expressed if the individual is heterozygous for the allele","It is expressed if the individual is heterozygous for the allele","A dominant allele is expressed if the individual is heterozygous for the allele, meaning they have one copy of the dominant allele and one copy of the recessive allele.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-law-of-4e49f251","Science G9: Describing the development of genetics, and - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-4-1 Describing the development of genetics, and the use of Mendelian laws to explain the inheritance of genetic traits, and the probabilities of their appearance in different generations.","4. Distinguishing between homozygous and heterozygous genes, distinguish between homozygous genes organisms and non- homozygous organisms, and providing an example of each.","What is the law of independent assortment in genetics?","The law of segregation","The law of independent assortment","The law of dominance","The law of incomplete dominance","The law of independent assortment","The law of independent assortment states that alleles for different genes separate independently of each other during gamete formation.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-combination-b9bc7f6b","Science G9: Describing the development of genetics, and - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-4-1 Describing the development of genetics, and the use of Mendelian laws to explain the inheritance of genetic traits, and the probabilities of their appearance in different generations.","3. Clarifying the concept of genetics and its principles and explaining how traits are inherited, and explaining the role of alleles.","What is the term for the combination of two alleles in an individual?","Genotype","Phenotype","Genetic trait","Allele combination","Genotype","Genotype refers to the combination of two alleles in an individual, while phenotype refers to the physical expression of the genotype.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-role-of-e5243696","Science G9: Describing the development of genetics, and - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-4-1 Describing the development of genetics, and the use of Mendelian laws to explain the inheritance of genetic traits, and the probabilities of their appearance in different generations.","4. Distinguishing between homozygous and heterozygous genes, distinguish between homozygous genes organisms and non- homozygous organisms, and providing an example of each.","What is the role of the recessive allele in genetics?","It is always expressed","It is never expressed","It is expressed if the individual is homozygous for the allele","It is expressed if the individual is heterozygous for the allele","It is expressed if the individual is homozygous for the allele","A recessive allele is expressed if the individual is homozygous for the allele, meaning they have two copies of the recessive allele.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-probability-of-16a85fc5","Science G9: Describing the development of genetics, and - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-4-1 Describing the development of genetics, and the use of Mendelian laws to explain the inheritance of genetic traits, and the probabilities of their appearance in different generations.","2. Applying Mendel's first and second law for the transmission of genetic traits, and predicting the emergence of genetic traits in generations and their occurrence ratio.","What is the probability of two independent events occurring?","The probability of the first event multiplied by the probability of the second event","The probability of the first event plus the probability of the second event","The probability of the first event minus the probability of the second event","The probability of the first event divided by the probability of the second event","The probability of the first event multiplied by the probability of the second event","The probability of two independent events occurring is the product of the probabilities of each individual event.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-difference-a-c9c23c74","Science G9: Describing the development of genetics, and - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-4-1 Describing the development of genetics, and the use of Mendelian laws to explain the inheritance of genetic traits, and the probabilities of their appearance in different generations.","4. Distinguishing between homozygous and heterozygous genes, distinguish between homozygous genes organisms and non- homozygous organisms, and providing an example of each.","What is the difference between a homozygous and a heterozygous organism?","A homozygous organism has two copies of the same allele, while a heterozygous organism has two different alleles","A homozygous organism has two different alleles, while a heterozygous organism has two copies of the same allele","A homozygous organism has one dominant and one recessive allele, while a heterozygous organism has two copies of the same allele","A homozygous organism has no alleles, while a heterozygous organism has two different alleles","A homozygous organism has two copies of the same allele, while a heterozygous organism has two different alleles","A homozygous organism has two copies of the same allele, while a heterozygous organism has two different alleles.","","",""
