"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-probability-of-1c87428a","Science G9: Describing the development of genetics - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-4-1 Describing the development of genetics, and the use of Mendelian laws to explain the inheritance of genetic traits, and the probabilities of their appearance in different generations.","3. Clarifying the concept of genetics and its principles and explaining how traits are inherited, and explaining the role of alleles.","What is the probability of a trait being expressed if both parents are heterozygous?","25%","50%","75%","100%","75%","For a heterozygous-by-heterozygous cross, the expected phenotype ratio is 3 dominant to 1 recessive, so 75% show the dominant phenotype.","/image-source/sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-probability-of-1c87428a.png","",""
