"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-probability-of-6dc50f24","Science G9: Describing the development of genetics - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-4-1 Describing the development of genetics, and the use of Mendelian laws to explain the inheritance of genetic traits, and the probabilities of their appearance in different generations.","4. Distinguishing between homozygous and heterozygous genes, distinguish between homozygous genes organisms and non- homozygous organisms, and providing an example of each.","What is the probability of a trait being expressed if one parent is homozygous dominant and the other is heterozygous?","25%","50%","75%","100%","100%","A homozygous dominant parent passes a dominant allele to every offspring, so all offspring are expected to show the dominant phenotype.","","",""
