"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-happens-to-rate-ace1691a","Science G9: Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-9 Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying the factors affecting them","2. Determining the factors affecting the rate of a chemical reaction (concentration of reactants, concentration of reactants, pressure, temperature, catalyst).","What happens to the rate of a chemical reaction when the temperature increases?","It decreases","It stays the same","It increases","It remains constant","It increases","The rate of a chemical reaction increases when the temperature increases.","/image-source/sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-happens-to-rate-ace1691a.png","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-amount-70213f77","Science G9: Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-9 Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying the factors affecting them","2. Determining the factors affecting the rate of a chemical reaction (concentration of reactants, concentration of reactants, pressure, temperature, catalyst).","What is the term for the amount of substance that reacts in a given time?","Rate of reaction","Amount of substance","Molar concentration","Mole fraction","Rate of reaction","Rate of reaction is the term for the amount of substance that reacts in a given time.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-effect-of-679a672b","Science G9: Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-9 Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying the factors affecting them","2. Determining the factors affecting the rate of a chemical reaction (concentration of reactants, concentration of reactants, pressure, temperature, catalyst).","What is the effect of increasing the surface area of a reactant on the rate of a chemical reaction?","It decreases","It stays the same","It increases","It remains constant","It increases","The rate of a chemical reaction increases when the surface area of a reactant increases.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-main-factor-f2455e82","Science G9: Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-9 Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying the factors affecting them","2. Determining the factors affecting the rate of a chemical reaction (concentration of reactants, concentration of reactants, pressure, temperature, catalyst).","What is the main factor that affects the rate of a chemical reaction?","Temperature","Pressure","Concentration","Time","Temperature","Temperature is the main factor that affects the rate of a chemical reaction.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-energy-e4ecc079","Science G9: Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-4-4 Distinguishing between the kinetic and potential energy of a body and the factors affecting them.","3. Calculating the kinetic and potential energy of objects, and deducing the relationship between them.","What is the term for the energy of motion of particles in a substance?","Kinetic energy","Potential energy","Thermal energy","Mechanical energy","Kinetic energy","Kinetic energy is the energy of motion. The motion of particles in a substance is related to their kinetic energy.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-effect-of-47ae3196","Science G9: Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-9 Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying the factors affecting them","2. Determining the factors affecting the rate of a chemical reaction (concentration of reactants, concentration of reactants, pressure, temperature, catalyst).","What is the effect of decreasing the pressure of a reactant on the rate of a chemical reaction?","It decreases","It stays the same","It increases","It remains constant","It increases","The rate of a chemical reaction increases when the pressure of a reactant decreases.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-main-factor-5954ce6b","Science G9: Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-9 Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying the factors affecting them","2. Determining the factors affecting the rate of a chemical reaction (concentration of reactants, concentration of reactants, pressure, temperature, catalyst).","What is the main factor that affects the rate of a chemical reaction when the concentration of reactants is increased?","The pressure of the reactants increases.","The particles of the reactants gain more kinetic energy.","The catalyst is more effective at higher concentrations.","The rate of the reaction increases.","The particles of the reactants gain more kinetic energy.","When the concentration of reactants is increased, there are more particles available to collide and react, resulting in an increase in the rate of the chemical reaction.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-effect-of-c6f15328","Science G9: Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-9 Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying the factors affecting them","2. Determining the factors affecting the rate of a chemical reaction (concentration of reactants, concentration of reactants, pressure, temperature, catalyst).","What is the effect of decreasing the temperature on the rate of a chemical reaction?","The rate of the reaction increases slightly.","The rate of the reaction remains the same.","The rate of the reaction decreases slightly.","The rate of the reaction is not affected by temperature.","The rate of the reaction decreases slightly.","When the temperature is decreased, the particles of the reactants gain less kinetic energy, resulting in fewer and less energetic collisions, which decreases the rate of the chemical reaction.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-effect-of-faa49b54","Science G9: Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-9 Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying the factors affecting them","2. Determining the factors affecting the rate of a chemical reaction (concentration of reactants, concentration of reactants, pressure, temperature, catalyst).","What is the effect of increasing the pressure on the rate of a chemical reaction?","The rate of the reaction decreases slightly.","The rate of the reaction increases slightly.","The rate of the reaction remains the same.","The rate of the reaction is not affected by pressure.","The rate of the reaction increases slightly.","For reactions involving gases, increasing the pressure can increase the frequency of collisions between particles, resulting in an increase in the rate of the chemical reaction.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-role-of-0a94cfda","Science G9: Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-9 Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying the factors affecting them","3. Explaining the concept of activation energy and its role in the rate of reaction and providing an example of it.","What is the role of a catalyst in a chemical reaction?","A catalyst is a substance that slows down the rate of a chemical reaction.","A catalyst is a substance that increases the rate of a chemical reaction.","A catalyst is a substance that changes the products of a chemical reaction.","A catalyst is a substance that is consumed during a chemical reaction.","A catalyst is a substance that increases the rate of a chemical reaction.","A catalyst is a substance that increases the rate of a chemical reaction by lowering the activation energy required for the reaction to occur, without being consumed or altered in the process.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-happens-to-rate-dd756f4c","Science G9: Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-9 Describing the speed of chemical reactions and identifying the factors affecting them","2. Determining the factors affecting the rate of a chemical reaction (concentration of reactants, concentration of reactants, pressure, temperature, catalyst).","What happens to the rate of a chemical reaction when the concentration of reactants is doubled?","The rate of the reaction remains the same.","The rate of the reaction decreases slightly.","The rate of the reaction increases slightly.","The rate of the reaction doubles.","The rate of the reaction doubles.","When the concentration of reactants is doubled, there are more particles available to collide and react, resulting in an increase in the rate of the chemical reaction.","/image-source/sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-happens-to-rate-dd756f4c.png","",""
