"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-process-87c46d8e","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout - Set 4","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","4. Comparing alpha and beta particles, explaining the changes that occur in the nucleus upon emission of each of them, and their uses in life, explaining the concept of decay rate (half-life), and calculating the half-life of some isotopes.","What is the term for the process by which a nucleus emits a beta particle?","Beta decay is the process by which a nucleus emits a beta particle.","Alpha decay is the process by which a nucleus emits a beta particle.","Radioactive decay is the process by which a nucleus emits a beta particle.","Nuclear decay is the process by which a nucleus emits a beta particle.","Radioactive decay is the process by which a nucleus emits a beta particle.","Beta decay changes a neutron into a proton (or a proton into a neutron in beta-plus decay) and emits a beta particle.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-amount-29eb21f3","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout - Set 4","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","4. Comparing alpha and beta particles, explaining the changes that occur in the nucleus upon emission of each of them, and their uses in life, explaining the concept of decay rate (half-life), and calculating the half-life of some isotopes.","What is the term for the amount of time it takes for half of the original amount of a radioactive substance to decay?","Decay rate is the amount of time it takes for half of the original amount of a substance to decay.","Half-life is the amount of time it takes for half of the original amount of a substance to decay.","Radioactive half-life is the amount of time it takes for half of the original amount of a substance to decay.","The decay rate is the amount of time it takes for a substance to become stable.","Half-life is the amount of time it takes for half of the original amount of a substance to decay.","Half-life is the amount of time it takes for half of the original amount of a substance to decay.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-process-e7f972ae","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout - Set 4","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","4. Comparing alpha and beta particles, explaining the changes that occur in the nucleus upon emission of each of them, and their uses in life, explaining the concept of decay rate (half-life), and calculating the half-life of some isotopes.","What is the term for the process by which a radioactive nucleus emits an alpha particle?","Beta decay is the process by which a nucleus emits an alpha particle.","Alpha decay is the process by which a nucleus emits an alpha particle.","Radioactive decay is the process by which a nucleus emits an alpha particle.","Nuclear decay is the process by which a nucleus emits an alpha particle.","Alpha decay is the process by which a nucleus emits an alpha particle.","Alpha decay is the process by which a nucleus emits an alpha particle.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-total-f717ce22","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","2. Illustrating the components of the atom's nucleus (protons and neutrons) and their properties, describing the movement of electrons (electronic cloud) around the nucleus, and determining the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in the atom of the elements based on their atomic numbers.","What is the term for the total number of protons and neutrons in an atom's nucleus?","Atomic mass","Mass number","Proton count","Nuclear count","Mass number","The mass number is the total number of protons and neutrons in an atom's nucleus.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-main-difference-df021f46","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","2. Illustrating the components of the atom's nucleus (protons and neutrons) and their properties, describing the movement of electrons (electronic cloud) around the nucleus, and determining the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in the atom of the elements based on their atomic numbers.","What is the main difference between an isotope and an element?","Isotopes of the same element have the same number of protons but different numbers of neutrons.","Isotopes of the same element have different numbers of protons but the same number of neutrons.","Isotopes are different elements with the same mass number.","Isotopes are elements with no neutrons.","Isotopes of the same element have the same number of protons but different numbers of neutrons.","Isotopes are atoms of the same element, so they have the same number of protons, but they have different numbers of neutrons.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-main-function-5223c6c4","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","2. Illustrating the components of the atom's nucleus (protons and neutrons) and their properties, describing the movement of electrons (electronic cloud) around the nucleus, and determining the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in the atom of the elements based on their atomic numbers.","What is the main function of electrons in an atom?","To hold the nucleus together","To carry a positive charge","To carry a negative charge","To orbit the nucleus","To orbit the nucleus","Electrons carry a negative charge and orbit the nucleus of an atom.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-happens-to-number-8108a0eb","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","2. Illustrating the components of the atom's nucleus (protons and neutrons) and their properties, describing the movement of electrons (electronic cloud) around the nucleus, and determining the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in the atom of the elements based on their atomic numbers.","What happens to the number of protons in an atom when it is ionized?","It increases","It decreases","It remains the same","It becomes zero","It decreases","When an atom is ionized, the number of protons remains the same.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-main-difference-b41e923a","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","2. Illustrating the components of the atom's nucleus (protons and neutrons) and their properties, describing the movement of electrons (electronic cloud) around the nucleus, and determining the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in the atom of the elements based on their atomic numbers.","What is the main difference between protons and neutrons in an atom?","Protons are heavier than neutrons","Protons have a positive charge, while neutrons have a negative charge","Protons have a positive charge, while neutrons have no charge","Protons are smaller than neutrons","Protons have a positive charge, while neutrons have no charge","Protons have a positive charge, while neutrons have no charge.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-number-dae9c714","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","2. Illustrating the components of the atom's nucleus (protons and neutrons) and their properties, describing the movement of electrons (electronic cloud) around the nucleus, and determining the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in the atom of the elements based on their atomic numbers.","What is the term for the number of electrons in a neutral atom?","Atomic mass","Atomic number","Mass number","Electron count","Atomic number","The atomic number is also the number of electrons in a neutral atom.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-are-two-main-4a7ea79a","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","2. Illustrating the components of the atom's nucleus (protons and neutrons) and their properties, describing the movement of electrons (electronic cloud) around the nucleus, and determining the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in the atom of the elements based on their atomic numbers.","What are the two main subatomic particles found in the nucleus of an atom?","Protons and electrons","Protons and neutrons","Neutrons and electrons","Hydrogen and oxygen","Protons and neutrons","Protons and neutrons are found in the nucleus of an atom, while electrons are found in the electronic cloud.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-region-c7ca1677","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","2. Illustrating the components of the atom's nucleus (protons and neutrons) and their properties, describing the movement of electrons (electronic cloud) around the nucleus, and determining the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in the atom of the elements based on their atomic numbers.","What is the term for the region around the nucleus of an atom where electrons are found?","Atomic cloud","Electronic cloud","Proton cloud","Nuclear cloud","Electronic cloud","The electronic cloud is the region around the nucleus of an atom where electrons are found.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-an-1f8bfdd3","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-7 Explaining how atoms bond with each other, identifying what is a chemical bond and how it is formed, and distinguishing between different types","5. Distinguishing between an ion, a molecule, a compound, and give examples for each one, explaining what is meant by a chemical formula, and its indication through various examples.","What is the term for an atom that has gained or lost electrons?","Ion","Molecule","Compound","Element","Ion","An ion is an atom that has gained or lost electrons.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-number-of-05312c59","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","2. Illustrating the components of the atom's nucleus (protons and neutrons) and their properties, describing the movement of electrons (electronic cloud) around the nucleus, and determining the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in the atom of the elements based on their atomic numbers.","What is the number of protons in an atom's nucleus called?","Atomic mass","Atomic number","Mass number","Proton count","Atomic number","The atomic number is the number of protons in an atom's nucleus.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-main-difference-76b6fec8","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","3. Defining isotopes, providing an example of them, comparing isotopes of an element according to mass and atomic numbers, explaining the meaning of radioactive decay, and how it occurs, and differentiating between it and radioactive transformation.","What is the main difference between radioactive decay and radioactive transformation?","Radioactive decay involves a change in the number of protons, while radioactive transformation involves a change in the number of neutrons","Radioactive decay involves the emission of radiation, while radioactive transformation involves the absorption of radiation","Radioactive decay is a spontaneous process, while radioactive transformation is an induced process","Radioactive decay results in a more stable atom, while radioactive transformation results in a less stable atom","Radioactive decay is a spontaneous process, while radioactive transformation is an induced process","Radioactive decay is a spontaneous process where unstable atoms lose energy and stability, while radioactive transformation can be either spontaneous or induced, depending on the context, but the key distinction lies in the spontaneity of the decay process itself.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-mass-number-f30c4ab0","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","2. Illustrating the components of the atom's nucleus (protons and neutrons) and their properties, describing the movement of electrons (electronic cloud) around the nucleus, and determining the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in the atom of the elements based on their atomic numbers.","How does the mass number of an isotope relate to its atomic mass?","The mass number is equal to the atomic mass","The mass number is less than the atomic mass","The mass number is greater than the atomic mass","The mass number is the sum of the protons and neutrons, which approximates the atomic mass","The mass number is the sum of the protons and neutrons, which approximates the atomic mass","The mass number of an isotope is the sum of its protons and neutrons, which gives an approximate value of its atomic mass, considering that the mass of a neutron is slightly greater than that of a proton.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-radioactive-decay-b0883d9a","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","4. Comparing alpha and beta particles, explaining the changes that occur in the nucleus upon emission of each of them, and their uses in life, explaining the concept of decay rate (half-life), and calculating the half-life of some isotopes.","What is radioactive decay?","The process by which an atom gains protons","The process by which an atom loses energy","The process by which an unstable atom loses energy and stability by emitting radiation","The process by which an atom becomes more stable by gaining neutrons","The process by which an unstable atom loses energy and stability by emitting radiation","Radioactive decay is the process where unstable atoms lose energy and stability, resulting in the emission of radiation, such as alpha, beta, or gamma rays.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-do-isotopes-7813fecf","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","3. Defining isotopes, providing an example of them, comparing isotopes of an element according to mass and atomic numbers, explaining the meaning of radioactive decay, and how it occurs, and differentiating between it and radioactive transformation.","How do isotopes of the same element compare in terms of atomic number?","They have different atomic numbers","They have the same atomic number but different mass numbers","They have different mass numbers but the same atomic number","They have neither the same atomic number nor the same mass number","They have different mass numbers but the same atomic number","Isotopes of the same element have the same number of protons, which means they have the same atomic number, but they differ in the number of neutrons, resulting in different mass numbers.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-an-isotope-78d8f393","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","2. Illustrating the components of the atom's nucleus (protons and neutrons) and their properties, describing the movement of electrons (electronic cloud) around the nucleus, and determining the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in the atom of the elements based on their atomic numbers.","What is an isotope of an element?","An atom with a different number of protons in its nucleus","An atom with the same number of protons but a different number of neutrons in its nucleus","A molecule composed of two or more different elements","A compound made up of two or more isotopes of the same element","An atom with the same number of protons but a different number of neutrons in its nucleus","Isotopes are atoms of the same element that have the same number of protons in their nucleus but differ in the number of neutrons, resulting in different masses.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-of-is-an-2c9f43d4","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","2. Illustrating the components of the atom's nucleus (protons and neutrons) and their properties, describing the movement of electrons (electronic cloud) around the nucleus, and determining the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in the atom of the elements based on their atomic numbers.","Which of the following is an example of an isotope?","Oxygen with 8 protons and 8 neutrons","Oxygen with 8 protons and 9 neutrons","Nitrogen with 7 protons and 7 neutrons","Carbon with 6 protons and 8 neutrons","Oxygen with 8 protons and 9 neutrons","This option shows oxygen with a different number of neutrons, making it an isotope of oxygen.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-result-of-57acf92b","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","3. Defining isotopes, providing an example of them, comparing isotopes of an element according to mass and atomic numbers, explaining the meaning of radioactive decay, and how it occurs, and differentiating between it and radioactive transformation.","What is the result of radioactive decay in terms of the stability of the atom?","The atom becomes less stable","The atom becomes more stable","The atom remains stable","The atom becomes neutral","The atom becomes more stable","Radioactive decay is a process where unstable atoms lose energy and become more stable by emitting radiation, thus moving towards a more stable state.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-why-do-isotopes-b1fda375","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","2. Illustrating the components of the atom's nucleus (protons and neutrons) and their properties, describing the movement of electrons (electronic cloud) around the nucleus, and determining the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in the atom of the elements based on their atomic numbers.","Why do isotopes undergo radioactive decay?","Because they have too many protons in their nucleus","Because they have too few neutrons in their nucleus","Because they are unstable and have excess energy","Because they are stable and have a balanced number of protons and neutrons","Because they are unstable and have excess energy","Isotopes undergo radioactive decay because they are unstable, having an imbalance in the number of protons and neutrons, which leads to excess energy that is released through radiation.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-happens-to-atomic-dede08ff","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","4. Comparing alpha and beta particles, explaining the changes that occur in the nucleus upon emission of each of them, and their uses in life, explaining the concept of decay rate (half-life), and calculating the half-life of some isotopes.","What happens to the atomic number of an atom during radioactive decay?","It increases by one","It decreases by one","It remains the same","It changes randomly","It decreases by one","During certain types of radioactive decay, such as beta decay, the atomic number can change, but in the case of alpha decay, the atomic number decreases by two, and in beta decay, it can either increase or decrease by one, depending on the type of beta decay.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-of-statements-isotopes-eec018be","Science G9: Explaining the development of the atomic - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-1 Explaining the development of the atomic model throughout history, and understanding the structure and components of the atom.","2. Illustrating the components of the atom's nucleus (protons and neutrons) and their properties, describing the movement of electrons (electronic cloud) around the nucleus, and determining the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in the atom of the elements based on their atomic numbers.","Which of the following statements about isotopes is true?","Isotopes of the same element have different chemical properties","Isotopes of the same element have the same chemical properties but different physical properties","Isotopes of the same element have different physical properties but the same chemical properties","Isotopes of the same element have neither the same chemical nor the same physical properties","Isotopes of the same element have the same chemical properties but different physical properties","Isotopes of the same element have the same number of protons, which determines their chemical properties, but they differ in the number of neutrons, affecting their physical properties, such as mass.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-do-species-bf5fc047","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","How do species' abilities to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affect their ability to migrate?","It allows species to migrate more easily to new habitats, increasing their range.","It prevents species from migrating to new habitats, limiting their range.","It has no impact on species' ability to migrate as they are either adapted or not.","It leads to the extinction of species that are unable to adapt and migrate.","It allows species to migrate more easily to new habitats, increasing their range.","Species that can adapt to diverse environmental conditions are able to migrate more easily to new habitats, increasing their range.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-do-species-a93e4d39","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","How do species' abilities to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affect their ability to evolve?","It allows species to evolve more quickly in response to changing environmental conditions.","It prevents species from evolving in response to changing environmental conditions.","It has no impact on species' ability to evolve as they are either adapted or not.","It leads to the extinction of species that are unable to adapt and evolve.","It allows species to evolve more quickly in response to changing environmental conditions.","Species that can adapt to diverse environmental conditions are able to evolve more quickly in response to changing environmental conditions.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-impact-of-aac7a651","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","What is the impact of species' ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on ecosystem resilience?","It increases ecosystem resilience as species are able to adapt to changing conditions.","It decreases ecosystem resilience as species become specialized to specific environments.","It has no impact on ecosystem resilience as species are either adapted or not.","It leads to the extinction of species that are unable to adapt, disrupting ecosystem resilience.","It increases ecosystem resilience as species are able to adapt to changing conditions.","Species that can adapt to diverse environmental conditions are able to increase ecosystem resilience as they are able to adapt to changing conditions.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-do-species-e97d757c","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","1. inferring the impact of biodiversity on species survival and the sustainability of ecosystems.","How do species' abilities to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affect their ability to interact with other species?","It allows species to interact more effectively with other species, increasing their chances of survival.","It prevents species from interacting with other species, limiting their chances of survival.","It has no impact on species' ability to interact with other species as they are either adapted or not.","It leads to the extinction of species that are unable to adapt and interact with other species.","It allows species to interact more effectively with other species, increasing their chances of survival.","Species that can adapt to diverse environmental conditions are able to interact more effectively with other species, increasing their chances of survival.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-role-of-45dc24ee","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","What is the role of adaptation in maintaining ecosystem balance?","Adaptation allows species to compete more effectively for resources, leading to ecosystem imbalance.","Adaptation enables species to occupy specific niches, maintaining ecosystem balance.","Adaptation has no impact on ecosystem balance as species are either adapted or not.","Adaptation leads to the extinction of species that are unable to adapt, disrupting ecosystem balance.","Adaptation enables species to occupy specific niches, maintaining ecosystem balance.","Adaptation allows species to occupy specific niches, which helps to maintain ecosystem balance.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-do-species-dff52f06","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","How do species' abilities to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affect biodiversity?","It leads to a decrease in biodiversity as species become specialized to specific environments.","It allows species to occupy a wider range of habitats, increasing biodiversity.","It has no impact on biodiversity as species are either adapted or not.","It leads to an increase in invasive species, threatening native biodiversity.","It allows species to occupy a wider range of habitats, increasing biodiversity.","Species that can adapt to diverse environmental conditions are able to occupy a wider range of habitats, which increases biodiversity.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-main-reason-29816120","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","What is the main reason why some species are able to thrive in diverse environments?","Their ability to adapt to changing conditions allows them to survive and reproduce.","Their physical characteristics make them well-suited to specific environments.","Their behavior plays a key role in their ability to adapt to different ecosystems.","Their genetic makeup determines their ability to adapt to diverse conditions.","Their ability to adapt to changing conditions allows them to survive and reproduce.","Species that can adapt to changing conditions are able to survive and reproduce, which helps to maintain biodiversity.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-do-changes-313b275f","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","How do changes in species' abilities to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affect local ecosystems?","It leads to a decrease in local biodiversity as species become specialized to specific environments.","It allows species to occupy a wider range of habitats, increasing local biodiversity.","It has no impact on local biodiversity as species are either adapted or not.","It leads to an increase in invasive species, threatening native local biodiversity.","It allows species to occupy a wider range of habitats, increasing local biodiversity.","Species that can adapt to diverse environmental conditions are able to occupy a wider range of habitats, which increases local biodiversity.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-impact-of-d223eabe","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","What is the impact of species' ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on global ecosystems?","It leads to a decrease in global biodiversity as species become specialized to specific environments.","It allows species to occupy a wider range of habitats, increasing global biodiversity.","It has no impact on global biodiversity as species are either adapted or not.","It leads to an increase in invasive species, threatening native global biodiversity.","It allows species to occupy a wider range of habitats, increasing global biodiversity.","Species that can adapt to diverse environmental conditions are able to occupy a wider range of habitats, which increases global biodiversity.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-role-of-0df77955","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","1. inferring the impact of biodiversity on species survival and the sustainability of ecosystems.","What is the role of adaptation in species' ability to respond to environmental changes?","Adaptation allows species to respond more effectively to environmental changes, increasing their chances of survival.","Adaptation prevents species from responding to environmental changes, leading to extinction.","Adaptation has no impact on species' ability to respond to environmental changes as they are either adapted or not.","Adaptation leads to the extinction of species that are unable to adapt and respond to environmental changes.","Adaptation allows species to respond more effectively to environmental changes, increasing their chances of survival.","Adaptation allows species to respond more effectively to environmental changes, increasing their chances of survival.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-role-of-e9320550","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","3. inferring the consequences of the extinction of certain species of living organisms and its impact on biodiversity in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, proposes possible solutions to address a problem that threatens biodiversity in the local environment, and explains the national efforts made to reduce the extinction of endangered species .","What is the role of conservation efforts in maintaining biodiversity?","It has no impact on biodiversity.","It leads to a decrease in biodiversity.","It can help to maintain biodiversity by protecting habitats and reducing pollution.","It causes an increase in the number of invasive species.","It can help to maintain biodiversity by protecting habitats and reducing pollution.","Conservation efforts can help to maintain biodiversity by protecting habitats and reducing pollution.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-impact-of-c84eec75","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","What is the impact of invasive species on native species?","It has no impact on native species.","It leads to an increase in the number of native species.","It can lead to a decrease in the number of native species and a loss of ecosystem services.","It causes an increase in the number of native species.","It can lead to a decrease in the number of native species and a loss of ecosystem services.","Invasive species can lead to a decrease in the number of native species and a loss of ecosystem services.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-loss-of-d2b70484","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","How does the loss of pollinators affect ecosystems?","It has no impact on ecosystems.","It leads to an increase in the number of species.","It can lead to a decrease in the number of species and a loss of ecosystem services.","It causes an increase in the number of invasive species.","It can lead to a decrease in the number of species and a loss of ecosystem services.","The loss of pollinators can lead to a decrease in the number of species and a loss of ecosystem services.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-impact-of-ca1c4aee","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","3. inferring the consequences of the extinction of certain species of living organisms and its impact on biodiversity in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, proposes possible solutions to address a problem that threatens biodiversity in the local environment, and explains the national efforts made to reduce the extinction of endangered species .","What is the impact of habitat destruction on biodiversity?","It has no impact on biodiversity.","It leads to an increase in biodiversity.","It can lead to a decrease in biodiversity through the loss of habitats and the extinction of species.","It causes an increase in the number of invasive species.","It can lead to a decrease in biodiversity through the loss of habitats and the extinction of species.","Habitat destruction can lead to a decrease in biodiversity through the loss of habitats and the extinction of species.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-introduction-of-5a0374bf","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","How does the introduction of non-native species affect ecosystems?","It has no impact on ecosystems.","It leads to an increase in the number of species.","It can lead to a decrease in the number of species and a loss of ecosystem services.","It causes an increase in the number of invasive species.","It can lead to a decrease in the number of species and a loss of ecosystem services.","The introduction of non-native species can lead to a decrease in the number of species and a loss of ecosystem services.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-main-reason-115b456c","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","1. inferring the impact of biodiversity on species survival and the sustainability of ecosystems.","What is the main reason why biodiversity is crucial for the survival of species?","It allows species to adapt to changing environments.","It provides a source of food for many animals.","It helps to maintain the balance of ecosystems.","It has no impact on the environment.","It allows species to adapt to changing environments.","Biodiversity allows species to adapt to changing environments, which is essential for their survival.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-loss-of-be4fcf92","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","How does the loss of biodiversity affect ecosystems?","It leads to an increase in the number of species.","It has no impact on the ecosystem.","It can lead to a decrease in the number of species and a loss of ecosystem services.","It causes an increase in the number of invasive species.","It can lead to a decrease in the number of species and a loss of ecosystem services.","The loss of biodiversity can lead to a decrease in the number of species and a loss of ecosystem services.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-relationship-species-33d3cf47","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","What is the relationship between species diversity and ecosystem resilience?","Species diversity has no impact on ecosystem resilience.","Species diversity increases ecosystem resilience.","Species diversity decreases ecosystem resilience.","Species diversity has a neutral impact on ecosystem resilience.","Species diversity increases ecosystem resilience.","Species diversity increases ecosystem resilience by allowing ecosystems to adapt to changing conditions.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-human-activity-51668b37","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","How does human activity affect biodiversity?","It has no impact on biodiversity.","It leads to an increase in biodiversity.","It can lead to a decrease in biodiversity through habitat destruction and pollution.","It causes an increase in the number of invasive species.","It can lead to a decrease in biodiversity through habitat destruction and pollution.","Human activity can lead to a decrease in biodiversity through habitat destruction and pollution.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-climate-change-851ddda1","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","How does climate change affect biodiversity?","It has no impact on biodiversity.","It leads to an increase in biodiversity.","It can lead to a decrease in biodiversity through changes in temperature and precipitation patterns.","It causes an increase in the number of invasive species.","It can lead to a decrease in biodiversity through changes in temperature and precipitation patterns.","Climate change can lead to a decrease in biodiversity through changes in temperature and precipitation patterns.","/image-source/sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-climate-change-851ddda1.png","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-a-species-61c15e3a","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","How does a species' ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affect its ecological niche?","It decreases the ecological niche as the species becomes more specialized.","It increases the ecological niche as the species occupies a wider range of habitats.","It has no effect on the ecological niche as it is a separate concept.","It decreases competition with other species as the species becomes less competitive.","It increases the ecological niche as the species occupies a wider range of habitats.","A species' ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions allows it to occupy a wider range of habitats, increasing its ecological niche.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-impact-of-e0762150","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","What is the impact of a species' ability to adapt to environmental changes on its genetic diversity?","It decreases genetic diversity as the species becomes more specialized.","It increases genetic diversity as the species occupies a wider range of habitats.","It has no effect on genetic diversity as it is a separate concept.","It has a neutral effect on genetic diversity as it depends on the specific environmental conditions.","It increases genetic diversity as the species occupies a wider range of habitats.","A species' ability to adapt to environmental changes can increase its genetic diversity as it occupies a wider range of habitats and interacts with other species.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-impact-of-fd91dc56","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","What is the impact of a species' ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on its evolutionary potential?","It decreases evolutionary potential as the species becomes more specialized.","It increases evolutionary potential as the species occupies a wider range of habitats.","It has no effect on evolutionary potential as it is a separate concept.","It has a neutral effect on evolutionary potential as it depends on the specific environmental conditions.","It increases evolutionary potential as the species occupies a wider range of habitats.","A species' ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions can increase its evolutionary potential as it occupies a wider range of habitats and interacts with other species.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-a-species-74c196ae","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","How does a species' loss of adaptability affect its ability to migrate to new habitats?","It increases the species' ability to migrate as it becomes more competitive.","It decreases the species' ability to migrate as it becomes more specialized.","It has no effect on the species' ability to migrate as it is a separate concept.","It increases the species' ability to adapt to new environmental conditions.","It decreases the species' ability to migrate as it becomes more specialized.","A species' loss of adaptability can decrease its ability to migrate to new habitats, making it more vulnerable to extinction.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-happens-to-a-9e95d0d1","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","What happens to a species when it loses its ability to adapt to changing environmental conditions?","The species becomes more resilient and better equipped to handle environmental changes.","The species is able to migrate to new habitats and find new food sources.","The species may face extinction due to its inability to adapt.","The species' population size increases as it becomes more competitive with other species.","The species may face extinction due to its inability to adapt.","When a species loses its ability to adapt, it becomes vulnerable to extinction as it is unable to cope with changing environmental conditions.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-a-species-46000c80","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","How does a species' ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affect its biodiversity?","It decreases biodiversity by limiting the species' ability to interact with other species.","It increases biodiversity by allowing the species to occupy a wider range of habitats.","It has no effect on biodiversity as it is a separate concept.","It decreases biodiversity by making the species more specialized and less adaptable.","It increases biodiversity by allowing the species to occupy a wider range of habitats.","A species' ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions allows it to occupy a wider range of habitats, increasing its potential interactions with other species and contributing to higher biodiversity.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-impact-of-1c158695","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","What is the impact of a species' loss of adaptability on its ecosystem?","It has no effect on the ecosystem as the species is no longer present.","It decreases the ecosystem's resilience to environmental changes.","It increases the ecosystem's biodiversity as the species is no longer present.","It has a neutral effect on the ecosystem as it depends on the specific environmental conditions.","It decreases the ecosystem's resilience to environmental changes.","A species' loss of adaptability can decrease the ecosystem's resilience to environmental changes, making it more vulnerable to disturbances.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-impact-of-bc102a19","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","What is the impact of a species' ability to adapt to environmental changes on its population size?","It has no effect on population size as it is determined by other factors.","It increases population size as the species becomes more competitive with other species.","It decreases population size as the species becomes more specialized and less adaptable.","It has a neutral effect on population size as it depends on the specific environmental conditions.","It decreases population size as the species becomes more specialized and less adaptable.","A species' ability to adapt to environmental changes can affect its population size, as it may become more specialized and less adaptable, leading to decreased population size.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-a-species-e5570d45","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","How does a species' loss of adaptability affect its ability to respond to environmental changes?","It increases the species' ability to respond as it becomes more competitive.","It decreases the species' ability to respond as it becomes more specialized.","It has no effect on the species' ability to respond as it is a separate concept.","It increases the species' ability to adapt to new environmental conditions.","It decreases the species' ability to respond as it becomes more specialized.","A species' loss of adaptability can decrease its ability to respond to environmental changes, making it more vulnerable to extinction.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-a-species-e40bbfb0","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","How does a species' ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affect its interactions with other species?","It decreases interactions with other species as the species becomes more specialized.","It increases interactions with other species as the species occupies a wider range of habitats.","It has no effect on interactions with other species as it is a separate concept.","It increases competition with other species as the species becomes more competitive.","It increases interactions with other species as the species occupies a wider range of habitats.","A species' ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions allows it to occupy a wider range of habitats, increasing its potential interactions with other species.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-can-humans-a6a6ea46","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","3. inferring the consequences of the extinction of certain species of living organisms and its impact on biodiversity in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, proposes possible solutions to address a problem that threatens biodiversity in the local environment, and explains the national efforts made to reduce the extinction of endangered species .","How can humans help to reduce species extinction in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia?","By exploiting natural resources","By destroying habitats and ecosystems","By implementing conservation efforts and sustainable resource management","By ignoring the problem","By implementing conservation efforts and sustainable resource management","Humans can help to reduce species extinction in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia by implementing conservation efforts and sustainable resource management, such as habitat protection, species reintroduction, and sustainable agriculture.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-main-reason-60113297","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","3. inferring the consequences of the extinction of certain species of living organisms and its impact on biodiversity in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, proposes possible solutions to address a problem that threatens biodiversity in the local environment, and explains the national efforts made to reduce the extinction of endangered species .","What is the main reason for the decline in biodiversity in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia?","Overexploitation of natural resources for human needs","Climate change and rising temperatures","Pollution and habitat destruction","Natural disasters and geological events","Overexploitation of natural resources for human needs","The overexploitation of natural resources for human needs, such as deforestation, overfishing, and overhunting, has led to a significant decline in biodiversity in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-extinction-of-2658e806","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","How does the extinction of a species affect the ecosystem?","It has no impact on the ecosystem","It leads to an increase in the population of other species","It disrupts the balance of the ecosystem and can lead to further extinctions","It has no effect on the population of other species","It disrupts the balance of the ecosystem and can lead to further extinctions","The extinction of a species can disrupt the balance of the ecosystem, leading to a cascade of extinctions and changes in the population dynamics of other species.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-main-cause-e94d2506","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","3. inferring the consequences of the extinction of certain species of living organisms and its impact on biodiversity in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, proposes possible solutions to address a problem that threatens biodiversity in the local environment, and explains the national efforts made to reduce the extinction of endangered species .","What is the main cause of species extinction in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia?","Habitat destruction and fragmentation","Overexploitation of natural resources","Climate change and rising temperatures","Pollution and human activities","Overexploitation of natural resources","The overexploitation of natural resources, such as deforestation, overfishing, and overhunting, has led to a significant decline in biodiversity in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-impact-of-3bd52bde","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","What is the impact of the loss of biodiversity on human well-being?","It has no impact on human well-being","It leads to an increase in food security and economic growth","It disrupts the balance of ecosystems and can lead to the loss of essential ecosystem services","It has no effect on the economy","It disrupts the balance of ecosystems and can lead to the loss of essential ecosystem services","The loss of biodiversity can disrupt the balance of ecosystems and lead to the loss of essential ecosystem services, such as clean air and water, soil formation, and climate regulation, which are essential for human well-being.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-role-of-69d966be","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","3. inferring the consequences of the extinction of certain species of living organisms and its impact on biodiversity in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, proposes possible solutions to address a problem that threatens biodiversity in the local environment, and explains the national efforts made to reduce the extinction of endangered species .","What is the role of conservation efforts in reducing species extinction?","It has no impact on reducing species extinction","It leads to an increase in species extinction","It helps to protect and conserve species and their habitats, reducing the risk of extinction","It has no effect on the population of other species","It helps to protect and conserve species and their habitats, reducing the risk of extinction","Conservation efforts, such as habitat protection, species reintroduction, and sustainable resource management, can help to protect and conserve species and their habitats, reducing the risk of extinction.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-impact-of-fc4b9734","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","3. inferring the consequences of the extinction of certain species of living organisms and its impact on biodiversity in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, proposes possible solutions to address a problem that threatens biodiversity in the local environment, and explains the national efforts made to reduce the extinction of endangered species .","What is the impact of climate change on biodiversity in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia?","It has no impact on biodiversity","It leads to an increase in biodiversity","It disrupts the balance of ecosystems and can lead to the loss of essential ecosystem services","It has no effect on the population of other species","It disrupts the balance of ecosystems and can lead to the loss of essential ecosystem services","Climate change can disrupt the balance of ecosystems and lead to the loss of essential ecosystem services, such as clean air and water, soil formation, and climate regulation, which are essential for biodiversity.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-main-reason-32ae871a","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","3. inferring the consequences of the extinction of certain species of living organisms and its impact on biodiversity in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, proposes possible solutions to address a problem that threatens biodiversity in the local environment, and explains the national efforts made to reduce the extinction of endangered species .","What is the main reason for the decline in the population of the Arabian oryx in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia?","Habitat destruction and fragmentation","Overexploitation of natural resources","Climate change and rising temperatures","Pollution and human activities","Overexploitation of natural resources","The overexploitation of natural resources, such as hunting and poaching, has led to a significant decline in the population of the Arabian oryx in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-role-of-f41a1404","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","3. inferring the consequences of the extinction of certain species of living organisms and its impact on biodiversity in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, proposes possible solutions to address a problem that threatens biodiversity in the local environment, and explains the national efforts made to reduce the extinction of endangered species .","What is the role of education and awareness in reducing species extinction?","It has no impact on reducing species extinction","It leads to an increase in species extinction","It helps to raise awareness and promote conservation efforts, reducing the risk of extinction","It has no effect on the population of other species","It helps to raise awareness and promote conservation efforts, reducing the risk of extinction","Education and awareness can help to raise awareness and promote conservation efforts, reducing the risk of extinction and promoting the conservation of species and their habitats.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-impact-of-c82ea7dd","Science G9: Explaining the impact of changes in - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","3. inferring the consequences of the extinction of certain species of living organisms and its impact on biodiversity in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, proposes possible solutions to address a problem that threatens biodiversity in the local environment, and explains the national efforts made to reduce the extinction of endangered species .","What is the impact of pollution on biodiversity in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia?","It has no impact on biodiversity","It leads to an increase in biodiversity","It disrupts the balance of ecosystems and can lead to the loss of essential ecosystem services","It has no effect on the population of other species","It disrupts the balance of ecosystems and can lead to the loss of essential ecosystem services","Pollution can disrupt the balance of ecosystems and lead to the loss of essential ecosystem services, such as clean air and water, soil formation, and climate regulation, which are essential for biodiversity.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-primary-purpose-486ae224","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-2 Explaining the impact of extinction on biodiversity and describing the changes that have occurred in biodiversity throughout the history of life","1. Organizing data on the appearance of specific fossilized organisms (fossils) in the fossil record as a function of time, determined by their position in sedimentary layers or by rock ages.","What is the primary purpose of studying the fossil record?","To understand the history of the Earth's climate","To identify the different stages of evolution","To learn about the diversity of life on Earth","To determine the age of the Earth","To identify the different stages of evolution","The fossil record provides a chronological record of the history of life on Earth, allowing us to identify the different stages of evolution.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-do-fossils-09737b67","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-2 Explaining the impact of extinction on biodiversity and describing the changes that have occurred in biodiversity throughout the history of life","2. Analyzing data using graphs and maps to provide evidence illustrating the changes that have occurred in living organisms throughout the history of life on Earth.","How do fossils provide evidence for the theory of evolution?","By showing the diversity of life on Earth over time","By providing a record of the history of the Earth's climate","By demonstrating the gradual changes in life forms over time","By showing the complexity of life forms","By demonstrating the gradual changes in life forms over time","Fossils provide evidence for evolution by showing that life forms have changed over long periods of time.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-significance-of-96bce4c2","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-2 Explaining the impact of extinction on biodiversity and describing the changes that have occurred in biodiversity throughout the history of life","1. Organizing data on the appearance of specific fossilized organisms (fossils) in the fossil record as a function of time, determined by their position in sedimentary layers or by rock ages.","What is the significance of the Cambrian explosion in the history of life on Earth?","It marked the beginning of the dinosaurs","It was a period of rapid evolution of complex life forms","It was a time of mass extinction","It was a period of slow and gradual evolution","It was a period of rapid evolution of complex life forms","The Cambrian explosion was a period of rapid evolution of complex life forms, during which many animal phyla first appeared in the fossil record.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-process-fb0b32f0","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-2 Explaining the impact of extinction on biodiversity and describing the changes that have occurred in biodiversity throughout the history of life","1. Organizing data on the appearance of specific fossilized organisms (fossils) in the fossil record as a function of time, determined by their position in sedimentary layers or by rock ages.","What is the term for the process by which fossils are compressed?","Permineralization","Replacement","Impression","Compression","Compression","Compression is the process by which fossils are compressed, in which the weight of overlying rock causes the organism's remains to be flattened.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-why-is-study-6ee30741","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-2 Explaining the impact of extinction on biodiversity and describing the changes that have occurred in biodiversity throughout the history of life","1. Organizing data on the appearance of specific fossilized organisms (fossils) in the fossil record as a function of time, determined by their position in sedimentary layers or by rock ages.","Why is the study of fossils important for understanding the history of life on Earth?","Because it allows us to study the diversity of life on Earth over time","Because it helps us to understand the climate and geography of the past","Because it provides evidence for the theory of evolution","Because it allows us to identify the different stages of evolution","Because it allows us to study the diversity of life on Earth over time","The study of fossils provides a chronological record of the history of life on Earth, allowing us to understand the diversity of life on Earth over time.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-layer-0df6b949","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-2 Explaining the impact of extinction on biodiversity and describing the changes that have occurred in biodiversity throughout the history of life","1. Organizing data on the appearance of specific fossilized organisms (fossils) in the fossil record as a function of time, determined by their position in sedimentary layers or by rock ages.","What is the term for the layer of rock that contains the oldest fossils?","The oldest layer","The youngest layer","The base layer","The top layer","The oldest layer","The oldest layer of rock is the base layer, which contains the oldest fossils.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-do-fossils-770870b5","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-2 Explaining the impact of extinction on biodiversity and describing the changes that have occurred in biodiversity throughout the history of life","2. Analyzing data using graphs and maps to provide evidence illustrating the changes that have occurred in living organisms throughout the history of life on Earth.","How do fossils provide evidence for the theory of evolution?","By showing the diversity of life on Earth over time","By providing a record of the history of the Earth's climate","By demonstrating the gradual changes in life forms over time","By showing the complexity of life forms","By demonstrating the gradual changes in life forms over time","Fossils provide evidence for the theory of evolution by demonstrating the gradual changes in life forms over time, as seen in the transition from simple to complex life forms.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-process-55c3ba73","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-2 Explaining the impact of extinction on biodiversity and describing the changes that have occurred in biodiversity throughout the history of life","1. Organizing data on the appearance of specific fossilized organisms (fossils) in the fossil record as a function of time, determined by their position in sedimentary layers or by rock ages.","What is the term for the process by which fossils are formed?","Permineralization","Replacement","Impression","Compression","Permineralization","Permineralization is the process by which fossils are formed, in which minerals from the surrounding rock seep into the spaces in the organism's remains.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-why-is-study-e6ddaf65","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-2 Explaining the impact of extinction on biodiversity and describing the changes that have occurred in biodiversity throughout the history of life","1. Organizing data on the appearance of specific fossilized organisms (fossils) in the fossil record as a function of time, determined by their position in sedimentary layers or by rock ages.","Why is the study of fossils important for understanding biodiversity?","Because it allows us to study the diversity of life on Earth over time","Because it helps us to understand the climate and geography of the past","Because it provides evidence for the theory of evolution","Because it allows us to identify the different stages of evolution","Because it allows us to study the diversity of life on Earth over time","The study of fossils provides a chronological record of the history of life on Earth, allowing us to understand the diversity of life on Earth over time.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-how-do-geologists-b3de0368","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-2 Explaining the impact of extinction on biodiversity and describing the changes that have occurred in biodiversity throughout the history of life","2. Analyzing data using graphs and maps to provide evidence illustrating the changes that have occurred in living organisms throughout the history of life on Earth.","How do geologists determine the age of a fossil?","By counting the number of layers of sediment above it","By studying the shape and size of the fossil","By analyzing the type of rock it is found in","By comparing it to other fossils found in the same layer","By counting the number of layers of sediment above it","Geologists use the principle of superposition to determine the age of a fossil, which states that older layers of sediment are buried beneath younger layers.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-primary-reason-198b9492","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-3 Explaining how matter and energy are transferred within an ecosystem, predicting the changes resulting from the extinction of one of its components, describing material cycles in the ecosystem, and inferring their role in supporting its sustainability.","1. Explaining how matter is recycled and energy flows between biotic and abiotic components in food webs within an ecosystem, and predicting the impact of the extinction of a biotic component on ecosystem balance and stability.","What is the primary reason for the decline in biodiversity over the past few centuries?","Habitat destruction and fragmentation is the main cause of biodiversity loss.","Climate change is the primary driver of species extinction.","Human overpopulation is the main reason for biodiversity decline.","Pollution is the primary cause of species extinction.","Habitat destruction and fragmentation is the main cause of biodiversity loss.","Habitat destruction and fragmentation is the main cause of biodiversity loss because it reduces the available space for species to live and interact, leading to a decline in population sizes and eventually extinction.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-impact-of-9c23a099","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-3 Explaining how matter and energy are transferred within an ecosystem, predicting the changes resulting from the extinction of one of its components, describing material cycles in the ecosystem, and inferring their role in supporting its sustainability.","1. Explaining how matter is recycled and energy flows between biotic and abiotic components in food webs within an ecosystem, and predicting the impact of the extinction of a biotic component on ecosystem balance and stability.","What is the impact of extinction on ecosystems?","Extinction has no impact on ecosystems.","Extinction has a positive impact on ecosystems.","Extinction has a negative impact on ecosystems.","Extinction has no effect on ecosystems.","Extinction has a negative impact on ecosystems.","Extinction has a negative impact on ecosystems because it disrupts the balance of species interactions, leading to changes in population sizes, nutrient cycling, and ecosystem processes.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-number-6a472b79","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-3 Explaining how matter and energy are transferred within an ecosystem, predicting the changes resulting from the extinction of one of its components, describing material cycles in the ecosystem, and inferring their role in supporting its sustainability.","1. Explaining how matter is recycled and energy flows between biotic and abiotic components in food webs within an ecosystem, and predicting the impact of the extinction of a biotic component on ecosystem balance and stability.","What is the term for the number of individuals of a species in an ecosystem?","Species abundance is the number of individuals of a species in an ecosystem.","Species richness is the number of individuals of a species in an ecosystem.","Species diversity is the number of individuals of a species in an ecosystem.","Biodiversity is the number of individuals of a species in an ecosystem.","Species abundance is the number of individuals of a species in an ecosystem.","Species abundance is the number of individuals of a species in an ecosystem because it refers to the relative frequency of a species in a given area.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-impact-of-78ba0695","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-3 Explaining how matter and energy are transferred within an ecosystem, predicting the changes resulting from the extinction of one of its components, describing material cycles in the ecosystem, and inferring their role in supporting its sustainability.","1. Explaining how matter is recycled and energy flows between biotic and abiotic components in food webs within an ecosystem, and predicting the impact of the extinction of a biotic component on ecosystem balance and stability.","What is the impact of pollution on biodiversity?","Pollution has no impact on biodiversity.","Pollution has a positive impact on biodiversity.","Pollution has a negative impact on biodiversity.","Pollution has no effect on biodiversity.","Pollution has a negative impact on biodiversity.","Pollution has a negative impact on biodiversity because it leads to habitat degradation, species extinction, and ecosystem disruption, resulting in a decline in population sizes and ecosystem processes.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-variety-aae21fe5","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","What is the term for the variety of species within an ecosystem?","Species richness is the variety of species within an ecosystem.","Species diversity is the variety of species within an ecosystem.","Biodiversity is the variety of species within an ecosystem.","Species abundance is the variety of species within an ecosystem.","Species diversity is the variety of species within an ecosystem.","Species diversity is the variety of species within an ecosystem because it refers to the number of different species present in a given area, as well as their relative abundance and distribution.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-impact-of-2c29bf44","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-3 Explaining how matter and energy are transferred within an ecosystem, predicting the changes resulting from the extinction of one of its components, describing material cycles in the ecosystem, and inferring their role in supporting its sustainability.","1. Explaining how matter is recycled and energy flows between biotic and abiotic components in food webs within an ecosystem, and predicting the impact of the extinction of a biotic component on ecosystem balance and stability.","What is the impact of climate change on biodiversity?","Climate change has no impact on biodiversity.","Climate change has a positive impact on biodiversity.","Climate change has a negative impact on biodiversity.","Climate change has no effect on biodiversity.","Climate change has a negative impact on biodiversity.","Climate change has a negative impact on biodiversity because it leads to changes in temperature and precipitation patterns, resulting in habitat disruption, species migration, and extinction.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-process-9ea3c5d3","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-3 Explaining how matter and energy are transferred within an ecosystem, predicting the changes resulting from the extinction of one of its components, describing material cycles in the ecosystem, and inferring their role in supporting its sustainability.","1. Explaining how matter is recycled and energy flows between biotic and abiotic components in food webs within an ecosystem, and predicting the impact of the extinction of a biotic component on ecosystem balance and stability.","What is the term for the process by which new species emerge?","Speciation is the process by which new species emerge.","Evolution is the process by which new species emerge.","Adaptation is the process by which new species emerge.","Mutation is the process by which new species emerge.","Speciation is the process by which new species emerge.","Speciation is the process by which new species emerge because it refers to the formation of new species from a single species or from a group of species.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-impact-of-2b55057c","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-3-3-1 Tracking some of the changes that occurred to the Earth as a result of human activity and exploring the natural hazards that may occur on Earth and how to predict them.","1. Describing environmental changes and their negative effects on natural resources and tracks their occurrence over time.","What is the impact of human activities on biodiversity?","Human activities have no impact on biodiversity.","Human activities have a positive impact on biodiversity.","Human activities have a negative impact on biodiversity.","Human activities have no effect on biodiversity.","Human activities have a negative impact on biodiversity.","Human activities have a negative impact on biodiversity because they lead to habitat destruction, pollution, climate change, and overexploitation of resources, resulting in species extinction and ecosystem degradation.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-number-80898a77","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-1 Explaining the impact of changes in biodiversity on the environment and humans at both local and global levels, and describing how the ability of species to adapt to diverse environmental conditions affects biodiversity.","2. Explaining the impact of species’ ability to adapt to diverse environmental conditions on biodiversity in different ecosystems.","What is the term for the number of different species that exist in an ecosystem?","Biodiversity is the number of different species that exist in an ecosystem.","Species richness is the number of different species that exist in an ecosystem.","Species diversity is the number of different species that exist in an ecosystem.","Species abundance is the number of different species that exist in an ecosystem.","Biodiversity is the number of different species that exist in an ecosystem.","Biodiversity is the number of different species that exist in an ecosystem because it refers to the variety of species present in a given area.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-term-process-71dd1a04","Science G9: Explaining the impact of extinction on - Set 2","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-1-3-3 Explaining how matter and energy are transferred within an ecosystem, predicting the changes resulting from the extinction of one of its components, describing material cycles in the ecosystem, and inferring their role in supporting its sustainability.","1. Explaining how matter is recycled and energy flows between biotic and abiotic components in food webs within an ecosystem, and predicting the impact of the extinction of a biotic component on ecosystem balance and stability.","What is the term for the process by which species become extinct?","Speciation is the process by which species become extinct.","Extinction is the process by which species become extinct.","Evolution is the process by which species become extinct.","Adaptation is the process by which species become extinct.","Extinction is the process by which species become extinct.","Extinction is the process by which species become extinct because it refers to the permanent disappearance of a species from the Earth's surface.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-property-of-6bdf6557","Science G9: Explaining the properties of liquids, comparing - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-3 Determining the concept of solubility, the rate of solubility in a solution, and deducing the factors affecting the solubility rate of a solute in","1. Explaining the properties of liquids (viscosity, surface tension) according to the composition of the substance, the arrangement of its molecules, and the forces between them.","What is the property of liquids that allows them to take the shape of their container?","Viscosity","Surface tension","Density","Fluidity","Fluidity","Fluidity is the ability of a liquid to flow and take the shape of its container.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-of-elements-is-28ed10f9","Science G9: Explaining the properties of liquids, comparing - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-7 Explaining how atoms bond with each other, identifying what is a chemical bond and how it is formed, and distinguishing between different types","3. Illustrating the electronic distribution of a number of groups of the periodic table, and explaining the method of dot representation of electrons, and represent it for a number of elements.","Which of the following elements is a noble gas?","Carbon","Nitrogen","Oxygen","Neon","Neon","Neon is a noble gas, which is a group of elements in the periodic table that are unreactive and do not readily form compounds with other elements.","","",""
