"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-property-of-477b89f1","Science G9: Explaining the properties of liquids, comparing - Set 1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-3 Determining the concept of solubility, the rate of solubility in a solution, and deducing the factors affecting the solubility rate of a solute in","1. Explaining the properties of liquids (viscosity, surface tension) according to the composition of the substance, the arrangement of its molecules, and the forces between them.","What is the property of a liquid that causes it to resist changes in shape?","Viscosity","Surface tension","Density","Fluidity","Surface tension","Surface tension is the property of a liquid that causes it to resist changes in shape and behave as if it has an elastic skin at its surface.","","",""
