"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-main-property-7ee1ead2","Science G9: Explaining the properties of liquids - Set 2 T1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-4 Explaining the properties of liquids, comparing crystalline and amorphous solids, and describing the pattern of crystals in solids.","2. Explaining the properties of the elements in the periodic table sectors within the period and group, and lists the uses of the common elements around it.","What is a group in the periodic table?","A vertical column of elements that often have similar chemical properties.","A horizontal row of elements.","A list of compounds ordered by mass.","A set of liquids with the same boiling point.","A vertical column of elements that often have similar chemical properties.","A group is a vertical column in the periodic table. Elements in a group often have similar chemical properties.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-pattern-of-88cf5f8b","Science G9: Explaining the properties of liquids - Set 2 T1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-4 Explaining the properties of liquids, comparing crystalline and amorphous solids, and describing the pattern of crystals in solids.","2. Comparing crystalline and non-crystalline solids according to the organization and arrangement of their atoms.","What is the pattern of crystals in solids?","The pattern of crystals in solids is random and irregular.","The pattern of crystals in solids is a repeating arrangement of atoms.","The pattern of crystals in solids is a fixed shape and volume.","The pattern of crystals in solids is a mixture of regular and irregular structures.","The pattern of crystals in solids is a repeating arrangement of atoms.","The pattern of crystals in solids is a repeating arrangement of atoms.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-main-difference-f9c14925","Science G9: Explaining the properties of liquids - Set 2 T1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-4 Explaining the properties of liquids, comparing crystalline and amorphous solids, and describing the pattern of crystals in solids.","2. Comparing crystalline and non-crystalline solids according to the organization and arrangement of their atoms.","What is the main difference between crystalline and amorphous solids?","Crystalline solids have a regular arrangement of particles, while amorphous solids have a random arrangement.","Crystalline solids have a random arrangement of particles, while amorphous solids have a regular arrangement.","Crystalline solids are always liquids, while amorphous solids are always gases.","Crystalline solids have no particles, while amorphous solids have particles.","Crystalline solids have a regular arrangement of particles, while amorphous solids have a random arrangement.","Crystalline solids have particles arranged in a regular repeating pattern, while amorphous solids have particles arranged more randomly.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-periodic-table-bf845cb3","Science G9: Explaining the properties of liquids - Set 2 T1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-4 Explaining the properties of liquids, comparing crystalline and amorphous solids, and describing the pattern of crystals in solids.","2. Explaining the properties of the elements in the periodic table sectors within the period and group, and lists the uses of the common elements around it.","What is the periodic table sector within a group?","A period of elements that have the same number of protons in their atomic nuclei.","A period of elements that have the same number of electrons in their outermost energy level.","A period of elements that have the same number of electrons in their inner energy levels.","A period of elements that have the same number of neutrons in their atomic nuclei.","A period of elements that have the same number of electrons in their outermost energy level.","A period of elements that have the same number of electrons in their outermost energy level.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-use-of-55431631","Science G9: Explaining the properties of liquids - Set 2 T1","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-1-4 Explaining the properties of liquids, comparing crystalline and amorphous solids, and describing the pattern of crystals in solids.","2. Comparing crystalline and non-crystalline solids according to the organization and arrangement of their atoms.","What is the use of the element Copper?","Copper is used in the production of steel.","Copper is used in the production of plastics.","Copper is used in the production of glass.","Copper is used in the production of semiconductors.","Copper is used in the production of semiconductors.","Copper is used in the production of semiconductors.","","",""
