"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-purpose-of-44fd3ab9","Science G9: Understanding the relationship between the electric field - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-3-1 Explaining the concept of electric current and methods of generating it in electrical circuits and its relationship to voltage and electrical resistance, and distinguishing between direct and alternating currents.","2. Describing the methods of generating electric current in electrical circuits","What is the purpose of a switch in an electrical circuit?","To increase the voltage of the circuit","To reduce the resistance of the circuit","To control the flow of electric current","To improve the efficiency of the circuit","To control the flow of electric current","A switch is used to turn the circuit on or off, allowing for control over the flow of electric current.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-role-of-86267545","Science G9: Understanding the relationship between the electric field - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-3-1 Explaining the concept of electric current and methods of generating it in electrical circuits and its relationship to voltage and electrical resistance, and distinguishing between direct and alternating currents.","2. Describing the methods of generating electric current in electrical circuits","What is the role of a conductor in an electrical circuit?","To insulate the circuit from the surroundings","To increase the resistance of the circuit","To allow the flow of electric current","To reduce the voltage of the circuit","To allow the flow of electric current","A conductor is a material that allows electric current to flow through it, enabling the circuit to function properly.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-role-of-17f10432","Science G9: Understanding the relationship between the electric field - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-3-1 Explaining the concept of electric current and methods of generating it in electrical circuits and its relationship to voltage and electrical resistance, and distinguishing between direct and alternating currents.","2. Describing the methods of generating electric current in electrical circuits","What is the role of an insulator in an electrical circuit?","To allow the flow of electric current","To increase the resistance of the circuit","To reduce the voltage of the circuit","To prevent the flow of electric current","To prevent the flow of electric current","An insulator is a material that prevents the flow of electric current, ensuring the circuit operates safely and efficiently.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-primary-function-86a255be","Science G9: Understanding the relationship between the electric field - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-3-1 Explaining the concept of electric current and methods of generating it in electrical circuits and its relationship to voltage and electrical resistance, and distinguishing between direct and alternating currents.","2. Describing the methods of generating electric current in electrical circuits","What is the primary function of a fuse in an electrical circuit?","To increase the voltage of the circuit","To protect the circuit from excessive current","To reduce the resistance of the circuit","To improve the efficiency of the circuit","To protect the circuit from excessive current","A fuse is designed to melt and break the circuit when the current exceeds a certain limit, preventing damage to the circuit and its components.","","",""
"sci-g9-9-5-3-1-1-is-function-of-4048a0cc","Science G9: Understanding the relationship between the electric field - Set 3","Science","9","Assessment for Grade 9 Science","false","2027-01-05T21:00:00.000Z","9-5-2-3-1 Explaining the concept of electric current and methods of generating it in electrical circuits and its relationship to voltage and electrical resistance, and distinguishing between direct and alternating currents.","2. Describing the methods of generating electric current in electrical circuits","What is the function of a capacitor in an electrical circuit?","To increase the voltage of the circuit","To reduce the resistance of the circuit","To allow the flow of electric current","To store electric charge","To store electric charge","A capacitor is a component that stores electric charge, allowing it to be released when needed and controlling the flow of electric current.","","",""